<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2293/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2293/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2293/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-23T17:12:54'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Idromarambiente MAR-3 probe'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Idromarambiente MAR-3 multiparameter probe'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A multiparameter probe suitable for deployment in all aquatic environments such as marine, inland and brackish waters. Can be used in autonomous monitoring stations. It can be equipped with up to eight internal sensors, with an additional 6 connected to the upper head. The 8 standard sensors that can be equipped include temperature, pressure, conductivity, dissolved oxygen saturation, pH, redox, turbidity and chlorophyll-a. Derived parameters calculated by the probe are salinity, relative density and dissolved oxygen in mg/l. Examples of the additional sensors that can be added to the probe include PAR, current velocity, quantum meter and bottom contact (altimeter). The probe is available in either Delrin or titanium housing, and features a bluetooth interface aswell as XMAR software for PC and XAPP software for Android devices. It features internal memory of 4 MB and a 4 Ah internal lithium battery. It is depth-rated to 100 bar.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2293'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2295/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2295/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2295/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-23T17:12:54'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Oengineering Guard-1 camera'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Oengineering Guard-1 underwater autonomous smart camera'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An underwater autonomous smart camera designed for infrastructure or environmental monitoring applications in marine protected areas, coastal areas or open sea. It can be deployed on fixed or mobile platforms such as drifter buoys, Argo floats, sea gliders, oceanographic moorings, landers, cabled observatories, or for other long-term missions. It features AI autonomous systems using PIXALIS (HDR) and SONY CMOS sensor configurations, with onboard storage for over 10000 images (depending on quality). It features a Linux PC board for implementation of customised processing algorithms (C++/Python), using YOCTO OS. It includes an image pre-processing function library for rapid prototyping, and an integrated illumination system. It is battery-operated, with a battery life > 12 months depending on the computational load. Includes an ethernet cable for PC data communication in shallow water deployments (1-3 m) or for connection to vehicles or buoys. It is available in several configurations, with a maximum deployment depth of 1000 m.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2295'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2294/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2294/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2294/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-23T17:12:54'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Sony SNC-RZ25N-P camera'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sony SNC-RZ25N/P network camera'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A network camera offering both JPEG or MPEG4 compression, designed for a range of web casting and remote monitoring applications. Two versions of the instrument are available (SNC-RZ25P and SNC-RZ25N), the only difference being the regional output format; the SNC-RZ25P outputs in European PAL format, and the SNC-RZ25N outputs in NTSC North American format. It is equipped with a 100BaseTX/10Base-T network interface and a built-in web server. Once the network connection is established, images from the camera can be efficiently streamed over the network. It features a 1/4 type CCD imager (Exwave HAD Technology) and has Pan/Tilt/Zoom (PTZ) capability. This allows camera movements and the 18x optical zoom to be controlled from a PC using a standard web browser. Additional features include \'Day/Night\' functions, audio monitoring and alarm functions. It can handle up to 20 simultaneous users in JPEG mode, or 8 users in MPEG4 mode. Its built-in multicasting capability allows efficient streaming of video and audio to a large number of users. The following image sizes are selectable: 640x480, 480x360, 384x288, 320x240, 256x192, and 160x120. Optional accessories include the SNCA-CFW1 Wireless Card and the SNCA-AN1 Wireless LAN Antenna (for use with SNCA-CFW1 Wireless Card. It has a pan range of 340 degrees and a tilt range of 120 degrees. Maximum frame rate is 30 fps for the SNC-RZ25N, 25 fps for the SNC-RZ25P.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2294'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2296/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2296/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2296/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-23T17:12:54'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Teledyne FLIR Blackfly S GigE'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Teledyne FLIR Blackfly S GigE BFS-PGE-27S5C-C 2D area scan camera'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A 2D area scan camera designed for various industrial machine vision applications including automated optical inspections, microscopy, robot guidance, laser beam profiling and autonomous vehicle guidance. It features a Sony IMX429 CMOS 2/3 inch sensor, and can switch between high sensitivity and low noise, or high saturation and dynamic range with selectable conversion gain. It can be used in conjunction with FLIR\'s GenICam3 API with GUI library, and detailed event logging is supported by comprehensive documentation. It has a resolution of 1936x1464, 1-43 FPS frame rate, 4.5 um pixel size, 0-47 db gain range, 15 us to 30 s exposure range, 6 MB of flash memory, operating temperature 0-50 degC.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2296'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1113/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1113/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1113/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-23T11:55:34'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'AA3 SFA'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Seal Analytical AutoAnalyser 3HR'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A fully automated Segmented Flow Analysis (SFA) system, ideal for water and seawater analysis. It comprises a modular system which integrates an autosampler, peristaltic pump, chemistry manifold and detector. The sample and reagents are pumped continuously through the chemistry manifold, and air bubbles are introduced at regular intervals forming reaction segments which are mixed using glass coils. The AA3 uses segmented flow analysis principles to reduce inter-sample dispersion and can analyse up to 100 samples per hour using stable LED light sources. This instrument can be updated piece-by-piece to SEAL Analytical’s later model, the AA500 (http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2290/).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1113'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1811/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1811/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1811/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-23T11:49:30'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'OceanPack RACK MK2 pCO2'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'SubCtech OceanPack Rack MK2 pCO2 analyser and continuous water sampler'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The OceanPack 19 inch Rack is an Underway or FerryBox autonomous measuring system. The OceanPack includes everything to run unattended and measure water parameters: power supply, data logger, and water system. The MK2 pCO2 analyser can be mounted to the Rack. Mobile & Modular Flow-through / Underway System for precise pCO2 measurements. It uses a LI-COR Biosciences LI-840x pCO2 sensor. The MK2 pCO2 analyser can have up to 6 external gases connected (e.g. span or reference gases or for atmospheric measurements).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1811'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2292/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2292/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2292/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-23T10:09:15'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'OceanPack BOUY MK2 pCO2'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'SubCtech OceanPack BUOY MK2 pCO2 analyser'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A pCO2 sensor suitable for shallow water use on small buoys, long-term monitoring, and deployment in remote locations. This instrument uses an LI-COR LI-840x analyser to measure partial pressure of carbon dioxide, while automatically compensating for temperature, pressure, and H2O. It features a robust compact submergible housing, anti-fouling protection, and auto-zeroing calibration. Data are automatically quality flagged by the data logger. Instrumentation including nutrient analysers, CTDs, and oxygen optodes may be easily integrated through the data logger. External modules may be added via the RS-485 MBUS bus. Optional add-ons include GPS geo references for data and position event control, online telemetry data transfer and alarm services, and an external or internal Li-Ion PowerPack. An optional Top-box with gas inlet may be added to measure pCO2 in air. Range: 0 to 3000 ppm CO2 (standard), up to 20,000 ppm CO2 available; 0 to 80 ppt H2O. Resolution: 0.01 ppm CO2; 0.001 ppt H2O. Accuracy: < 1.5 percent. Sampling rate: 1 Hz.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2292'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2291/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2291/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2291/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-21T13:28:57'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thies Clima 5.4107'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thies Clima 5.4107 precipitation analyser'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A precipitation analyser used to detect and measure different precipitation types, this instrument may be used in weather warning systems to notify users of ice onset. Data is output via a RS485 interface ASCII protocol. This sensor analyses temperature peaks of precipitation to detect the heat of crystallisation and the different dielectric properties of water and ice, enabling it to discriminate between and quantify precipitation incidents, including phase changes. This instrument is capable of measuring a range of incidents including liquid precipitation, supercooled rain, ice, and sensor soiling. It features a pyramid shaped design of four ceramic measuring surfaces with resistant glass coating. Versions of this sensor are capable of measuring hoarfrost and mixed solid/liquid precipitation types (5.4107.00.000) or may use an ASCII data interface with THIES command interpreter (5.4107.00.100). Minimum instrument intensity: 0.4 mm/hour, 5 minutes from minimum intensity this instrument will produce a precipitation signal. Accuracy: detection of supercooled precipitation - 95 percent of events. Ambient operating conditions: -40 to 85 degC, 0 - 100 percent relative humidity, including condensation.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2291'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2290/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2290/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2290/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-21T08:49:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SEAL AA500'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'SEAL Analytical AutoAnalyser 500'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A fully automated Segmented Flow Analysis (SFA) system, ideal for water and seawater analysis. It comprises a modular system which integrates an autosampler, peristaltic pump, chemistry manifold and detector. The sample and reagents are pumped continuously through the chemistry manifold, and air bubbles are introduced at regular intervals forming reaction segments which are mixed using glass coils. This is an upgrade of the AA3(HR), offering a full start-up to shut-down automation, a smaller footprint, and a simplified workflow. The instrument uses a high resolution dual beam LED digital photometer with optional LED wavelength modules 250 - 880 nm and optional 10 - 50 mm flow cells.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2290'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0911/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0911/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0911/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-16T11:49:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Atlas Hydrosweep DS  echo sounder'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Atlas Hydrographic {Teledyne Reson} Hydrosweep DS multibeam echo sounder'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A deep water multi-beam echo sounder which uses an operating frequency of 15.5 kHz to determine bathymetric depth. It can generate 59 receive beams per ping and has a swath width of 90 degrees. This is the 1st generation of the Hydrosweep DS which was replaced by the DS-2. Atlas Hydrographic is now part of the Teledyne Reson group.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL0911'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0910/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0910/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0910/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-16T11:46:50'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Atlas Hydrosweep DS 2 echo sounder'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Atlas Hydrographic {Teledyne Reson} Hydrosweep DS 2 multibeam echo sounder'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A deep water multi-beam echo sounder which uses an operating frequency of 15.5 kHz to determine bathymetric depth. As a special feature, it contains extended coverage of 2x 60 degrees (with 1 or 2 x 59 sound beams, each with approximately 2, 3 degree beam width). Available transducers are T-type arrays. The system has a depth range of 10 to 11,000 m. This is the 2nd generation of the Hydrosweep DS. Atlas Hydrographic is now part of the Teledyne Reson group.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL0910'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0909/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0909/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0909/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-16T11:46:09'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Atlas Hydrosweep DS 3 echo sounder'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Atlas Hydrographic {Teledyne Reson} Hydrosweep DS 3 multibeam echo sounder'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Also known as a DS 3G. A deep water multi-beam echo sounder which uses operating frequencies between 14 - 16 kHz to determine bathymetric depth. It can generate 320 receive beams per ping which can be modulated using beamforming into 960 soundings per swath. It also generates 2 swaths simultaneously per ping. The third generation uses not only continuous wave (CW) pulses, but also frequency-modulated (chirped) pulses and Barker coded pulses which result in 20 - 50% more swath width. Available transducers are planar  arrays with beam resolutions of  0.5x1, 1x1, 1x2 and 2x2 degrees. The system has a depth range of 10 - 11,000 m. This is the 3rd generation of the Hydrosweep DS. Atlas Hydrographic is now part of the Teledyne Reson group.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL0909'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2288/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2288/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2288/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-15T12:25:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'ANB Sensors AQ50'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ANB Sensors AQ50 pH sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A solid-state pH, conductivity, and temperature sensor suitable for remote monitoring in demanding environments. Applications include deployment on profilers, moorings, and vehicles. This sensor is solid-state, containing no glass electrode or moving parts. The AQ50 requires no calibration as the sensor is automatically calibrated without the need for manual intervention. It constantly monitors itself, providing real time feedback on sensor performance and notifying operators if manual intervention is required. This sensor can be stored wet or dry without degradation of performance and operate in any orientation. It is designed to stop biofouling by electrochemically inhibiting the formation of biofilm on the transducer. pH range: 2 - 10; resolution: 0.01 pH; accuracy: +/- 0.05 pH. Salinity range: 0 - 40 ppt. Temperature resolution: 0.1 degC. Operational temperature: -5 to 40 degC. 50 m depth rating.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2288'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2289/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2289/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2289/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-15T12:25:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'B and C Electronics SA8065.101'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'B and C Electronics SA8065.101 multiparameter probe'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A multiparameter probe designed for analysis of liquids. Applications include environmental monitoring, waste-water treatments, and depth profile analysis. This instrument is equipped to measure depth, temperature, conductivity, pH, oxidation-reduction potential (ORP), and dissolved oxygen. The SA8065.101 does not contain a data logger and has external power supply. Turbidity and ISE sensors may be added. Operating pressure: 35 bar maximum. Maximum depth: 20 m.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2289'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2286/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2286/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2286/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-10T07:59:49'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'BD FACSCanto II'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'BD Biosciences FACSCanto II flow cytometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A high sensitivity benchtop flow cytometer that allows for the characterisation of cells/particles in suspension. The instrument can be configured with 2 (blue 488 nm and red 633 nm) or 3 lasers (addition of violet 405 nm) to detect up to 8 colours. Hydrodynamic focusing within the quartz flow cell and a fixed optical pathway using beam-shaping prisms and achromatic focusing lenses ensure that alignment remains fixed between uses with no operator alignment required. Emission signals are transmitted from the flow cell by an octagon detector array with 6 photomultiplier tubes (PMTs) for the blue laser signal, and a trigon detector array (2 PMTs) each for the red and violet laser signals. This design enables collection of the dimmest emission signals first and enhances instrument sensitivity. The forward scatter (FSC) detector is a photodiode with a 488/10 bandpass filter (FSC resolution = 1.0 um) and side scatter (SSC) detector is a PMT with a 488/10 bandpass filter (SSC resolution = 0.5 um). Recommended maximum particle size is 50 um, minimum sample flow rate is 10 uL/min and maximum sample flow rate is 120 uL/min. Sample acquisition rate is 10 000 events/second with 6 compensated fluorescence parameters and 2 scatter parameters. Sample carryover is less than or equal to 0.1 %. A high throughput sampler is available for fully automated rapid sample acquisition, and a FACS Loader carousel can be mounted for the automatic loading of up to 40 12x75 mm tubes.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2286'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2287/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2287/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2287/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-10T07:59:49'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'UnSpec flow cytometer'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Unspecified flow cytometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An instrument used to detect and measure the physical and chemical characteristics of a population of cells or particles. A flow cell with a liquid stream of sheath fluid aligns the cells in the sample to pass through one or more laser beams, ideally in single file. The resulting visible light scatter and fluorescent signals are filtered to improve specificity and are picked up by detectors (photomultiplier tubes or photodiodes) and converted to electrical signals that can be analysed by a computer. The fluorescence parameters and direction of light scatter in two different directions (forward scatter and side scatter) provide information of cell size and complexity and can be characteristic of different cell populations. Fluorescent reagents may be added to samples and beads can be used for quality control and calibration of the data produced. The fluidics in flow cytometers can also be used to sort cells into collection tubes or wells. Some flow cytometers can capture images of cells (imaging flow cytometry).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2287'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2285/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2285/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2285/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-01T15:00:27'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'D-Link DCS-7010L'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'D-link DCS-7010L HD mini bullet outdoor network camera'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A high definition (HD) Cloud-enabled IP video camera suitable for outdoor surveillance. This camera is built with a megapixel image sensor which provides up to 720p HD resolution images and videos. An infrared cut removable (ICR) filter is built into the DCS-7010L, which blocks infrared light during the day for improved image quality. At night this filter moves out of the way to use all available light for low-light surveillance, and the camera is equipped with an IR LED illuminator with 10 m range. The DCS-7010L also comes with zoom and panning capability. A solid metal IP-66 weatherproof housing protects this camera from dirt and rain, making it suitable for outdoor use. A wire-in bracket protects the power cable from damage. Built in motion detection allows this camera to automatically record video and notify the user when motion is detected. Audio connectors may be used with a microphone, enabling two-way communication via the DCS-7010L. Configurable features of this camera include image size, frame rate, shutter speed, brightness, saturation, contrast, and sharpness. HD resolution: 1280 x 720) and up to 1 Megapixel (1280 x 800). Focal length: 4.3 mm; aperture: F2.0; angle of view: 73.5 degrees (H) 42.5 degrees (V) 83.3 degrees (D). Operating humidity: 20 percent to 80 percent non-condensing. Operating temperature: -25 to 50 degC.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2285'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2284/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2284/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2284/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-31T17:11:56'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'TriOS nanoFlu'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'TriOS nanoFlu fluorometer series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The TriOS nanoFlu fluorometer is a submersible, miniature fluorometer that can be configured to make precise and selective measurements of CDOM (Coloured Dissolved Organic Matter), chlorophyll a, phycocyanin in cyanobacteria, and rhodamine or fluorescein dependent on the LED excitation wavelength. The instrument can be used in commercial and research applications for monitoring seawater, river water, drinking water, or waste water. An environmentally neutral coating on the instrument\'s optical windows prevents biofouling and the sensor can be housed in stainless steel, titanium, or POM (Polyoxymethylene). Dependent on the parameter being detected, the sensor operates at measurement ranges of 0 to 200 ug/L or 0 to 500 ug/L and an accuracy of +/- 5%. Operating temperature ranges from 2 to 40 degC and measurements are taken at 3 second intervals, with a 6 second response time. With either a SubConn (pressure rated to 30 bar) or fixed cable connection (pressure rated to 3 bar) the nanoFlu can be configured with 3 different serial interfaces: ethernet, RS-232, or RS-485.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2284'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2283/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2283/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2283/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-31T10:32:53'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Agilent SureScan G2600D'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Agilent SureScan G2600D Microarray Scanner'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A microarray scanner for high-resolution fluorescence scanning of microarray slides. It has applications in molecular diagnostics, synthetic biology, and bioprocessing research for example, gene expression profiling and genotyping studies in biotechnology and clinical diagnostics. The scanner system provides a laser-induced fluorescence scanning solution designed to read microarrays printed on standard 1 by 3-inch glass slides. The microarray instrumentation measures the fluorescence intensity of two dyes simultaneously from labelled sample nucleic acid bound to microarrays. The system can continuously load from a 24-slide cassette and automatically load data files into Feature Extraction Software. It also features built-in ozone protection to minimise signal degradation.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2283'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2282/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2282/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2282/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-26T11:07:25'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'PNI TCM 2'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'PNI TCM 2 electronic compass module'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A sensor module which combines a three-axis magnetometer and a two-axis tilt sensor to determine orientation. The TCM 2 is suitable for a range of applications including GPS systems requiring backup azimuth data; automobile and marine navigation systems; aircraft compasses and avionics systems; oceanographic buoys and data stations; and tracking animal migration patterns. It measures heading, pitch, roll, temperature and magnetic direction and transmits data across the RS232 interface in response to input commands. Analogue output is available on all TCM models; however, analogue output modes do not provide full resolution, error flags, tilt data, or magnetic field information. It uses an inclinometer to mathematically correct for tilt in order to eliminate moving parts and provide more information about the environment than would be available with the use of a mechanical gimbal. The TCM 2 may have tilt compensation of +/- 20 degrees (TCM 2-20) or +/- 50 degrees (TCM 2-50). TCM 2-20 - Heading accuracy when level: 0.5 degrees RMS; heading accuracy when tilted: 1.0 degree RMS; heading resolution: 0.1 degree. Tilt accuracy: +/- 0.2 degrees; tilt resolution: 0.1 degree; tilt range: +/- 20 degrees. TCM 2-50 - Heading accuracy when level: 1.0 degree RMS; heading accuracy when tilted: 1.5 degrees RMS; heading resolution: 0.1 degree. Tilt accuracy: +/- 0.4 degrees; tilt resolution: 0.3 degrees; tilt range: +/- 50 degrees. Magnetic field - absolute accuracy: +/- 1 micro-T (0 - 70 micro-T), +/- 5 micro-T (70 - 80 micro-T); resolution: 0.01 micro-T; range: +/- 80 micro-T. Temperature measurements from -20 to 70 degrees at +/- 1 degC accuracy (after calibration) and +/- 1 degC resolution. TCM 2-20 and 2-50: 1 - 30 Hz sampling rate available, operating temperature: -20 to 70 degC.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2282'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2281/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2281/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2281/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-26T08:40:05'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Hydrolab Quanta'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Hydrolab Quanta multiparameter water quality probe'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A compact water quality monitoring instrument capable of measuring multiple parameters at the same time. Can be operated with the Quanta display and connecting cable, or with a datalogger using an SDI interface. Each instrument is custom configured with the following sensors available: temperature, dissolved oxygen (Clark Cell technology), conductivity, pH, ORP (Redox), depth, vented level (to 10 m). An integrated sample circulator creates a flow of water past the sensors with the benefits of reducing response time, reducing fouling, and allowing deployment in low flow environments. The Quanta can measure at depths up to 100 m. The Quanta display is rugged and waterproof, shows readings of 5 parameters at once, and allows quick calibration of the instrument. Optional accessories include a flow cell (allows monitoring within smaller diameter wells) and a Secchi disk. Temperature range of operation is -5 to 50 deg C and salinity range is 0 to 70 PSS.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2281'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2280/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2280/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2280/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-13T15:30:52'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'LISST-Tau'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sequoia LISST-Tau transmissometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Sequoia Laser In-Situ Scattering and Transmissometry (LISST)-Tau is a transmissometer suitable for use on underwater vehicles, profiling packages, CTDs, and other systems. It measures optical transmission and beam attenuation. The LISST-Tau transmits a collimated beam through the water and measures the light transmitted through its 15 cm path. Light modulation with synchronous detection rejects ambient light, while oversampling and averaging yield better than 16-bit resolution. LISST-Tau\'s digital controller applies calibration coefficients, corrects for temperature effects, and transmits data from both digital and analog outputs. Included software provides real-time display of data, and functions for checking and updating pure-water calibrations. Optical path length: 15 cm; source wavelength: ~532 nm (green) or ~ 650 nm (red) LED; source spectral bandwidth: <10 nm Full Width at Half Maximum; acceptance angle (half angle, in water): 1 degree. An optional flow-through chamber is available for use. Operating temperature range: -3 to 40 degC; storage temperature range: -20 to 60 degC; beam attenuation range: ~0 to 30 m^-1; linearity (concentration): >99 percent. Depth rating to 2000 m; sampling rate: 1 Hz.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2280'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2279/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2279/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2279/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-11T09:15:07'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Rockland Scientific FloatRider'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Rockland Scientific FloatRider turbulence sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A sensor package designed to integrate onto profiling floats, providing persistent direct measurements of micro-scale turbulence autonomously. The FloatRider is suitable for studying ocean mixing, ocean-atmosphere interactions, heat transfer, and fluxes of energy, oxygen, and nutrients. It delivers near-real-time band averaged spectra data. This instrument measures small-scale fluctuations in temperature in order to determine turbulence. This sensor includes two microstructure micro-temperature sensors as standard. A shear probe configuration is available. Micro-temperature range: -5 to 35 degC; accuracy: 0.005 degC; resolution: 0.00001 degC. Sampling rate: 256 Hz (optional 512 Hz sampling available). Depth rating: 2000 m.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2279'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2277/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2277/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2277/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-06T11:06:26'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'ARI Universal Percussion Corer'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Aquatic Research Instruments Universal Percussion Corer sediment corer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A sediment sampling device designed to collect long, undisturbed cores from the sediment-water interface in lakes and other aquatic environments. The percussion corer is a specific deployment configuration of the Aquatic Research Instruments (ARI) Universal Core Head that uses rapid, repeated impacts (hammering) to drive a core barrel into sediments. The core samples can be used for palaeoecological analysis. It uses a thin‑walled clear polycarbonate core barrel (68 mm internal diameter; 71 mm external diameter) driven into sediments using a percussion slide‑hammer assembly. The system can be deployed by divers, via extension rods in shallow waters, or by lowering line with optional weights in deeper environments. A typical sampler can be easily deployed in 20+ meters of water. Polycarbonate Core Barrels are available in standard lengths of 60 cm, 1.2 m, and 2.4 m.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2277'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2276/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2276/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2276/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-06T11:06:26'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Dionex ASE 200'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Dionex {ThermoFisher Scientific} ASE 200 Accelerated Solvent Extractor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An automated system for extracting organic compounds from a variety of solid and semisolid samples. The ASE 200 accelerates the traditional extraction process by using solvent at elevated temperatures. Pressure is applied to the sample extraction cell to maintain the heated solvent in a liquid state during the extraction. After heating, the extract is flushed from the sample cell into a standard collection vial and is ready for analysis.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2276'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2278/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2278/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2278/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-06T11:06:26'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Geotek MSCL-S'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'GEOTEK Multi-Sensor Core Logger S {MSCL-S} core analyser system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An automated, high-resolution, multi-sensor system used for non-destructive, geophysical measurements of sediment and rock cores. It is used in many geological coring workflows, including those for palaeoclimate, mineral exploration, geometallurgy, oil and gas, nuclear or geotechnical. Compatible sensors include gamma density, P-wave velocity (Vp), shear wave velocity (Vs), electrical resistivity, magnetic susceptibility (loop and point sensors), natural gamma spectroscopy, line-scan imaging, colour spectrophotometry, X-ray fluorescence, and infrared spectroscopy. The multi-sensor arrangement allows users to compare micro and macro scale changes in physical and chemical properties downcore. Data are output in tab-delimited ASCII files containing all measured parameters with depth in section and core. The system can accept either whole/split unconsolidated sediment cores in liners, or whole/slabbed rock cores with or without a liner. It automatically moves core samples past a series of sensors. The system can be setup to take depth co-registered measurements for each sensor between 1 mm and 100 mm intervals downcore with a position accuracy of better than 0.1 mm. The system can be upgraded with new sensors as new technologies become available. The system can accept cores up to 155 cm in length and up to 15 cm in diameter. It has a linear precision of 0.01 mm, and a typical logging speed of 4 m per hour.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2278'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2273/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2273/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2273/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-05T16:56:32'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'TSK XCTD'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Tsurumi-Seiki XCTD expendable CTD profiler'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An expendable free-fall CTD probe which provides oceanographic measurements of temperature and conductivity against depth, calculated using a fall-rate model. It can be launched using a handheld, deck-mounted or automatic launcher from moving platforms such as ships, submarines or aeroplanes at speeds of up to 12 knots. Temperature detection is performed using a high performance disk thermistor. The XCTD system determines salinity by performing calculations using electrical conductivity data and water temperature data. Maximum depth of profiling: 1000 m. Probe weight: 668 g. Wire length: 1025 m. Temperature range: -2 to +35 degC. Temperature accuracy: 0.02 degC. Salinity accuracy: 0.03 mS/cm.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2273'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2274/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2274/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2274/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-05T16:56:32'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'TSK XCTD-2'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Tsurumi-Seiki XCTD-2 expendable CTD profiler'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An expendable free-fall CTD probe which provides oceanographic measurements of temperature and conductivity against depth, calculated using a fall-rate model. It can be launched using a handheld, deck-mounted or automatic launcher from moving platforms such as ships, submarines or aeroplanes at speeds of up to 3.5 knots. Temperature detection is performed using a high performance disk thermistor. The XCTD system determines salinity by performing calculations using electrical conductivity data and water temperature data. Maximum depth of profiling: 1850 m. Probe weight: 682 g. Wire length: 1954 m. Temperature range: -2 to +35 degC. Temperature accuracy: 0.02 degC. Salinity accuracy: 0.03 mS/cm.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2274'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2275/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2275/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2275/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-05T16:56:32'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'TSK XCTD-2F'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Tsurumi-Seiki XCTD-2F expendable CTD profiler'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An expendable free-fall CTD probe which provides oceanographic measurements of temperature and conductivity against depth, calculated using a fall-rate model. It can be launched using a handheld, deck-mounted or automatic launcher from moving platforms such as ships, submarines or aeroplanes at speeds of up to 8 knots. Temperature detection is performed using a high performance disk thermistor. The XCTD system determines salinity by performing calculations using electrical conductivity data and water temperature data. Maximum depth of profiling: 1850 m. Probe weight: 662 g. Wire length: 1954 m. Temperature range: -2 to +35 degC. Temperature accuracy: 0.02 degC. Salinity accuracy: 0.03 mS/cm.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2275'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2272/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2272/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2272/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-05T14:04:37'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Biospherical MPE-PAR'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Biospherical Instruments MPE underwater PAR sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Biospherical Micro Profiling Irradiance (MPE) Photosynthetically Active Radiation (PAR) sensor is sensitive over a spectral rage of 400 to 700 nm and is depth rated to 2000 m. It can be configured for integration into autonomous platforms (e.g. gliders and argo floats) and is housed in an anodised-aluminium casing. The sensor can either be operated with a generic terminal emulation program such as HyperTerminal or RealTerm, or with BSI\'s dedicated uLoggerLight software. A high-pressure version depth rated to 7500 m is also available. An integrated digital temperature sensor monitors the temperature of the microradiometer producing temperature data at a resolution of 0.41 degC. The sensor operates at a temperature range of -2 to 45 degC and has a sampling rate of up to 250 Hz.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2272'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2271/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2271/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2271/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-05T14:04:37'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'DeepSea OSC-2080-IP'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'DeepSea Power and Light Optim SeaCam 2080-IP (4K Ultra HD) camera'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A 4K ultra high-definition video camera designed to fit almost any platform from medium inspection class vehicles to large manned submersibles for subsea operations. Video footage can be live streamed over an Ethernet network or captured on internal memory (up to 1 TB). Housed in 6Al-4V titanium it comes in versions depth rated to 6000 or 11,000 m. The wide angle lens offers a 78-degree horizontal field of view and can focus from 50 mm to infinity. The OSC-2080-IP has a 15.5x optical zoom, a 5.7 mm to 88.4 mm, F/2.0 to F/3.8 lens, and a 1/2.5" CMOS progressive scan image sensor.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2271'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1232/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1232/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1232/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-04T13:58:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Rockland MicroRider-1000'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Rockland Scientific MicroRider-1000 turbulence microstructure profiler'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A self-contained device designed to measure turbulence microstructure using 2 x SPM-6000 turbulence shear probes, 2 x FP07-1000 fast thermistors, 1 x SBE7-6000 conductivity sensor, 1 x pressure sensor, 2 x accelerometers and 1 x tilt sensor. Integrates with a variety of marine instrument carriers, such as gliders, AUVs, moorings, CTD rosettes, or profiling floats. It is pressure rated up to 1000 dbar or 6000 dbar. Accuracy is +/- 5% velocity shear. The instrument is available with an optional data logger which can perform in-situ near-real time (NRT) data processing.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1232'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2270/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2270/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2270/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-23T10:39:24'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'UMN IGT Sampler'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'University of Minnesota [custom] Isobaric Gas-Tight sampler - Seewald et al. (2002)'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A custom-designed isobaric, single shot gas-tight sampler created at the University of Minnesota based on the instrument design in Seewald et al. (2002). The device is constructed of chemically inert titanium, is gas-tight to 450 bar and can be used to sample fluids with temperatures up to 400 degC. The sampler has been designed to collect hydrothermal fluid at the seafloor and incorporates a compressed nitrogen gas chamber connected to a precharge valve which prevents degassing by maintaining the sample fluid at seafloor pressure (e.g. during transport to the sea surface and on-deck sample removal). The custom sampler primarily comprises an inlet snorkel and thermocouple, a sample valve, a sample and accumulator chamber with respective pistons, and a gas precharge valve. During transport from sea floor to surface, the compressed nitrogen in the accumulator chamber buffers internal pressure fluctuations caused by cooling of the sample fluid or external temperature/pressure changes. During extraction of the fluid sample onboard, water is simultaneously pumped through the gas precharge valve into the accumulating chamber to maintain constant pressure within the sampler. The instrument is 47 cm in length (excluding the inlet snorkel) and 29 cm in height. Sample volume is unspecified. Reference: Seewald, J. S., Doherty, K. W., Hammar, T. R., & Liberatore, S. P. (2002). A new gas-tight isobaric sampler for hydrothermal fluids. Deep Sea Research Part I: Oceanographic Research Papers, 49(1), 189-196.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2270'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1181/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1181/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1181/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-19T13:01:10'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'BAS MUDL net'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'British Antarctic Survey MUDL Bongo net'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A motion-compensated upwards and downwards looking Bongo net - one facing upwards, one downwards. The instrument is designed for capturing zooplankton moving up and down the water column. It uses a spring mechanism to compensate for the platform\'s movements, maintaining the net\'s upward and downward velocity close to steady-state. The system uses sealed cod ends and a time-controlled open/close mechanism. The cod ends need to be pre-filled with water before deployment to avoid implosion.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1181'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2269/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2269/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2269/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-17T15:28:10'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Linovision IPC608UW-10'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Linovision IPC608UW-10 underwater camera'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An industrial 4K POE underwater camera designed for underwater inspection and aquaculture applications. This camera features white LEDs with on/off light control, a remote access web GUI and mobile app, and a 2.8 mm lens (horizontal FOC: 102 degrees, vertical FOV: 55 degrees, diagonal FOV: 120 degrees). Stainless steel anti-corrosion casing makes this camera suitable for long-term underwater deployment. Optional add-ons include an NVR recorder with 10 TB to 80 TB storage capacity; a solar power system; and a 4G router. Maximum resolution: 3840 x 2160. Maximum depth rating: 50 m. Operating conditions: temperature range -30 to 60 degC, Humidity 95% or less within the casing (con-condensing). Shutter speed 1/3 s to 1/100,000 s.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2269'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2267/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2267/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2267/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-11T16:03:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'NOC NO3+NO2 LOC v5'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'National Oceanography Centre (NOC) Nitrate and Nitrite v5 Lab-On-Chip (LOC) sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A developmental microfluidic nitrate plus nitrite sensor designed for autonomous in-situ measurements. The NOC v5 nitrate and nitrite Lab-On-Chip (LOC) sensor autonomously performs laboratory-style wet chemical analysis using the Griess array. This instrument is rated to 6000 m depth.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2267'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2268/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2268/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2268/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-11T16:03:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'NOC Phosphate LOC v5'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'National Oceanography Centre (NOC) Phosphate v5 Lab-On-Chip (LOC) sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A developmental microfluidic phosphate sensor designed for autonomous in-situ measurements. The NOC v5 phosphate Lab-On-Chip (LOC) sensor autonomously performs laboratory-style wet chemical analysis using the molybdenum blue assay. This instrument is rated to 6000 m depth.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2268'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2266/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2266/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2266/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-11T14:18:04'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Kongsberg Seatex Seapath 330+ GPS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Kongsberg Seatex Seapath 330+ precise heading, attitude and positioning sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A navigational system including a dual frequency Global Navigation Satellite System (GNSS) receiver and a motion reference unit (MRU) 5+ inertial sensor. The GNSS receiver can use multiple satellite constellations (GPS, GLONASS, Galileo, and Beidou when available), and SBAS corrections (WAAS, EGNOS, MSAS, and GAGAN), to provide accurate heading and position data. The inertial sensor employs linear accelerometers and unique microelectromechanical systems (MEMS)-type angular rate gyros to provide 0.01 degree RMS pitch and roll accuracy. Sub decimetre position accuracy can be achieved through download of satellite orbit and clock data from internet and by post processing of satellite and inertial measurement unit (IMU) data. Output rate is up to 200 Hz. Heading accuracy is 0.04 degrees RMS (4 m baseline). Position accuracy is 1 cm + 1 ppm RMS (X and Y) or 2 cm + 1 ppm RMS (Z). Velocity accuracy is 0.03 m/s RMS. Heave accuracy is 5 cm or 5% (whichever is greatest) in real-time, or 2 cm or 2% (whichever is greatest) in delayed mode.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2266'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2265/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2265/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2265/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-10T15:33:15'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Rockland MicroRider-1000G'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Rockland Scientific MicroRider-1000G turbulence microstructure profiler'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Rockland Scientific MicroRider-100G turbulence microstructure profiler is a self-contained device designed to integrate into the nose of autonomous vehicles and measure velocity shear and dissipation of turbulent kinetic energy (TKE). The device contains 2x SPM-6000 turbulence shear probes, 2x FP07-1000 fast thermistors, 1x pressure sensor, 2x accelerometers and 1x tilt sensor as standard. An optional FP07 micro-temperature sensor can be added. The turbulence microstructure is pressure rated to 1000 dbar or 6000 dbar and has a sampling rate of 512 Hz with optional rates of up to 2048 Hz. Velocity shear accuracy is +/- 5%.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2265'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2262/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2262/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2262/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-05T14:17:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SubC Aquorea'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'SubC Imaging Aquorea white LED'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A subsea LED for use with remotely operated vehicles (ROVs) or in sync with SubC camera systems as a strobe. It is available in two depth ratings - a 3000 m option with anodised aluminium housing and a 6500 m option with titanium housing. The flat viewport lens material is scratch-resistant sapphire. The lamp output is 4800 lumens, strobe output is 6000 - 8000 lumens, and the colour temperature is 6500 K. The beam angle is 90 degrees and electrical efficiency is 89 lumens/watt. LED lifespan is over 60000 h with thermal monitoring and input voltage protection adding to the robustness of the light. Serial (RS-232) or analogue control is available.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2262'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2263/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2263/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2263/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-05T14:17:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SubC Aquorea Mk2'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'SubC Imaging Aquorea Mk2 white LED'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A hybrid strobe and video high power LED lamp for use in underwater applications. It can be used integrated with SubC camera systems or as a stand-alone product with serial control (RS-232/RS-485). It is rated to 6000 m depth with a Grade 5 titanium housing. The adjustable lamp output is 2400 - 12000 lumens, strobe output is +25000 lumens, and colour temperature is 5000 K. The beam angle is 80 degrees (circular cone) and electrical efficiency is 145 lumen/watt at 15 deg C in water. A diffusion lens is available to go over the LED.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2263'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2264/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2264/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2264/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-05T14:17:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SubC Aquorea Mk3'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'SubC Imaging Aquorea Mk3 white LED'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A high-efficiency subsea LED that can simultaneously operate as a lamp and a strobe. It can be integrated into subsea camera systems such as those found on remotely operated vehicles (ROVs), observatories, drop and tow systems, and battery-operated systems. It is available in two depth ratings - a 500 m option with anodised aluminium housing and a 6000 m option with Grade 5 titanium housing. Lens material is sapphire. LED activation time is tightly synchronised with the camera system exposure time to ensure the video stream is uninterrupted while collecting photos. The lamp output is up to 15000 lumens, strobe output is +32000 lumens, and colour temperature is 5000 K. The beam angle is 80 degrees circular and electrical efficiency is 180 lumen/watt at 15 deg C in water. Control is via a serial RS-485 port. A beam diffuser is available to be attached in front of the LED.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2264'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2259/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2259/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2259/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-04T15:59:14'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Apollo SciTech AS-C5'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Apollo SciTech AS-C5 Dissolved Inorganic Carbon (DIC) analyser'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A Dissolved Inorganic Carbon (DIC) analyser, for total dissolved inorganic carbon analysis in a variety of aquatic conditions such as in river and lake waters, coastal and open ocean waters, sediment porewater, and groundwater. The system can work in both land and shipboard laboratories. The AS-C5 DIC analyser is comprised of a solid state infrared CO2 detector (LI-850, by LI-COR, USA), a digital syringe pump for precise delivery of reagent and sample solutions (Kloehn, USA), a mass flow controller to accurately regulate the carrier gas flow rate, a specifically designed CO2 stripping reactor that allows for an efficient and smooth stripping of CO2 from the water sample, an electronic cooling system for removing moisture, and a computer communication assembly (USB to RS232 converter with a data acquisition unit; included) The analyser can handle sample volumes from 0.1 - 1.8 millilitres and takes approximately 3 minutes per analysis. The system has an analytical range of 0.2 - 20 mM and maintains a minimum precision of +/- 0.15% or +/-3 uM for seawater.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2259'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2261/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2261/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2261/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-04T15:59:14'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'RBR Legato4'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'RBR Legato4 CTD'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A conductivity, temperature and pressure sensor designed for use on gliders and autonomous underwater vehicles (AUVs). It can be used to derive salinity, density and sound velocity and is optimised for turbulence measurements and passive acoustic monitoring due to its silent operation (non-pumped). Conductivity is measured with an inductive sensor, suitable for deployment in marine, estuarine, or fresh water. There are no exposed contacts, which increases robustness, avoids susceptibility to surface contamination, and allows it to be frozen into ice without damage. The temperature sensor is built and calibrated in-house using an aged thermistor. Pressure is measured with a piezoresistive transducer built with a nickel-based superalloy diaphragm to avoid corrosion. Additional sensors such as Optical Dissolved Oxygen (ODO), Photosynthetically Active Radiation (PAR), Radiometer, Turbidity, Backscatter, Chlorophyll a, Fluorescence, and pH are supported. The RBRlegato4 is designed to fit into a standard 2 x 7 inch sensor bay and is rated to 1250m (1250dbar). Pressure accuracy is 0.01% of the full-scale rating and resolution is 0.001%. The conductivity range is 0-85 mS/cm with an accuracy of +/- 0.003 mS/cm and resolution of <0.0001 mS/cm. The temperature channel is calibrated an accuracy of +/- 0.002 degC (ITS-90) over the range -5 to +35 degC. Extended range calibrations are available.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2261'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2260/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2260/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2260/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-04T15:59:14'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Rainin Dynamax UV-C'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Rainin Instrument {Mettler-Toledo Rainin} Dynamax UV-C UV-VIS spectrophotometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A manually operated variable wavelength ultraviolet absorbance detector for High-performance liquid chromatography (HPLC).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2260'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1103/4/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1103/4/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1103/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-02T15:04:48'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'NOC NO3+NO2 LOC v3.2c'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'National Oceanography Centre (NOC) Nitrate and Nitrite v3.2c Lab-On-Chip (LOC) sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A stand-alone microfluidic wet-chemical (colourimetric) nitrate and nitrite lab-on-chip (LOC) system designed to perform automated in-situ chemical analysis using the Griess assay. The instrument detects nitrate and nitrite (up to 350 µM, 21.7 mg/L as NO3-) with a limit of detection (LOD) of 0.025 µM for nitrate (0.0016 mg/L as NO3-) and 0.02 µM for nitrite (0.00092 mg/L as NO2-). This performance is suitable for all natural waters except for the oligotrophic open ocean. Beaton et al. (2012) has a full description of the technology.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1103'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2112/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2112/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2112/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-02T15:03:31'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'NOC spectrophotometric pH LOC sensor'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'National Oceanography Centre (NOC) spectrophotometric pH Lab-On-Chip (LOC) sensor - Rerolle et al. (2012)'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A microfluidic pH Lab-On-Chip (LOC) sensor designed to perform automated in-situ analysis of seawater. The microfluidic cell comprises of an absorption cell, connected to light source and detector by two optical fibres, and a static mixer. Fluidics are controlled by four micro-inert valves directly mounted on the chip, and fluid propulsion is conducted using two syringe pumps. The light source is a tri-coloured LED with wavelengths of 435 nm and 596 nm corresponding to the absorption maximum of the pH indicator added to the seawater, and 750 nm to monitor sample turbidity. A linear array photodiode spectrophotometer (Ocean Optics HR4000) is used as detector. Short-term precision: 0.001 pH unit. Long term precision not yet evaluated.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2112'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2258/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2258/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2258/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-02T10:54:39'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Tekran 2537X'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Tekran 2537X CVAFS automated mercury analyser'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An automated ambient air analyser designed for continuous long-term, unattended analysis of gaseous elemental mercury. The 2537X is suitable for ambient air monitoring, determining differential surface emission and deposition rates, and measuring atmospheric mercury speciation. It uses a carrier gas (argon) and gold preconcentration with atomic fluorescence detection (Cold Vapor Atomic Fluorescence spectrophotometer) to measure Total Gaseous Mercury (TGM). It features a touch-screen interface and dual gold trapping for uninterrupted sampling. It performs automatic calibrations using internal permeation source and a manual injection port is also provided. It is available in two configurations to extend the upper range of the analyser, suitable if mercury concentrations are expected to far exceed typical ambient air concentrations. Sensetivity: < 0.1 ng/m3. Sampling cycle: 2 - 60 mins. Sample flow: 0.7 - 1.5 L/min.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2258'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1695/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1695/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1695/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-02T10:33:31'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'MCAT-IMP-CTP-IDO'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sea-Bird SBE 37 MicroCat IMP-CTP-IDO (submersible) CTD sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A high accuracy conductivity and temperature recorder with an integrated pressure sensor and a membrane-type Integrated Dissolved Oxygen sensor (IDO) designed for deployment on moorings. The IMP model uses an Inductive Modem (IM) for real-time data transmissions and has internal batteries. It is fitted with an integral pump (P).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1695'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0020/5/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0020/5/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0020/>;
    dc:modified '2026-02-02T10:28:53'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'MCAT-SIP-CT(P)'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sea-Bird SBE 37 MicroCat SIP-CT with optional pressure (submersible) CTD sensor series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A series of high accuracy conductivity and temperature recorders with optional pressure sensors designed for deployment on moorings. The SI model uses a serial interface (SI) for real-time data transmissions and is externally powered. It is fitted with an integral pump (P). The sensors may or may not have an integrated pressure sensor.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL0020'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1129/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1129/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1129/>;
    dc:modified '2026-01-29T10:41:26'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'UoS NOC pH sensor'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'National Oceanography Centre Colorimetric Microfluidic pH sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A National Oceanography Centre custom designed sensor for shipboard autonomous seawater pH measurements, developed in collaboration with the University of Southampton. The seawater sample and thymol blue indicator solution are pumped by two syringe pumps and mixed in the flow cell in a static mixer before entering the absorption cell. The fluid distribution is controlled by four micro-inert valves. A three-wavelength LED light source transmits light through the absorption cell which is detected by a HR4000 spectrometer. The measurements are made close to in situ temperature (plus 0.2 degrees celsius) by placement of the microfluidic flow cell in the sampling chamber which has continuous access to the ship\'s underway seawater supply. The LED\'s wavelengths are 435 nm (25 nm full width half maximum (FWHM)), 596 nm (15 nm FWHM) and 750 nm (30 nm FWHM).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1129'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2068/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2068/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2068/>;
    dc:modified '2026-01-29T10:39:07'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Sunburst AFT-pH'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sunburst Autonomous Flow Through Instrument {AFT-pH} pH sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An autonomous flow through instrument designed to be plumbed into a sample line / flow through system on a research vessel. The instrument uses a highly accurate colourimetric reagent method to measure pH in the 7 - 9 range, in salinities between 25 - 40 PSU. The instrument can also measure the pH of individual bottle samples. The AFT-pH logs its own data and can be configured to support other external instruments if required. It has a response time of 3 minutes, a precision of less than 0.001 pH units, a low long-term drift of less than 0.001 pH units over 6 months, and an accuracy of +/- 0.003 pH units. Thermistor accuracy is to within 0.1 degC, and precision is +/- 0.01 degC. Duration of use is 15,000 measurements from one reagent bag.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2068'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2067/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2067/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2067/>;
    dc:modified '2026-01-29T10:39:05'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Sunburst AFT-CO2'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sunburst Autonomous Flow Through Instrument {AFT-CO2} pCO2 sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An autonomous flow through instrument designed to be plumbed into a sample line / flow through system on a research vessel. The instrument uses a precise and stable colourimetric reagent method to measure the partial pressure of CO2 in water (pCO2- wet) from 150 - 700 microatmospheres, with an accuracy of +/- 3 microatmospheres. The AFT-CO2 logs its own data and can be configured to support other external instruments if required. It is calibrated against a National Institute of Standards (NIST)-traceable non-dispersive infrared (NDIR) system. The instrument has a response time of 5 minutes, a precision of less than 1 microatmosphere, a low long-term drift of less than 1 microatmosphere over 6 months, and a thermistor accuracy of 0.1 degC and precision of +/- 0.01 degC. Duration of use is 7,500 measurements from one reagent bag.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2067'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2257/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2257/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2257/>;
    dc:modified '2026-01-23T17:19:08'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'WET Labs ECO FLNTU-SLC'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'WET Labs {Sea-Bird WETLabs} ECO Puck FLNTU-SLC fluorescence turbidity sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A variant of the ECO Puck Triplet (http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0673/). It is a two-optical-sensor, user-defined instrument that carries a chlorophyll-a fluorometer and an optical turbidity sensor. ECO Pucks are real-time only sensors as they are integrated onto the platform that provides power and data handling. The SLC designation signifies this is a third generation model that is specific for integration into Slocum gliders. The fluorometers and turbidity sensor are single wavelength sensors. The fluorometer excitation / emission wavelengths are 470 / 700 nm respectively. Turbidity is measured at 700 nm, the detectors for both fluorescence and turbidity are positioned at a 142-degree intersection.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2257'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2256/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2256/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2256/>;
    dc:modified '2026-01-22T11:22:20'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'settlement collector cage'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Custom-made (passive) postlarval settlement collector cage - Wahle et al. (2009)'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A postlarval settlement collector cage built to the specifications described by: Wahle, R.A., Wilson, C., Parkhurst, M. and Bergeron, C. (2009). A vessel‐deployed passive postlarval collector to assess settlement of the American lobster Homarus americanus. New Zealand Journal of Marine and Freshwater Research, 43(1), pp.465-474. doi:https://doi.org/10.1080/00288330909510015. It is designed for monitoring benthic recruitment of lobsters, crabs, and other taxa. The cage is constructed from 10-gauge wire mesh with 37 mm openings and overall dimensions of approximately 61 cm x 91.5 cm x 15 cm, providing a floor area of about 0.55 m^2. The interior is lined with a 2 mm plastic mesh to retain newly settled organisms, overlaid with a 5 mm plastic mesh to prevent chafing. The cage is typically filled with clean, rounded cobbles to create suitable settlement substrate.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2256'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2255/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2255/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2255/>;
    dc:modified '2026-01-22T11:17:35'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Idronaut OS 310 CTD'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'IDRONAUT Ocean Seven 310 CTD'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A fast response, multi-parameter conductivity, temperature, depth (pressure), oxygen, pH, and redox probe. The OS310 does not require any pumps or external devices to flush the sensors, minimising power consumption, allowing it to be integrated/adapted into third-party platforms such as floating profilers, moorings, ROVs, and AUVs. It can be interfaced with other instruments. The OS310 can sample at rates between 1 to 28 Hz (samples per second). It features a platinum resistance thermometer with a response time of 50 ms. The conductivity cell is a high accuracy seven-platinum-ring quartz cell. The dimensions are designed to guarantee self-flushing and no clogging after long-term deployment. An optional 280 nm UV LED is available for integration into the conductivity cell to sterilise the sample under measurement, and prevent the early growth of biofouling inside the quartz measuring cell. Data memory is 4 GB. Ranges are 0 to 7000 dbar (pressure), -5 to 50 degC (temperature), 0 to 70 mS/cm (salt water conductivity), 0 to 7000 microS/cm (fresh water conductivity), 0 to 50 ppm (polarographic determination of oxygen), 0 to 500 %sat (polarographic determination of oxygen saturation), 0 to 44 mg/l (optical determination of oxygen), 0 to 500 %sat (optical determination of oxygen), 1 to 13 pH (pH), -1000 to 1000 mV (redox). Initial accuracies are 0.05% FS (pressure), 0.0015 degC (temperature), 0.003 mS/cm (salt water conductivity), 5 microS/cm (fresh water conductivity), 0.1 ppm (polarographic determination of oxygen), 1 %sat (polarographic determination of oxygen saturation), 0.1 mg/l (optical determination of oxygen), 1 %sat (optical determination of oxygen), 0.01 pH (pH), 1 mV (redox). Resolutions 0.002% FS (pressure), 0.0001 degC (temperature), 0.0001 mS/cm (salt water conductivity), 0.1 microS/cm (fresh water conductivity), 0.01 ppm (polarographic determination of oxygen), 0.1 %sat (polarographic determination of oxygen saturation), 0.025 mg/l (optical determination of oxygen), 0.25 %sat (optical determination of oxygen), 0.0001 pH (pH), 0.1 mV (redox).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2255'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0224/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0224/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0224/>;
    dc:modified '2026-01-21T09:10:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'CS300 pyranometer'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Apogee CS300 pyranometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A silicon pyranometer with a spectral range of 300-1100nm. Accuracy for total daily radiation is +-5%. Manufactured by Apogee Instruments and marketed by Campbell Scientific.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL0224'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2254/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2254/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2254/>;
    dc:modified '2026-01-15T14:50:21'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Vaisala PTU200 series'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Vaisala PTU200 pressure, humidity and temperature transmitter series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Vaisala PTU200 is a series of air pressure, humidity, and temperature transmitters suitable for a range of meteorological and environmental monitoring applications. The PTU200 transmitter uses the Vaisala BAROCAP Sensor for pressure measurement, and a platinum RTD sensor for temperature measurement. The humidity and temperature probes are fitted with the Vaisala HUMICAP Sensor. For outdoor use, a Vaisala Meteorological Installation Kit PTU200MIK1 is available, which includes an IP65 (NEMA 4) rated enclosure for the barometer, a static pressure head, and a radiation shield for the humidity and temperature probe. A Vaisala Tripod may be equipped to the transmitter to enable quick field setup. The PTU200 can be equipped with a second pressure sensor for added reliability. Pressure: range 50 to 1300 hPa (dependant on class); accuracy (at 20 degC) +/-0.10 to +/-0.30 hPa (dependant on class). Relative humidity: range 0.8 to 100 percent; accuracy (at 20 degC) +/-1 percent RH (factory references), +/-2 percent RH (0-90 percent RH against field calibration references), +/-3 percent RH (90-100 percent against field calibration references). Temperature: range -36 to 60 degC; accuracy +/-0.5 degC (at -40degC), +/-0.2 degC (at 20 degC), +/-0.4 degC (at 60 degC).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2254'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2253/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2253/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2253/>;
    dc:modified '2026-01-15T10:05:04'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'UIC MODICA'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'UIC MODICA multifunction Dissolved Inorganic Carbon (DIC) analyser'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A multi-detector, multi-channel instrument designed for the analysis of dissolved inorganic carbon (DIC), spectrophotometric pH, CO2, and C13/C12 ratios in aquatic and soil samples. It features multi-sample batch processing of up to 10 samples per run, which can include certified reference materials (CRMs). MODICA can be connected to UIC\'s CM5017 or CM5018 coulometers, and CRD-based instruments such as Picarro\'s isotopic analyser. MODICA also features integrated pure CO2 gas calibration hardware, giving users additional tools to evaluate instrument performance by measuring CO2 from two calibrated CO2 loops. MODICA software is available via a built-in Windows 10 computer, enabling the user to configure a run sequence based on sample type. The software then automatically loads appropriate predefined settings appropriate to the sample type, applying relevant calculations. At each step of the analysis, readings of salinity, temperature and pressure are also recorded by the software using onboard probes and a pressure transducer. Additional WiFi, USB and ethernet connections are provided.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2253'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2252/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2252/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2252/>;
    dc:modified '2026-01-15T09:47:40'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Apogee SQ series'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Apogee SQ Quantum PAR sensor series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The quantum PAR (photosynthetically active radiation) sensors in the Apogee SQ series are designed for continuous photosynthetic photon flux density (PPFD) measurement in indoor or outdoor environments. The SQ series sensors output an analogue voltage that is directly proportional to PPFD under sunlight (for models SQ-212 and SQ-215) or electric lights (for models SQ-222 and SQ-225). Sensitivity, calibration factors, and output ranges differ by model and serial number. The sensors operate at a spectral range of 410 to 655 nm in temperatures ranging from -40 to 70 degC and can be submerged in water up to depths of 30 m.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2252'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2251/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2251/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2251/>;
    dc:modified '2026-01-06T10:55:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Airmar SS510 EchoRange Smart Sensor'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Airmar SS510 EchoRange Smart Sensor - 200 kHZ Portable Survey depth sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A portable 200 kHz seafloor depth sensor designed for deployment on survey vessels for hydrographic surveying of harbours, waterways and other shallow coastal areas, via fixed mount for scour monitoring, or other mobile field work. The Smart Sensor features embedded microelectronics that process depth and temperature, which can be displayed on any device that accepts NMEA data. EchoRange transfers NMEA 0183 data in real time to a computer via RS422. It has a 500 W RMS, with minimal sidelobes for concentrated energy on the target. Accurate water depth measurements from 0.4 - 200 m. Stainless steel housing is depth rated to 10 m. 9 degrees beam angle. Operating temperature from -5 to +60 degC.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2251'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0973/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0973/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0973/>;
    dc:modified '2026-01-05T10:23:25'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Satlantic PAR sensor'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Satlantic {Sea-Bird} Photosynthetically Active Radiation (PAR) sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'PAR (400 - 700 nm) sensor that measures quantum irradiance with near flat spectral response and cosine spatial response. Cosine collectors for in air and in water measurements for 2 depth ratings, 1000 m and 7000 m. Digital and analog output options. Compatible with SeaBird CTD platforms. Tilt and internal temperature measurements carried out for data quality analysis. Max sample rate of 100 Hz, PAR range 0 - 5000 umol photons m^-2 s^-1. Cosine error 0-60 deg <3% and 60-85 deg <10%.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL0973'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2250/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2250/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2250/>;
    dc:modified '2025-12-18T15:13:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Aanderaa DCPS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Aanderaa Doppler Current Profiler Sensor (DCPS) series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Aanderaa Doppler Current Profiler Sensor series are medium-range, 600 kHz current profiler smart sensors designed to collect high quality current information on moving and tilting platforms. Available as 300 m depth rated (5400/5400R), 4500 m (5402/5402R), or 6000 m (5403/5403R). R-versions are equipped with RS-422 interface for use as stand-alone sensors with long cables, whereas the standard versions can be connected to a SeaGuardII or SmartGuard using the AiCaP output or third party systems through the RS-232 interface. The 5400 version is available with an integrated pressure sensor (5400P/5400PR) depth rated to 100 m. Narrowband Velocity Range: 0 to 500 cm/s (up to 1000 cm/s for tilt less than +/- 5 deg); Broadband Velocity Range: 0 to 400 cm/s; Velocity Accuracy: 0.3 cm/s or 1 % of reading; Velocity Resolution: 0.1 cm/s; Ping Rate: up to 10 Hz; Output Interval: 30 seconds to 2 hours.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2250'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2249/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2249/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2249/>;
    dc:modified '2025-12-18T15:13:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Aanderaa In-line ZPulse DCS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Aanderaa In-line ZPulse Doppler Current Sensor (DCS) series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Aanderaa In-line ZPulse DCS series are single-point acoustic doppler velocimeters based on a modified version of the ZPulse DCS 4520. The 5 models within this series include: 5800, 5800R, 5800RR, 5810, and 5810E. All of the models have a maximum depth rating of 2000 m and the in-line design facilitates the connection of up to 4 In-line DCS in a string (max. length of 300 m). The 5810(R) versions have the option to directly connect additional sensors as an integrated package, including: temperature, conductivity, wave and tides, pressure, and oxygen. Output interfaces for the sensors are AiCaP (5800/5810/5810E), RS-232 (5800RR/5810E), and RS-422 (5800R/5810E). Vector Averaged Current Speed Range: 0 to 300 cm/s; Resolution: 0.1 mm/s; Mean Accuracy: +/- 0.15 cm/s; Statistic Precision (std): 0.3 cm/s (ZPulse mode). Current Direction Range: 0 to 360 deg; Resolution: 0.01 deg; Accuracy: +/- 5 deg for 0 to 15 deg tilt, +/- 7.5 deg for 15 to 35 deg tilt.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2249'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2248/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2248/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2248/>;
    dc:modified '2025-12-18T15:13:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Aanderaa ZPulse DCS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Aanderaa ZPulse Doppler Current Sensor (DCS) series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Aanderaa ZPulse DCS series are single-point acoustic doppler velocimeters designed to be used with the Aanderaa SeaGuard platform to form a Recording Current Meter (RCM) in both commercial and research applications. The ZPulse technology improves the statistical precision by comprising several distinct frequencies into a single acoustic pulse. The 8 versions of the sensor (4420/4420R, 4520/4520R, 4830/4830R, and 4930/4930R) differ in output, depth rating, and the addition of an integrated temperature sensor. The respective R-versions operate with an RS-422 output for use as stand-alone sensors with long cables (up to 1500 m) and are incompatible with SeaGuard applications. The standard models operate with RS-232 or AiCaP ouput, the latter being compatible with the CANbus interface used by SeaGuard platforms and smart sensors. 2 depth-ratings exist across the DCS series: 300 m (4420/4420R, 4830/4830R) and 6000 m (4520/4520R, 4930/4930R). The 4830(R) and 4930(R) models include a temperature sensor that measures in the range of -5 degC to 40 degC with a resolution of 0.01 degC and a 0.1 degC accuracy. Vector Averaged Current Speed Range: 0 to 300 cm/s; Resolution: 0.1 mm/s; Mean Accuracy: +/- 0.15 cm/s; Statistic Precision (std): 0.3 cm/s (ZPulse mode). Current Direction Range: 0 to 360 deg; Resolution: 0.01 deg; Accuracy: +/- 5 deg for 0 to 15 deg tilt, +/- 7.5 deg for 15 to 35 deg tilt.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2248'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2247/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2247/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2247/>;
    dc:modified '2025-12-17T17:03:55'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SubC Rayfin Mk2'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'SubC Imaging Rayfin Mk2 Benthic camera'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A high definition (HD) underwater camera which provides Ethernet 4K and HD video and communication, and high resolution stills. It features a built in tilt and roll sensor, with optional depth and temperature sensors. The camera is depth rated to 6000 metres, with an optional 11,000 metre rating available. The camera features a grade 5 titanium and sapphire construction. It has ROV and autonomous applications, for deep-sea research, and live inspections and surveys, in addition to battery powered systems or observatories. Voltage is 16.5 - 32.5 VdC at 13.5 Watts. Angle of view in water is 81 degrees diagonal, with less than 3.4% distortion. The image sensor is 12.3 megapixels, 4056 x 3040 pixels, 12-bit complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor (CMOS). Focus range is 15 cm to infinity. Operating temperature in water is -20 to 30 degC. Zoom is 10x (digital).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2247'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2246/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2246/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2246/>;
    dc:modified '2025-12-11T16:32:21'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Advanced Navigation GNSS Compass'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Advanced Navigation GNSS Compass'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A plug and play GNSS/INS navigation and heading solution that is suitable for marine navigation, hydrography, autonomous agriculture, and antenna targeting. The GNSS Compass features dual GNSS antennas to determine heading and is simple to interface with hydrographic packages; it supports satellite navigation systems including GPS, GLONASS, GALILEO, and BeiDou. GNSS Compass features L1/L2 RTK to deliver time position accuracy of 10 mm. GNSS Compass is available in both a serial and ethernet variants. Horizontal position accuracy: 1.5 m (0.01 m with RTK); Vertical position accuracy: 2.0 m (0.015 m with RTK); Velocity accuracy: 0.05 m/s; Roll and Pitch accuracy: 0.4 degrees; Heading accuracy: 0.2 degrees; Unlimited range; Up to 200 Hz output data rate.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2246'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2245/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2245/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2245/>;
    dc:modified '2025-12-04T13:02:27'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Kongsberg OE1324 SIT'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Kongsberg OE1324 enhanced SIT camera'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An underwater video camera with enhanced low-light performance and long-range viewing capabilities designed for ROV navigation, turbid water inspections, ambient light operations, scientific research, and defence applications. The camera combines the Silicon Intensifier Target (SIT) image-intensifier with new video processing circuitry developed from military technology. Other features include adaptive contrast enhancement, automatic tube protection circuits, over-voltage protection, and special high-frequency amplifier circuits for operating on long cable lengths. The standard lens is 6.5 mm f/1.8, the focus control is fixed (150 mm to infinity), and the angle of view is 86 degrees diagonal (nominal) in water. The horizontal resolution is 700 television (TV) Lines, the full video light sensitivity is 1 x 10-3 Lux and the limiting light sensitivity is 2 x 10-4 Lux. A corrosion-resistant titanium alloy housing provides a depth rating of 3000 m as standard, but deeper options are available. Operating temperature range is -5 to 40 degC.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2245'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2244/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2244/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2244/>;
    dc:modified '2025-12-04T12:34:18'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Unspecified streamers'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Unspecified (towed) hydrophone streamers'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An array of hydrophones towed on one or more cables behind a vessel that is used to detect sound waves in aquatic environments. Applications include seismic exploration, passive acoustic monitoring of marine mammals, monitoring of underwater noise, and military surveillance. Each streamer typically has multiple hydrophones placed at set intervals along the cables and streamers can be deployed at the same depth or at different depths depending upon the application. A separate data logger and specialised software may be used to record and process the acoustic signals detected by the deployed hydrophones. This term should only be used where the application of the streamers is unknown and where the streamers are not a part of a larger seismic reflection system.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2244'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2243/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2243/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2243/>;
    dc:modified '2025-12-03T15:40:33'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Airmar 220WX'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Airmar Ultrasonic WeatherStation 220WX'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Airmar Ultrasonic WeatherStation 220WX is a compact meteorological station designed to provide real-time, site-specific weather information on moving platforms. The instrument can measure wind speed and direction, barometric pressure, temperature, relative humidity, GPS, speed and course over ground, and pitch and roll. The device operates at a temperature range of -25 degC to 55 degC and measures: a barometric pressure range of 300 to 1100 hPa (accuracy of +/- 0.5 hPa at 25 degC); wind speeds of up to 40 m/s (with an accuracy of 5% at 10 m/s); and an air temperature range of -40 to 80 degC (with an accuracy of +/- 1.1 degC at 20 degC). Output options include NMEA 0183 and NMEA 2000.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2243'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2242/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2242/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2242/>;
    dc:modified '2025-11-21T16:11:49'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Insite Pacific Aurora Plus'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Insite Pacific Aurora Plus miniature colour camera'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A miniature colour CCD video camera, ideal for applications including surveillance, inspection ROV, and remote tooling systems. The camera has a fixed focus, wide angle lens and requires no external controls in normal operation. Video output: Composite 1Vpp. The Aurora Plus has a high resolution, low light, colour CCD sensor within a compact titanium pressure housing. Lens: 3.6 mm, F2.0; Focus Range: 8 inches to infinity; Field of View: 73 degrees diagonal, 61 degrees horizontal; 48 degrees vertical. Storage temperature: -10 to 50 degrees C. Operating temperature: -20 to 60 degrees C. Optional pressure housings up to 13 km depth rating are available.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2242'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2241/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2241/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2241/>;
    dc:modified '2025-11-18T10:34:55'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Insite Pacific Mini Zeus 4K'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Insite Pacific Mini Zeus 4K camera'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A 4K high definition (HD) complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor (CMOS) colour zoom video camera. This camera provides 8,510,000 pixels compared to 410,000 pixels from standard definition cameras. Applications include offshore oil and gas industries, marine archaeology, and oceanographic research. The Mini Zeus 4K provides HD-SDI, 3G-HDI, and 6G-SDI HD/4K digital video outputs. A glass hemispherical viewport and Insite Pacific\'\'s bespoke fully water corrected optical lens system corrects for chromatic and geometric distortion, astigmatism, and other optical abnormalities including eliminating zoom and focus tracking errors. Focus, iris, and zoom can be controlled using Insite Pacific\'\'s optional Camera/Lens Controller. Focus range (at full wide): Front of dome to infinity; Focus range (at full telephoto): 203.2 mm to infinity; Iris range: F2.0 to closed; Lens: 4.4 mm (wide angle) to 88.4 mm (telephoto), 20X optical zoom lens. The camera is provided in a titanium housing with a 4,500 m depth rating as standard with options up to 7,500 m available. Operating temperature: 0 to 60 degrees C. Storage temperature: -20 to 60 degrees C.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2241'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2240/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2240/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2240/>;
    dc:modified '2025-11-11T16:49:28'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Bruker SkyScan 1172'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Bruker SkyScan 1172 (desktop) micro-CT scanner'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A desktop micro-CT scanner used for non-destructive 3D imaging of a sample\'s internal structure. Used in the fields of tissue biology and materials science because it offers the ability to obtain in-depth quantitative data on the 3D structure of bone, teeth, cartilage, lung, microvasculature and other soft tissues, as well as composite materials, fuel cells, rocks, etc. It generates a complete 3D representation by taking multiple X-ray transmission images from different angles and using algorithms to construct a 3D model. This allows for detailed, quantitative analysis of samples like bone, soft tissues, and materials without physical slicing. This instrument has a fully distortion corrected 11 Mp X-ray camera that is a 12-bit cooled charge-coupled device (CCD) fibre-optically camera coupled to scintillator. The X-ray source is 20-100 kV, 10 W, with a <5 um spot size. The detail detectability is 1 um at highest resolution to 25 um.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2240'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2239/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2239/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2239/>;
    dc:modified '2025-11-10T16:36:53'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Neil Brown 100 series CT'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Neil Brown 100 series CT sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A series of conductivity-temperature sensors designed to integrate with mobile platforms. CT 100 series sensors consist of an externally mounted CT cell and an internally mounted precision electronics board. Available models come in rectangular and cylindrical form to suit application. Temperature standard range: 0 to 30 degrees C (-5 to 60 degrees C extended range); Initial accuracy: 0.002 degrees C; Resolution: 0.0001 degrees C. Conductivity standard range: 0 to 60 mS/cm; Initial accuracy: 0.01 mS/cm; Resolution: 0.0001 mS/cm. Suitable for use up to 6750 dbar pressure.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2239'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2238/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2238/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2238/>;
    dc:modified '2025-11-10T14:31:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Sensoid 2degreesC Wavelet'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sensoid 2degreesC Wavelet CTD, accelerometer, radiometer, and GPS receiver'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A low cost ocean climate data sensor, capable of measuring conductivity, temperature, depth, light, acceleration, and position (GPS). The 2 degreesC Wavelet has several use cases, the primary use case involves attaching the sensor to volunteer SCUBA divers to collect oceanographic data during dives. Alternatively, the Wavelet can be used to produce vertical profiles of the water column via an extendable tether from the surface, short term (<24 hour) deployments on the sea bed or water column via weighted tethers, or attached to moving vessels to perform wide area in situ sampling. Measurement ranges are as follows: temperature 0 - 40degC, depth 0 - 300 m, conductivity 30 - 38 ppt, light 0 - 1800 lx, and acceleration 0 - 8g. Accuracies are +/- 0.15degC (temperature), +/- 1.5 mb (pressure). Conductivity resolution is 0.01 ppt with a drift of 0.5 ppt/200 hours, acceleration resolution is 0.01 g, and light resolution is 0.1 lx with an RTC of 0.4 s/day (drift). The sensor is powered by a 200 - 1200 mAh 1S LiPo battery, charged via solar or USB.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2238'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2237/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2237/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2237/>;
    dc:modified '2025-11-06T16:17:10'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'NKE WiMo'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'NKE WiMo multiparameter sonde'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The NKE WiMo is a four-port multiparameter sonde, suitable for sea and fresh water monitoring on a range of platforms. It features a smart digital sensor suite capable of measuring up to 20 parameters at a time, including temperature, conductivity, and pressure. The WiMo includes a wiper to maintain sensors from biofouling during deployment. Depth rating: 250 m; operating temperature: -5 to 50 degrees C; storage temperature: -20 to 70 degrees C.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2237'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2236/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2236/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2236/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-31T16:39:20'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'PAM system'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Unspecified (moored) Passive Acoustic Monitoring (PAM) hydrophone system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A stationary, underwater listening station that uses hydrophones and specialised software to detect, monitor, and analyse the sounds of marine animals and other ocean phenomena without disturbing the environment. These systems are deployed for extended periods and record acoustic data from a fixed location on the seafloor to understand long-term acoustic trends in an area. The data is collected and analysed after the mooring is retrieved. A PAM system will typically consist of one or more hydrophones, a data logger and storage to save the recorded acoustic data. The hydrophones are suspended in the water column between an anchor weight and a buoyant float. Systems may also have a satellite transmitter to allow real-time data transmission.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2236'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2233/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2233/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2233/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-31T14:37:02'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'C-FLUOR CDOM/FDOM fluorometer'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Turner Designs C-FLUOR 2120-000-U fluorometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A compact, factory-calibrated, single wavelength in-situ fluorescence sensor with low power consumption, suitable for long term real-time monitoring deployments. This instrument uses a 325/120 nm excitation filter and 470/60 nm emission filter to measure coloured dissolved organic matter (CDOM)/ Fluorescent dissolved organic matter (FDOM). Analogue and digital output options available. 2000 m depth rating. Ambient temperature range: 0 to 50 degrees C; water temperature range: -2 to 50 degrees C.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2233'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2234/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2234/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2234/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-31T14:37:02'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'C-FLUOR chlorophyll (blue excitation) fluorometer'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Turner Designs C-FLUOR 2120-000-C fluorometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A compact, factory-calibrated, single wavelength in-situ fluorescence sensor with low power consumption, suitable for long term real-time monitoring deployments. This instrument uses a 470/60 nm excitation filter and 696/44 nm emission filter to measure chlorophyll in vivo (blue excitation). Analogue and digital output options available. 2000 m depth rating. Ambient temperature range: 0 to 50 degrees C; water temperature range: -2 to 50 degrees C.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2234'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2235/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2235/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2235/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-31T14:37:02'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'C-FLUOR turbidity sensor'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Turner Designs C-FLUOR 2120-000-T turbidity sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A compact, factory-calibrated, single wavelength in-situ turbidity sensor with low power consumption, suitable for long term real-time monitoring deployments. This instrument uses an 850 nm excitation filter and 850 nm emission filter to measure turbidity. Analogue and digital output options available. 2000 m depth rating. Ambient temperature range: 0 to 50 degrees C; water temperature range: -2 to 50 degrees C.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2235'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2230/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2230/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2230/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-31T12:57:25'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Turner Designs C-FLUOR'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Turner Designs C-FLUOR fluorometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A compact, factory-calibrated, single wavelength in-situ fluorescence and turbidity sensor with low power consumption, suitable for long term real-time monitoring deployments. Analogue and digital output options available. Available optical kits: Blue/Green Algae; CDOM/FDOM; Chlorophyll in vivo; Fluorescent Dye Tracing; Hydrocarbons; Turbidity; Wastewater Monitoring. 2000 m depth rating. Ambient temperature range: 0 to 50 degrees C; water temperature range: -2 to 50 degrees C.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2230'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2232/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2232/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2232/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-30T11:20:36'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Davis 6250 (6357) Vantage Vue'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Davis Instruments Vantage Vue 6250 (6357) (wireless) weather station'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A weather station with pre-installed meteorology sensors. Wind speed is measured using a solid-state magnetic sensor. A wind vane and potentiometer are used to measure wind direction. Rain is collected in a tipping spoon type collector. Temperature is measured using a PN junction silicon diode and relative humidity is measured using a film capacitor element. The package is equipped with console (6351) and Integrated Sensor Suite (ISS) with outside and inside temperature and humidity, barometer, wind, and rain sensors as standard. The radiation shield is \'passive\'. It can receive and display data from the Vantage Pro2 Plus which includes two additional sensors: UV sensor and solar radiation sensor. The console power is sourced via batteries or AC adapter. Data is transferred using a wireless solar-powered transmitter. WeatherLink Live or Weather Link data loggers allow the station to interface with a computer to log and upload data to the internet. Compatible Integrated Sensor Suite product numbers: 6357 (uses ISS model 6357OV).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2232'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2231/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2231/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2231/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-29T11:53:06'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Horiba Aqualog'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Horiba Aqualog optical spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A benchtop optical spectrometer suitable for measuring coloured dissolved organic matter (CDOM). Outputs include absorbance spectra, fluorescence emission spectra, and fluorescence excitation-emission matrices. This instrument simultaneously measures absorbance spectra and fluorescence Excitation-Emission Matrices. It employs the Absorbance-Transmission Excitation Emission Matrix (A-TEEM) technique to acquire an Excitation Emission Matrix.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2231'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2229/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2229/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2229/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-16T12:09:14'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'iSPEX 2 spectropolarimeter'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'iSPEX 2 spectropolarimeter smartphone add-on'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A smartphone-mounted spectropolarimeter suitable for above-water measurements. The iSPEX 2 can be mounted to a smartphone and a picture taken of the water surface. Data of the intensity and polarisation of light at different wavelengths are collected and analysed to output information on the concentration of materials such as chlorophyll a, dissolved inorganic matter, and particulate matter. This sensor measures the polarised intensity of light in two orthogonal directions (horizontal and vertical polarisation). Wavelengths are measured hyper-spectrally from 390-700 nm at approximately 9 nm resolution (exact figures are dependent on the smartphone used). The iSPEX 2 works by using two slits alongside each other, letting light through from a single direction. This is modulated by a set of SPEX optics which encode the polarisation information into the spectrum as light and dark bands. A grating disperses the light onto a smartphone camera in the form of two spectrums of light with opposing light/dark bands. The smartphone camera registers these data, and they are processed using SPECTACLE app, a standardised methodology and database for spectral and radiometric calibrations of consumer cameras.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2229'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2227/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2227/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2227/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-09T12:07:04'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'FAU-HBOI AUTOHOLO'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Florida Atlantic University - Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute AUTOHOLO (autonomous) holographic imaging system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An autonomous submersible holographic imaging system developed by Florida Atlantic University - Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute (FAU-HBOI) for long-term in situ marine studies. It is used for in situ holographic imaging of marine particles, plankton, bubbles, and detritus. The instrument comprises dual cylindrical housings - one containing laser optics and the other housing a high-resolution 16 MP Imperx camera, power supply, and control electronics. It supports both lens-less and microscopic objective configurations, enabling particle resolution down to 2.3 um/pixel. Sampling volumes range from 12.4 mL to 71.4 mL per hologram. Data acquisition is programmable in continuous or burst modes, with onboard storage via 4 TB solid-state drives. Integrated GPU-based processing routines allow rapid hologram reconstruction and 3D particle analysis.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2227'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2228/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2228/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2228/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-09T12:07:04'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'PROBE fishing tracker'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Djup AB PROBE fishing tracker'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A smart sensor providing anglers with precise information on depth, temperature, and water clarity at the exact position of their hook bait or lure. Water temperature accuracy is +/-2 degrees Celsius before calibration and improves to +/-0.2 degrees Celsius after calibration (pending confirmation). Depth readings are accurate to within +/-1.4 decimeters, while conductivity and light measurements each have an accuracy of +/-2.5%. The accelerometer provides readings with a precision of +/-20 milli-G. Measurement ranges include water depths from 0 to 300 meters, temperatures between 1 and 40 degrees Celsius (adjustable), conductivity levels from 249 to 1501 millisiemens per centimeter.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2228'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2226/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2226/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2226/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-09T11:48:19'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Sensoid_Deepod_V1'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sensoid Technologies Deepod V1 depth, temperature, and light logger'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A small logger with WiFi connectivity that can be attached to fishing lines to measure temperature, depth, and light down to a depth of 50 m. The Deepod V1 can be used to measure the depth of a paravane/lure combination, and can also be attached to divers, buoys, or submerged chains. Data can be read from the built-in OLED display or from a smartphone, tablet, or laptop using the Deepod Web tool. Light, temperature, and pressure sensors are all positioned on the front side of the logger and are potted with epoxy resin for reliable operation. A joystick and white power LED are also present on the front of the logger. The OLED display and magnetic power switch are positioned on the back of the logger. Depth sensor range is 0 to 300 m which is beyond the working depth rating of 50 m. Temperature range is 0 to 30 deg C and light level range is 0 to 1800 Lux. Crush depth is rated at >100 m. The logger weighs 34 g in air, and the shape has been optimised to work well with trollling (length 87 mm, width 32 mm, thickness 19 mm). A rechargeable lithium polymer (LiPo) battery provides approximately 8 hours of use. USB charging is possible with a standard microUSB connector. This charge port is plugged during deployment in water. Wave height monitoring is possible with a min and max depth high speed logging function that can estimate wave height (0.1 to 10.0 m).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2226'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2225/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2225/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2225/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-09T09:47:39'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'P-ONE_P-CAL'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Pacific Ocean Neutrino Experiment Calibration Module'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A pair of glass hemispheres containing photomultiplier tubes as well as optical and acoustic calibration systems that acts as a hybrid module for detection and calibration within the Pacific Ocean Neutrino Experiment (P-ONE) large-volume neutrino telescope. Multiple Calibration Modules (P-CALs) will be deployed on instrumented mooring strings as integrated calibration instruments but also to avoid blind spots along the detector string. Data provided by P-CALs are used to measure the real-time relative positions of modules within the moorings, help to monitor the efficiency of the modules, and provide information on the optical properties of the seawater. Each 17 inch borosilicate glass hemisphere contains 4 photomultiplier tubes (PMTs) and a plastic shroud that acts as a mounting platform for calibration components and shields the PMTs from diffuse light flashes . A diffusing PTFE sphere allows the creation of isotropic flashes and is used for optical calibration. Five high-power nanosecond light pulsers positioned below the diffuser provide a choice of wavelength and pulse properties of the flash. The PTFE diffuser is optically coupled to the glass of the hemisphere using a fill of optical gel to minimise unwanted refractions at the glass interface. Ten beamed sub-nanosecond light flashers are also integrated into each module to measure time synchronisation between instruments, light scattering, and spectral dispersion. The acoustic positioning system uses piezo-based acoustic receivers acoustically coupled to the glass hemispheres to detect signals from acoustic transceivers distributed on the seafloor. This allows precise monitoring of the mooring string and module positions. A photodiode and silicon photomultiplier are present in each module for self-monitoring of module efficiency and flash timing. The module also hosts a CMOS camera to monitor sedimentation and biofouling levels on the instrument and to monitor bioluminescence events. Each module has several temperature, pressure, humidity, acceleration, and magnetic field sensors for continuous system monitoring.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2225'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2224/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2224/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2224/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-09T09:47:39'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'P-ONE_P-OM'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Pacific Ocean Neutrino Experiment Optical Module'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A pair of glass hemispheres containing photomultiplier tubes that utilises Cherenkov radiation to detect high-energy neutrinos. Multiple Optical Modules (P-OMs) will be deployed on instrumented mooring strings as part of the Pacific Ocean Neutrino Experiment (P-ONE) large-volume neutrino telescope. Each 17 inch borosilicate glass hemisphere contains 8 photomultiplier tubes (PMTs) each with a diameter of 3.1 inches. These PMTs detect the emission of light (Cherenkov radiation) from secondary particles produced in neutrino interactions within the water. The arrangement of the PMTs within the Optical Module ensure that photons with low incident angles that miss the primary PMT can be collected by adjacent PMTs. The PMTs are mounted in a spring-loaded configuration to accommodate temperature gradients, hydrostatic compression, and shock and vibrational loads during deployment or transportation. Silicon-based optical gel pads molded to the photosensitive area provide optical coupling to the glass hemispheres and increase the effective photocathode area by utilising total internal reflection. The mounting scheme and the easily removable gel pads allow for the safe removal and replacement of PMTs during production and testing. A custom high-voltage subsystem provides each PMT with a self-regulated programmable high-voltage supply, and the analog output signals from the PMTs are fed to a mainboard. Openings between PMTs will be used to mount additional devices for calibration purposes, including light beacons, axicons for light collimation, and acoustic receivers. Each module has several temperature, pressure, humidity, acceleration, and magnetic field sensors for continuous system monitoring.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2224'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2223/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2223/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2223/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-03T12:59:24'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'EnvLogger T7.3'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ElectricBlue EnvLogger T7.3 temperature sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The EnvLogger T7.3 is a customisable temperature sensor suitable for deployment in harsh aquatic and terrestrial environments. It can operate within a temperature range of -30 to 60 degC and can be deployed at depths of down to 4000 m. The logger comes in a standard 29 mm resin disc or can be encapsulated in biomimetic casings. The battery has a minimum lifespan of approximately 15 years at a 1 per hour sample rate (at 20 degC). The logger can record at a resolution of 0.1 or 0.5 degC. Data from the logger are transferred to a smartphone via the EnvLogger Viewer software using wireless Near Field Communication (NFC) technology.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2223'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2222/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2222/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2222/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-03T09:41:17'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Water Level Ultra'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Coastal-e Solutions Water Level Ultra water level sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A small and solar powered ultrasonic water level sensor suitable for real-time water level monitoring in coastal or terrestrial waters. 1 measurement per minute. Data update every 12 minutes. Range: 28 cm - 750 cm. Accuracy: 1 cm.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2222'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2220/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2220/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2220/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-02T17:34:03'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Brewtek Midi'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Brewtek Midi Secchi disk'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A 3D-printed device for measuring Secchi depth (water transparency) and water clarity (based on the Forel-Ule (FU) colour scale) in lakes, estuaries and near-shore environments to a depth of 20 m. The device consists of a 20 m tape measure held within a case, attached to a small Secchi disk (12.5 cm diameter) and a weight. The disk can be wound in and out using a bobbin and handle. The body of the device features an FU colour scale sticker, a finger strap and lanyard. The FU colour sticker is based on an FU to RGB (red, green, blue) conversion (Wernand et al., 2013). These RGBs were converted to a CMYK (cyan, magenta, yellow, black) scale, required for colour printing. Designed for use with a mobile phone application for citizen science data entry.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2220'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2221/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2221/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2221/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-02T17:34:03'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Brewtek Mini'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Brewtek Mini Secchi disk'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A 3D-printed device for measuring Secchi depth (water transparency) and water clarity (based on the Forel-Ule (FU) colour scale) in turbid lacustrine, estuarine and nearshore regions to a depth of 10 m. The device consists of a 10 m tape measure held within a case, attached to a small Secchi disk (10 cm diameter) and a weight. The disk can be wound in and out using a bobbin and handle. The body of the device features an FU colour scale sticker, a finger strap and lanyard. The FU colour sticker is based on an FU to RGB (red, green, blue) conversion (Wernand et al., 2013). These RGBs were converted to a CMYK (cyan, magenta, yellow, black) scale, required for colour printing. Designed for use with a mobile phone application for citizen science data entry.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2221'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2219/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2219/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2219/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-01T15:09:34'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Metrohm 800 Dosino'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Metrohm 800 Dosino dosing drive'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A dosing drive which can be used with a number of different Metrohm dosing devices or Metrohm titrators for simple dosing, titrations, complex automation and liquid handling tasks such as sample transfers or pipetting. This instrument uses a push rod to deliver liquid, via cylinders of variable sizes, to the attached dosing unit. The 800 Dosino can be used with cylinder sizes: 2 mL, 5 mL, 10 mL, 20 mL, or 50 mL.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2219'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2217/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2217/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2217/>;
    dc:modified '2025-09-26T14:29:25'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Metrohm 843'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Metrohm 843 peristaltic pump'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Metrohm 843 peristaltic pump operates at a flow rate of > 450 mL/min (at a pressure of 2 m) and can be used to provide a constant flow of fluid for e.g. rinsing sample containers. The pump station has two in-built membrane pumps which can be controlled directly via the interface using remote signals or manually by pressing a button. The pump can be supplied with additional accessories to suit different needs (e.g. for VA applications) and additional control instruments can be connected to the pump as well as other system instruments.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2217'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2218/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2218/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2218/>;
    dc:modified '2025-09-26T14:29:25'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Metrohm Autolab PG101'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Metrohm Autolab PG101 potentiostat'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Metrohm Autolab PG101 potentiostat/galvanostat is a computer-controlled voltammetry analyser that, when used as part of a larger electrochemical system (e.g. with a Metrohm 663 VA Stand mercury electrode), obtains information about an analyte by applying a potential and measuring the current produced in the analyte. The potentiostat operates at an applied potential range of -10 to 10 V (accuracy: +/- 0.2%; resolution: 150 uV), a maximum bandwidth of 1 MHz, and an input impedance of 100 GOhm. The instrument can supply and measure currents of up to 100 mA with a +/- 0.2% accuracy and a resolution of up to 0.015%. All operations for the Metrohm Autolab PG101 are conducted with NOVA software.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2218'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2216/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2216/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2216/>;
    dc:modified '2025-09-18T13:30:30'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'NKE Ifremer piezometer'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'NKE Ifremer piezometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A piezometer-instrumented stake developed by Ifremer for the in-situ measurement and monitoring of deep-sea sediment pore pressure at different depths, for various geotechnical applications. Manufactured and sold by NKE Instrumentation. Available as the standard piezometer or V2 version. It can be deployed in 3 modes: long-term mode for up to two years; short-term yoyo mode where it remains connected to the vessel via cable, for 8 - 24 hour deployments; autonomous yoyo mode for short-term measurements down to 1500 m depth, 1 - 10 days deployment. Consists of several connecting tubes and an outer sleeve. It contains a differential pressure sensor and temperature sensor. An electronic board is integrated in the sleeve, which digitises the data from the differential pressure sensor and temperature probe (MPT card). The sleeve provides the mechanical link between the tubes. A digital link bus interconnects the digitising boards; this link is controlled by a data storage module (MDS) located in the retrievable assembly. The Data logging card (MDS module) allows the measurement acquisition rate to be set, and the values to be recorded on a memory card. This module is located in a waterproof titanium container. Depth-rated up to 6000 m. Pressure measurement range +/- 200 kPa, pressure measurement accuracy +/- 0.5 kPa. Temperature measurement accuracy +/- 0.05 degC, temperature measurement range 0 - 50 degC.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2216'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2214/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2214/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2214/>;
    dc:modified '2025-09-11T09:57:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Electric bilge pump'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Unknown electric bilge pump'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An electronically powered, submersible pump that can be used to suck water from the water body for sampling as well as other applications.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2214'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2215/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2215/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2215/>;
    dc:modified '2025-09-11T09:57:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thermo Finnigan MAT 252 IRMS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thermo Finnigan {Thermo Fisher Scientific} MAT 252 isotope ratio mass spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An isotope ratio mass spectrometer designed to determine stable isotope ratios of H/D, 13C/12C, 15N/14N, 18O/16O, 34S/32S (from SO2 to SF6) as well as Kr and Xe. It is a high-performance analytical instrument used for a variety of applications in various fields, including environmental science, geology, and biomedical research. It has a dual micro-volume inlet system, electromagnet, 24X multiport manifold interfaced with a Pentium PC using ISODAT software. The mass range is 1 - 150 Dalton at 10 kV. The resolution (m/delta m) for Carbon (C), Nitrogen (N), Oxygen (O), and Sulphur (S) is 200 (10 % valley), and for Hydrogen (H) and Deuterium (D) it is 25 (10 % valley). The absolute sensitivity is 1000 molecules CO2 per mass 44 ion at the collector (1000 molecules/ion). The contribution of the mass 44 intensity to the intensity of mass 45 is less than 2 x 10e-6.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2215'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1512/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1512/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1512/>;
    dc:modified '2025-09-04T12:59:12'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Davis 6162C (6327C) Vantage Pro2 Plus'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Davis Instruments Vantage Pro2 Plus 6162C (6327C) (cabled) weather station'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A weather station with pre-installed meteorology sensors. Wind speed is measured using a solid-state magnetic sensor. A wind vane and potentiometer are used to measure wind direction. Rain is collected in a tipping spoon type collector. Temperature is measured using a PN junction silicon diode and relative humidity is measured using a film capacitor element. The package is equipped with console and Integrated Sensor Suite (ISS) with outside and inside temperature and humidity, barometer, wind, and rain sensors as standard. The radiation shield is passive. The \'plus\' also integrates UV and solar radiation sensors. The console power is sourced via an AC adapter with battery backup. Data is transferred using a cable. Compatible Integrated Sensor Suite product numbers: 6327C (uses ISS model 6327OV).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1512'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1511/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1511/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1511/>;
    dc:modified '2025-09-04T12:59:11'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Davis 6162 (6327) Vantage Pro2 Plus'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Davis Instruments Vantage Pro2 Plus 6162 (6327) (wireless) weather station'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A weather station with pre-installed meteorology sensors. Wind speed is measured using a solid-state magnetic sensor. A wind vane and potentiometer are used to measure wind direction. Rain is collected in a tipping spoon type collector. Temperature is measured using a PN junction silicon diode and relative humidity is measured using a film capacitor element. The package is equipped with console and Integrated Sensor Suite (ISS) with outside and inside temperature and humidity, barometer, wind, and rain sensors as standard. The radiation shield is passive. The \'plus\' also integrates UV and solar radiation sensors. The console power is sourced via three C batteries or AC adapter. Data is transferred using a wireless solar-powered transmitter. The instrument may be optionally fitted with a fan-aspirated radiation shield (becomes product number 6163). Compatible Integrated Sensor Suite product numbers: 6327 (uses ISS model 6327OV).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1511'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2213/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2213/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2213/>;
    dc:modified '2025-09-03T16:01:58'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Ifremer GM interface corer'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Ifremer Ronanberg interface corer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A seabed-deployed sediment sampling device developed by Ifremer. It is used to collect detailed, undisturbed sediment cores for scientific research, to study sedimentary deposits, benthic communities, and other environmental factors in the marine environment. It is deployed using a winch and an A frame/crane. It can recover up to 80cm on a 1 m tube, and can be used in clay to sandy-shell sediments. It has a minimum operating depth of 2m, and can be used in mild sea conditions with waves under 4m.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2213'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/NETT0212/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/NETT0212/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/NETT0212/>;
    dc:modified '2025-09-03T16:01:58'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Large Juday net'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Modified Juday net - Bogorov (1947)'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A biconical plankton net with a non-filtering upper part and filtering lower part. The net is designed for vertical towing and is closed by releasing a messenger. It has a mouth diameter of 36 cm, a mouth area of 0.10 m^2, a medium ring diameter of 50 cm, an upper cone length of 120 cm, and a filtering cone length of 150 cm. The mesh size is 150 um. Described in Bogorov V.G. 1947. Instruction for hydrobiological works in sea (plankton and benthos). Arctic Inst., Serial: Manuals and Instructions, vol.18, Moscow-Leningrad.- 126 pp. (In Russian).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::NETT0212'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1673/4/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1673/4/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1673/>;
    dc:modified '2025-09-03T11:47:57'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Vaisala HMP155'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Vaisala HMP155 hygrometer series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A series of sensors that measure relative humidity and temperature, designed for outdoor applications. Alternative humidity variables are also reported (dew point/frostpoint temperature, wet bulb temperature, mixing ratio). Humidity measurement on the sensor is based on the capacitive thin film polymer HUMICAP sensor. Temperature measurement is based on platinum resistance (Pt100 RTD element, Class F 0.1 IEC 60751) sensors. The sensor is installed inside a radiation shield and is fitted with a digital RS-485 output. Active output (HMP155A, HMP155E) and passive output (HMP155D) models are available. The instrument can be fitted with standard humidity sensors, composite humidity sensors that are also suitable for heated applications or sensors resistant to chemical interfacing (INTERCAP, INTERCAPC, HUMICAP180C, HUMICAP180R, HUMICAP180RC, HUMICAPR2, HUMICAPR2C). It may also be fitted with an additional temperature sensor for enhanced temperature response. Several voltage output signal ranges: 0 -1 V, 0-5 V, 0-10 V. HMP155 replaces the HMP45 series of sensors.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1673'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2212/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2212/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2212/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-28T09:32:55'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Metrohm 858'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Metrohm 858 sample processor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Metrohm 858 sample processor prepares samples from 500 ul to 500 mL by performing filtration, dialysis, dilution, inline calibration, and eluent production in an automated fashion for ion chromatography analysis. The sample processor can be integrated with other Metrohm instruments (e.g. with an Eco IC) to produce an automated ion chromatography system. The instrument comprises an interchangeable sample rack, a lift, three Metrohm Serial Bus (MSB) connectors, two USB connectors, a stirrer connector, and can optionally be fitted with a two-channel peristaltic pump and a returnable injection valve. The maximum lift load is approximately 30 N with an adjustable speed of 5 - 25 mm/s. The two-channel peristaltic pump operates at a rate of 6 - 90 rpm, has a typical flow rate of 0.3 mL/min at 18 rpm (with Metrohm 6.1826.320 standard pump tubing), and a maximum pressure of 4 bar. The stirring rates range from 180 - 3000 rpm (for the 722/802 propeller stirrer) and 180 - 2600 rpm (for the 741 magnetic stirrer). The Metrohm 858 should be stored and operated at ambient temperatures in the range of 5 to 45 degC, at a maximum humidity of 80%.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2212'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2192/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2192/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2192/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-27T16:16:55'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thies Clima 5.4103.10.000'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thies Clima 5.4103.10.000 Precipitation Monitor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A precipitation monitor designed to detect the beginning and end time of precipitation. This instrument outputs precipitation status (yes/no). The output of the precipitation status/event occurs galvanically isolated via a relay and an optocoupler. The measuring principle of an optical/infrared photo sensor is used. The relay signalizes the start and end of the precipitation period as the recorded events (raindrops, hailstones, etc.) are compared with the set threshold value (number of events) within a 50 second timeframe. On reaching the threshold value the relay is switched. The reset of the relay occurs when no more events are detected after a defined delay, and the precipitation period is considered to be over. The optocoupler signalizes each event, as soon as a particle has been acquired by the light barrier. The acquisition of signalizing is carried out without filtering and without delay. This instrument has a collection area of 25 square centimetres; a contact load of 230 V AC/DC, 4 A maximum; and a cable gland electrical connection. Precipitation events are measured to a drop size > 0.2 mm.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2192'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2211/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2211/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2211/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-27T12:28:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thies Clima 1.1005.54'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thies Clima 1.1005.54 Hygro-Thermo Transmitter compact series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A series of instruments designed for the measurement of temperature and air humidity. Data are output as electrical analogue signals. The transmitter consists of a capacitive humidity element and a pt100 resistance thermometer. Multiple models are available with varying temperature and humidity measuring range, accuracy, and output. Temperature - Measuring range: -30 to 70 degrees Celsius (-40 to 60 degrees Celsius for 1.1005.54.461); Accuracy: 0.1 K (1.1005.54.000), 0.2 K (1.1005.54.160; 1.1005.54.173; 1.1005.54.461; 1.1005.54.161), 0.3 K (1.1005.54.241; 1.1005.54.441). Relative humidity - Measuring range: 0 - 100 percent relative humidity; Accuracy: +/- 2 percent relative humidity (at 5 - 95 percent relative humidity and 10 - 40 degrees Celsius).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2211'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2210/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2210/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2210/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-22T15:49:46'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Gill R3-50 anemometer'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Gill Instruments R3-50 research sonic anemometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Triaxial sonic anemometer with symmetrical head (vertical configuration with 3-fold rotational symmetry) and a data output rate of 50 Hz. The sensor head incorporates three pairs of transducers orientated orthogonally across the measurement region. Each transducer in a pair alternately transmits and receives ultrasound pulses to and from its partner. By measuring the travel time of the pulse in both directions, the velocity component of the air flow along the line of each transducer pair is determined. A mathematical transformation converts the three wind vectors into U, V, W resultants. Capable of measuring wind speed between 0 - 45 m/s, omnidirectionally. Operating temperature range is -40 to 60 degC.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2210'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2209/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2209/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2209/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-22T15:49:46'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'K&Z CUV3 radiometer'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Kipp and Zonen CUV3 total UV radiometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An instrument for measuring broadband global UV irradiance. The instrument has a sensitivity covering the entire UV range - UVA and UVB. The CUV3 is designed for continuous outdoor use in routine monitoring applications with the sun as a source, but can also be used for indoor applications such as monitoring or controlling of different types of UV lamps, having radiation in the wavelength range of 290 - 400 nm. The instrument outputs a voltage signal representing the actual UV radiation. Sensor signal at 365 nm is 200 - 400 microvolts/W/m^2. Operating offset is < 10 microvolts. Temperature range is -40 to 50 degC.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2209'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1598/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1598/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1598/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-22T10:50:41'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'K&Z CUV5 radiometer'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Kipp and Zonen CUV5 total UV radiometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An instrument for measuring the total UV radiation from natural sunlight for applications in meteorology and outdoor material testing. The dome and diffuser provide optimized directional response. A specially designed optical filter provides sensitivity to combined UVA and UVB irradiance. The photodiode generates a voltage output linearly proportional to the UV intensity. It has a spectral range of 280 - 400 nm, sensitivity of 300 - 500 microV/W/m^2, and a maximum UVA/UVB irradiance measuring capability of 400 W/m^2. The operational temperature range of the instrument is -40 to +80 degrees Celsius.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1598'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2208/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2208/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2208/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-21T15:23:32'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thies Clima 4.383x'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thies Clima 4.383x Ultrasonic Anemometer 3D series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A series of ultrasonic anemometers designed to measure horizontal and vertical components of wind velocity, wind direction, and acoustic virtual temperature. This instrument series measures the propagation of sound, as this velocity is superposed by the velocity component of an air flow. The propagation velocity resulting from superposition leads to different propagation times of sound at different wind velocities and directions. It consists of six ultrasonic transformers which function both as acoustic transmitters and receivers, in pairs facing each other, resulting in three measurement paths which are vertical in relation to each other. Virtual temperature is determined via measurement of sound propagation, the thermodynamic interrelationship between the propagation velocity of sound and the absolute temperature of air is defined by a root function. The influence of temperature on the measurement result is ruled out as the propagation time of sound is measured on each of the three measurement paths in both directions. The ultrasonic measurement principle this instrument series uses allows for the inertia-free measurement of running variable dimensions with high precision and accuracy. Cold Climate models are available with heated housing, for use in sites where frequent icing may be expected. Wind speed - Measuring range: 0 - 85 m/s; Resolution: 0.1 m/s (standard), 0.01 m/s (user defined); Accuracy: +/- 0.1 m/s + 1 percent rms (0 - 35 m/s), +/- 2 percent rms (35 - 65 m/s), +/- 3 percent rms (65 - 85 m/s). Wind direction - Measuring range: 0 - 360,540,720 degrees; Resolution: 1 degree (standard), < 1 degree (user defined); Accuracy: +/- 1 degree (1 - 35 m/s), +/- 2 degrees (35 - 65 m/s), +/- 4 degrees (65 - 85 m/s). Virtual temperature - Measuring range: -50 - 80 degrees Celsius; Resolution: 0.1 Kelvin; Accuracy: +/- 0.5 Kelvin.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2208'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2207/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2207/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2207/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-19T10:12:07'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'DGSI VW piezometer series'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Durham Geo Slope Indicator VW piezometer series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A series of pluck-type vibrating wire (VW) piezometers manufactured by Durham Geo Slope Indicator (DGSI) for in-situ pore water pressure measurements. Seven versions of the VW piezometer are available - all of which have the same instrument specifications but vary in size, weight, and material making them suited to different applications. The seven variations are: standard, corrosion-resistant, heavy-duty, low-pressure, push-in, vented, and multi-level and are available in varying standard pressure ranges from 0.7 bar (for the low-pressure model) to 35 bar (for the standard, push-in, and heavy-duty models) as well as custom pressure ranges. The instruments operate at a resolution of 0.025 % FS, an accuracy of +/- 0.1 % FS for 0.7 - 7 bar sensors and +/- 0.3 % FS for 17 - 35 bar sensors, and a temperature coefficient of < 0.04 % FS / degC. Signal cables for the instruments also come in standard and armoured versions with varying lengths. Readings are stored on the data logger in Hz.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2207'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2206/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2206/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2206/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-15T09:42:13'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SINTEF Ocean Silcam'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'SINTEF Ocean SilCam telecentric particle imaging system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A telecentric in-situ particle imaging system designed to quantify high concentrations of suspended particulates in seawater, such as zooplankton, large phytoplankton, mineral grains, marine snow and pollutants such as oil droplets and gas bubbles. SilCam can characterise particle types based on optical properties. It is a restricted path length telecentric system, using backlighting to create quasi-silhouettes of particles suspended between the light and the camera. Background illumination consists of a white LED array, and its beam is expanded and diffused using a holographic diffuser immediately prior to the housing window. The incident light passes through the sample volume, through the housing window and into the telecentric receiving optics, which is attached to a colour CCD (Charge-Coupled Device) camera. It produces 15 images per second which are recorded onto solid-state disk to enable continuous operation at 15 Hz, with a path length that is adjusted according to the concentration of particles. The optical configuration is mounted into two underwater housings (one for the illumination and one for the receiving optics and camera), which are rated to 3000 m depth. Three different magnifications (x0.5, x0.25, and x0.125) are available, each resulting in pixel sizes of 7.2 um, 14.4 um and 27.5 um. It provides particle size distribution and concentrations ranging from 50 um to several cm in length.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2206'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2205/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2205/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2205/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-14T11:11:25'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'IOS hydrophone array'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Institute of Ocean Sciences hydrophone array system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A system comprised of a custom array of hydrophones, designed by the Institute of Ocean Sciences, Canada. The system typically employs three hydrophones to facilitate the determination of directionality. Three hydrophone models have been used for the hydrophone arrays over time, the Burns Electronics CR-100-27 hydrophone (TOOL2204), the High Tech Inc HTI-99-HF hydrophone (TOOL1498), and the Teledyne Reson TC4032 hydrophone (TOOL1731).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2205'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2204/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2204/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2204/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-13T16:18:01'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Burns CR-100-27'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Burns Electronics CR-100-27 hydrophone'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The CR-100-27 is an encapsulated active ceramic hydrophone, featuring a sound-transparent rubber encapsulant. This provides high sensitivity and wide band (between 7 and 100 kHz) frequency range. The hydrophone also features an ultra-low noise, high impedance 27 dB field-effect transistor (FET) preamplifier to provide signal conditioning. The hydrophone has both scientific and commercial applications in cetacean research/monitoring, and underwater filming. Ceramic resonant frequency is > 200 kHz. Typical sensitivity is -179 dB +/- 5 dB. Operating depth is up to 400 metres, and operating temperature range is -1 to 55 degC. The hydrophone is omnidirectional when deployed horizontally (+/- 3 dB at 1 kHz), and 260 degrees when deployed vertically (+/- 6 dB at 1 kHz).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2204'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/NETT0211/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/NETT0211/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/NETT0211/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-11T16:18:16'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Unknown 25 m beach seine'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Unknown 25 m beach seine net'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An unknown beach seine fishing net that is 25 m long. It is 1.5 m wide and made from knotless netting. It consists of a single panel with 9 mm mesh. This seine net is shot from the shore by hand or by a small vessel in a circular shape and drawn ashore from both ends, encircling fish living close to the shoreline.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::NETT0211'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2203/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2203/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2203/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-07T16:47:26'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'T40 temperature sensor'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sea and Sun Technology T40 temperature sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A temperature sensor designed for long term measurements under rough conditions. This instrument uses an Isotech Pt100 platinum resistor. The housing is made of pure hard copper and consists of a housing with connector and a bottom end cap containing the temperature sensor. Measurement range: -2 to 36 degrees Celsius. Resolution: 0.0006 degrees Celsius. Initial accuracy: 0.005 degrees Celsius.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2203'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2202/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2202/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2202/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-07T14:10:02'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Subsea ONC SMART Cable system'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Subsea Data Systems Ocean Networks Canada prototype SMART Cable system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A prototype SMART (Science Monitoring And Reliable Telecommunications) Cable system manufactured by Subsea Data Systems and deployed by Ocean Networks Canada in a pilot project as part of the NEPTUNE cabled observatory . The system consists of a Sea-Bird SBE 3S temperature sensor, a Paroscientific 410K-101 pressure sensor, and a Silicon Audio Low-Noise optical seismic sensor. These sensors are deployed conventionally and are connected by cables to a subsea junction box. The seismic sensor is housed by a SMART sensor housing, and the temperature and pressure sensors are each connected to this housing by a 3 m Falmat cable. The SMART sensor housing is connected to a junction box connector port on the NEPTUNE observatory by a 15 m Falmat cable. Power and communications to shore are provided by this connector port. Temperature and pressure data are obtained as channels of the seismic data acquisition system. This pilot project is contributing to the development of SMART Cable systems with the objective being to integrate temperature, pressure, and seismic acceleration sensors into future telecommunications cables. These SMART systems will contribute towards tsunami and earthquake early warning monitoring, global climate monitoring, and telecommunication network integrity monitoring.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2202'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2200/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2200/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2200/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-06T12:58:42'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'BioTek Uvikon 923 UV-VIS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'BioTek Kontron Uvikon 923 Double Beam UV-VIS Spectrophotometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A double beam UV/VIS spectrophotometer designed for measuring the absorption, transmission or reflection of ultraviolet and visible light by a sample. Applications span pharmaceuticals, environmental monitoring, biotechnology, and materials science, with techniques ranging from absorbance-based quantification to thermal melt analysis and reflectance measurements. Double beam UV-Vis spectrophotometers use two beams of light, one that passes through the sample and one that serves as a reference. The ratio of the intensities of the two beams is used to calculate a highly accurate measurement. This ratio corrects any instrument fluctuations in real-time.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2200'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2201/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2201/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2201/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-06T12:58:42'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SensorLab SP200-SM'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'SensorLab SP200-SM (High accuracy Submarine) pH sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A rugged and stable pH sensor for shallow waters, designed for oceanographic research. The SP200-SM uses colorimetric methods to measure pH removing dye effect in each determination, making it valid for long deployments taking thousands of measurements. The system includes a real time clock allowing autonomous operation, as well as a high accuracy internal temperature sensor. It can be connected to an external conductivity / temperature sensor for deployments where high salinity variations occur. The system can be equipped with an internal rechargeable Li-ion battery allowing fully autonomous operation for periods as long as one full year. The instrument is pressure-rated to 2 Bar, suitable for deployments to depths of approximately 10 meters. The pH Range is 7 - 8.5 in sea water with a precision of +/- 0.002 pH units and an accuracy of +/- 0.005 pH units.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2201'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2199/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2199/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2199/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-05T16:09:52'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'ICM KduPRO-Multi'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Institute of Marine Sciences KduPRO-Multi radiometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The KduPRO-Multi is a low-cost do-it-yourself (DIY) instrument evolved from the KdUINO (Bardaji et al, 2016). The KduPRO-Multi utilises an AS7341 light sensor, which measures the light intensity at wavelengths of 415, 445, 480, 515, 555, 590, 630, 680, and 910 nm, and photosynthetically active radiation (PAR) band. Several instances of the KduPRO-Multi may be used at different depths in the water column in series to estimate the diffuse attenuation coefficient, Kd.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2199'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2198/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2198/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2198/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-05T16:09:52'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'ICM KduPRO-Multi system'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Institute of Marine Sciences KduPRO-Multi radiometer system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The KduPRO-Multi is a low-cost and modular do-it-yourself (DIY) moored system evolved from the KdUINO (Bardaji et al, 2016). It is based on a modular system of light sensors, independent of each other, measuring the irradiance at different depths. The depth of each module can be modified according to the requirements of the project or the environment, offering the user a custom array of sensors. This provides light sensing values at several depths in the water column to estimate the diffuse attenuation coefficient, Kd. The KduPRO utilises an AS7341 light sensor, which measures the light intensity at wavelengths of 415, 445, 480, 515, 555, 590, 630, 680, and 910 nm, and photosynthetically active radiation (PAR) band.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2198'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2197/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2197/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2197/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-05T16:09:52'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'ICM KduPRO-RGB'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Institute of Marine Sciences KduPRO-RGB radiometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The KduPRO-RGB is a low-cost do-it-yourself (DIY) instrument evolved from the KdUINO (Bardaji et al, 2016). The KduPRO-RGB utilises a TCS34725 light sensor, which provides a digital return of lighting intensity by photo-diodes on four different channels (red, green, blue, and PAR), and includes an infrared blocking filter. It contains an integrated analogue to digital converter (ADC) to modify the lighting intensity into digital values. The units are defined as counts by simply counting the number of pulses (Rodero et al, 2022). Several instances of the KduPRO-RGB may be used at different depths in the water column in series to estimate the diffuse attenuation coefficient, Kd.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2197'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2196/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2196/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2196/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-05T16:09:52'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'ICM KduPRO-RGB system'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Institute of Marine Sciences KduPRO-RGB radiometer system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The KduPRO-RGB is a low-cost and modular do-it-yourself (DIY) moored system evolved from the KdUINO (Bardaji et al, 2016). It is based on a modular system of light sensors, independent of each other, measuring the irradiance at different depths. The depth of each module can be modified according to the requirements of the project or the environment, offering the user a custom array of sensors. This provides light sensing values at several depths in the water column to estimate the diffuse attenuation coefficient, Kd. The KduPRO-RGB utilises a TCS34725 light sensor, which provides a digital return of lighting intensity by photo-diodes on four different channels (red, green, blue, and PAR), and includes an infrared blocking filter. It contains an integrated analogue to digital converter (ADC) to modify the lighting intensity into digital values. The units are defined as counts by simply counting the number of pulses (Rodero et al, 2022).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2196'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2195/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2195/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2195/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-04T17:05:14'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'PerkinElmer 3300 XL ICP-OES'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'PerkinElmer Optima 3300 XL ICP-OES'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An axially viewed (XL) dual-detector Inductively Coupled Plasma Optical Emission Spectrometer (ICP-OES). It uses a high-energy echelle-based polychromator, which utilizes a dual-detector, and a Segmented-array Charge-coupled-device Detector (SCD). This instrument is capable of measuring over 70 elements at multiple wavelengths in less than one minute; it features a 40 MHz free-running RF generator which provides a robust plasma and instantly compensates for changes in sample types or solvents. Plasma ignition is computer-controlled and totally automated. Wavelength range: 165 - 782 nm.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2195'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2194/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2194/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2194/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-01T14:40:21'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'ThermoF Element I ICP-MS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thermo Finnigan {Thermo Fisher Scientific} Element I inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Thermo Finnigan Element I is a double focusing, sector field inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer. It uses a demountable Meinhard nebulizer for sample introduction and a magnetic sector as a mass filter. It has a scanning rate at full mass range of under 60 ms. Short term precision is 2 %. Its sensitivity is 20 Mcps/ppm at R=300 and 1 Mcps/ppm at R=3000, with a detection limit under 0.1 ng/L for In at R=300.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2194'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2193/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2193/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2193/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-01T11:47:26'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'TA SDT Q600'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'TA Instruments SDT Q600 simultaneous thermal analyser'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The SDT Q600 is a combined thermogravimetric analyser (TGA) and differential scanning calorimeter (DSC) that provides simultaneous measurement of weight change and true differential heat flow on the same sample from ambient to 1500 degC. It has a dual beam design with automatic beam growth compensation and the ability to analyse 2 TGA samples simultaneously. DSC heat flow data is dynamically normalised using the instantaneous sample weight at any given temperature. The setup comprises a horizontal furnace encased in perforated stainless steel, a purge gas system with digital mass flow control, and a dual balance mechanism to enhance precision. The instrument has a DTA sensitivity of 0.001 degC, a calorimetric precision of +/- 2 %, and a heating rate of 0.1 to 25 degC per minute.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2193'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2189/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2189/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2189/>;
    dc:modified '2025-07-24T11:54:48'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Agilent 8800 QQQ ICP-MS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Agilent 8800 triple quadrupole inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Agilent 8800 is a triple quadrupole inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer. It contains two quadrupole mass spectrometers (MS/MS) in tandem which are separated by the octopole reaction system 3 (ORS3) collision cell which uses an octopole ion guide. The first quadrupole prevents all off-mass ions from entering the cell, ensuring consistent and controlled interference removal in reaction mode. The instrument in reaction mode can use either On-Mass Mode, where reactive interferences are removed to allow an unreactive analyte to be measured at its original mass; or Mass-Shift Mode, where the reactive analyte is moved to a new mass free from the original interference. The MS/MS enables low level analysis of difficult elements such as S, P and Cl, and provides an abundance sensitivity of <10^-10.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2189'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2190/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2190/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2190/>;
    dc:modified '2025-07-24T11:54:48'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'BASi Epsilon Eclipse'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'BASi Epsilon Eclipse potentiostat/galvanostat/bipotentiostat'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The BASi Epsilon Eclipse is an electrochemical analyser. It is a potentiostat/galvanostat with a second working electrode for bipotentiostat measurements. The instrument includes software which allows for the use of different techniques including different types of voltammetry, coulometry, amperometry, electrolysis, potentiometry, and polarography. The potentiostat is made up of 2 applied potential channels with 16 and 8 bit dynamic digital-to-analogue converters (DAC) with ranges of 3.275 V at 0.1 mV resolution or 10 V at 0.33 mV resolution, and 2.55 V at 10 mV resolution, respectively. The current to voltage converter has full scale sensitivity of 1 nA, 10 nA, 100 nA, 1 uA, 10 uA, 100 uA, 1 mA, 10 mA, and 100 mA, and a sampling rate of 50 Hz. The galvanostat has an applied current of 50 pA to 50 mA, a range of 10 V, and a measured potential resolution of 0.02 mV.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2190'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2191/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2191/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2191/>;
    dc:modified '2025-07-24T11:54:48'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'PerkinElmer Elan DRC II ICP-MS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'PerkinElmer Elan DRC II inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Elan DRC II inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer contains a simultaneous dual stage detector, a Dynamic Reaction Cell (DRC), and a quadrupole. The simultaneous dual stage detector measures both high and low level analytes simultaneously. The DRC uses high temperature plasma for analysis, allowing analysis on all elements in the same run, and it eliminates reaction by-products using the Dynamic Bandpass Tuning (DBT) mechanism. The DBT function ejects the precursor ions before they can react to form new interferences, and allows for the use of a variety of reaction gases. In addition, computer control allows automatic switching of reaction gases during analysis. Detection limits vary between 0.02 to 1.93 ppt for Thallium, Bismuth, and Uranium to Boron, respectively. Background equivalent concentrations vary between 0.01 to 2.6 ppt for Thallium, Bismuth, and Uranium to Potassium, respectively.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2191'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2140/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2140/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2140/>;
    dc:modified '2025-07-22T13:24:06'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thies Clima 5.4032'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thies Clima 5.4032 Precipitation Transmitter'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A precipitation transmitter designed to measure quantity and intensity of precipitation. This instrument uses a tipping bucket rain gauge. Precipitation is collected into the tipping bucket via the collecting area and funnel, upon reaching maximum volume capacity the bucket tips over. The tipping action is detected and transmitted as a digital pulse. The 5.4032 has a collecting area of 200 square centimetres. This device is available in various models, without heating (5.4032.35.007), with heating (5.4032.35.008), and with extended heating (5.4032.45.008). Models with heating (maximum 50 W) operate in ambient temperatures of -25 to 60 degrees C; models with extended heating (maximum 114 W) operate in ambient temperatures -35 to 60 degrees C; models without heating operate in ambient temperatures of 0 to 60 degrees C. For each model - Measuring range: maximum 11 mm/min; Resolution: 0.1 mm; Accuracy: +/- 3 percent.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2140'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2188/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2188/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2188/>;
    dc:modified '2025-07-22T10:26:16'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thies Clima 4.3120.22.012'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thies Clima 4.3120.22.012 Wind Direction Transmitter Classic'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A wind direction measurement device used to measure the direction of the horizontal air flow, with potentiometer output. this instrument is equipped with a sliding potentiometer which offers a theoretically unlimited resolution. Wind direction measurement range: 0 to 360 degrees. Accuracy: +/- 2 degrees. Ambient temperature: -35 to 80 degrees C. Resolution: 1 degree.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2188'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2187/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2187/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2187/>;
    dc:modified '2025-07-21T12:01:56'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Silixa XT-DTS L'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Silixa XT-DTS L Distributed Temperature Sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A ruggedised distributed temperature sensor suitable for use in remote and hostile environments, ideal for longer-distance monitoring. The XT-DTS L works under the principle of Raman based temperature measurement combined with Optical Time-Domain Reflectometry (OTDR). The XT-DTS L can be configured and controlled remotely, via a wireless or satellite link. Low power consumption enables operation with solar or wind power. This instrument can be configured to produce both single-ended and double-ended measurements. Measuring range: 35 km; Sampling and temperature resolution: 100/200 cm, 0.03 degrees celsius; Temperature range: -20 to 60 degrees celsius; Humidity: 10 - 85 percent non-condensing.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2187'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2186/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2186/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2186/>;
    dc:modified '2025-07-21T12:01:56'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Silixa XT-DTS M'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Silixa XT-DTS M Distributed Temperature Sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A ruggedised distributed temperature sensor suitable for use in remote and hostile environments, ideal for shorter-distance, higher-resolution deployments. The XT-DTS M works under the principle of Raman based temperature measurement combined with Optical Time-Domain Reflectometry (OTDR). The XT-DTS M can be configured and controlled remotely, via a wireless or satellite link. Low power consumption enables operation with solar or wind power. This instrument can be configured to produce both single-ended and double-ended measurements. Measuring range: 10 km; Sampling and temperature resolution: 25/50 cm, 0.01 degrees celsius; Temperature range: -40 to 65 degrees celsius; Humidity: 10 - 85 percent non-condensing.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2186'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2185/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2185/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2185/>;
    dc:modified '2025-07-11T16:18:29'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Kistler 4260'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Kistler 4260 Piezoresistive absolute pressure transmitter series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A series of piezoresistive pressure sensors (M070, M091, M097, M098) suitable for use in harsh test environments with high levels of temperature and vibration, and the presence of shock levels. The 4260 series outputs electrical signals in millivolts, volts, or milliamps. This instrument uses a silicon sensing element, mounted within a high-integrity seal assembly isolated from the pressure media, which produces an electrical charge proportional to the pressure applied. Surface mount electronics condition the output from the silicon sensing element and provide temperature compensation. Additional electronic circuit boards can be added to configure the electrical output to suit a variety of data acquisition systems. The pressure sensing assembly features a unique sealing method which enables the sensor to withstand multiple cycles without fatigue. Pressure range (up to:) (psia) 1500 (M070 and M091), 350 (M097), 10000 (M098); maximum pressure without damage (psia): 4500 (M070 and M091), 2100 (M097), 11600 (M098); operating temperature range: -10 to 45 degrees Celsius; compensated temperature range: -10 to 40 degrees Celsius.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2185'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2184/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2184/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2184/>;
    dc:modified '2025-07-10T10:27:36'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Agilent 7700x ICP-MS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Agilent 7700x inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A benchtop quadrupole inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer (ICP-MS) with high-throughput commercial laboratory applications. The 7700x features high-performance sample introduction, matrix tolerant interface, and a fast, frequency matching radio frequency (RF) generator. The high matrix introduction standard on the 7700x enables high dissolved solids samples (such as undiluted seawater) to be run directly. The octupole reaction system (ORS) has been optimised to significantly improve the performance of helium (He) collision mode for the removal of polyatomic interferences. The electron multiplier detector provides a full 9 orders dynamic range. The 7700x has environmental applications such as drinking water analysis. A range of options and accessories are available to further customize the 7700x for advanced applications, such as discrete sampling, chromatographic coupling, and analysing organic solvents or highly corrosive acids.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2184'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2183/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2183/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2183/>;
    dc:modified '2025-07-09T11:21:21'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Mirion Alpha Analyst'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Mirion Alpha Analyst integrated alpha spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An alpha spectrometer designed for high-resolution analysis of alpha-emitting radionuclides and used for environmental monitoring, nuclear research and forensics, and healthcare assessments. The instrument has a modular design and can accomodate up to 6 Dual Spectrometer modules with Passivated Implanted Planar Silicon (PIPS) detectors and two vacuum chambers per module. The interactions as alpha particles from the sample strike the semiconductor material produce charge pulses which are proportional to the energy of the alpha particles. The pulses are converted to voltage and seen as peaks in the associated software. The instrument features automatic recoil suppression control, a clean vent port to reduce moisture and contamination buildup in chambers, a manual emergency venting valve, and Apex Alpha software for complete computer control. A range of detector sizes are available up to a maximum of 1200 mm squared. Based on use with a 450-18AM PIPS detector and a good quality Americium-241 point source: energy resolution <18 keV (full width at half maximum, FWHM) with a detector-source spacing equal to the detector diameter, detector efficiency >25% for detector-source spacing of less than 1 mm, and background < 1 count/hr above 3 MeV.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2183'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2182/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2182/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2182/>;
    dc:modified '2025-07-02T12:42:32'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'RST T strings'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'RST Instruments thermistor strings series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An instrument assembly of thermistors incorporated within a heavy-duty cable. The assembly is environmentally hardened for long-term temperature monitoring under demanding conditions such as burial, deployment in boreholes, or deployment underwater. Each thermistor string is custom manufactured to user specifications with the number of thermistors, spacing between thermistors, sensor accuracy, and length/type of cable differing between instruments. The Negative Temperature Coefficient (NTC) thermistors are non-linear thermistors that experience a drop in resistance with increasing temperature. The measured resistance readings can be converted to temperature using the Steinhart-Hart Linearization equation. Thermistors are curve-matched to desired temperature tolerance over selected temperature ranges, permitting the use of multiple sensors with a single readout or temperature logger. The operating temperature range is -80 degC to 75 degC and the stability is 0.01 degC or better over 100 months at 0 degC. The strings incorporate a triple encapsulation procedure to prevent water ingress and are tested to withstand pressures up to 3.5 MPa. The thermistor resistance rating at 25 degC is 3k ohms as standard, but other options available include 2252, 5k or 10k ohms.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2182'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2181/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2181/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2181/>;
    dc:modified '2025-07-02T11:32:21'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Kistler 4260A'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Kistler 4260A Piezoresistive absolute pressure transmitter'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A piezoresistive pressure sensor suitable for use in harsh test environments with high levels of temperature and vibration, and the presence of shock levels. The 4260A outputs electrical signals in millivolts, volts, or milliamps. This instrument uses a silicon sensing element, mounted within a high-integrity seal assembly isolated from the pressure media, which produces an electrical charge proportional to the pressure applied. Surface mount electronics condition the output from the silicon sensing element and provide temperature compensation. Additional electronic circuit boards can be added to configure the electrical output to suit a variety of data acquisition systems. The pressure sensing assembly features a unique sealing method which enables the sensor to withstand multiple cycles without fatigue. Pressure range 15 to 5000 psi; operating temperature: -65 to 250 degrees Fahrenheit (mV or V), -65 to 175 degrees Fahrenheit (mA).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2181'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2180/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2180/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2180/>;
    dc:modified '2025-07-01T14:35:59'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'PerkinElmer NexION 5000 ICP-MS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'PerkinElmer NexION 5000 multi-quadrupole inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A benchtop multi-quadrupole inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer designed for the determination trace elements in a range of sample types. It features a triple cone interface with OmniRing which can operate in extraction or focusing modes. It is available in two configurations, either non-cleanroom or cleanroom. The plasma is generated by the unique LumiCoil RF load coil, which is air cooled (does not require water or gas cooling), so maintenance-free. The first quadrupole Q0 (Ion Deflector) directs ions to the entrance of the first mass filter. The second quadrupole Q1 (Transmission Analyser 1) acts as a mass filter or as an ion guide to direct ions to the Quadrupole Universal Cell. The third quadrupole Q2 (Universal Cell), empowered by dynamic bandpass tuning, prevents side reactions with residual reaction gases in the cell. The fourth quadrupole Q3 (Transmission Analyser 2) acts as a mass filter or as an ion guide to direct ions to the detector. Transmission Analyser quadrupoles exhibit <0.7 amu mass resolution, driven by a 2.5 MHz power supply.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2180'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2179/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2179/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2179/>;
    dc:modified '2025-06-26T13:58:47'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'AA optode 4835'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Aanderaa 4835 oxygen optode'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A dissolved oxygen sensor designed to mount on an Aanderaa SeaGuard or SmartGuard platform or be used as a stand alone sensor. Measurement based on the ability of selected substances to act as dynamic fluorescence quenchers. The fluorescent indicator is a special platinum porphyrin complex embedded in a gas permeable foil that is exposed to the surrounding water. A black optical isolation coating protects the complex from sunlight and fluorescent particles in the water. This sensing foil is attached to a window providing optical access for the measuring system from inside a watertight titanium housing (depth rating 300 m). The foil is excited by modulated blue light, and the phase of a returned red light is measured. By linearizing and temperature compensating, with an incorporated temperature sensor, the absolute O2 concentration can be determined. Accuracy < 4 uM or 3 %.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2179'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2178/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2178/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2178/>;
    dc:modified '2025-06-26T10:57:26'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Bio-Rad CFX96'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Bio-Rad CFX96 Touch real-time polymerase chain reaction (PCR) detection system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A system for the real-time detection of polymerase chain reaction (PCR) products using fluorescence to enable both quantitative and qualitative analysis. The system combines a CFX96 Optical Reaction Module with a C1000 Touch Thermal Cycler chassis. It can be run as a stand-alone instrument or can be connected to a computer. The inclusion of a fluorescent reporter molecule in each reaction well allows the instrument to monitor the fluorescence as amplification occurs, and the change in fluorescence over time can be used to calculate the amount of amplicon produced in each cycle. The thermal cycler has 6 independently controlled thermal electric modules to maintain tight temperature uniformity and to allow faster heating and cooling during a run, leading to shortened run times. A thermal gradient of up to 24 degC can also be programmed to quickly identify optimal incubation temperature. The optical detection module has 6 excitation LEDs and 6 filtered photodiodes as detectors, with a wavelength range of 450 - 730 nm. Up to 5 targets can be discriminated in a single reaction well, and there are multiple data acquisition modes that allow for the use of single or multiplex protocols. The dynamic range of detection is 10 orders of magnitude, and the sensitivity is sufficient to detect 1 copy of target sequence in human genomic DNA. A CFX Automation System II robotic plate handler can be used with 1 or 2 CFX systems to maximize throughput.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2178'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2177/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2177/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2177/>;
    dc:modified '2025-06-26T08:05:41'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Tisch TE-5170V-BL'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Tisch TE-5170V-BL high volume air sampler'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A high volume ambient Total Suspended Particulate (TSP) air sampler featuring a volumetric flow controller (VFC) for particulate sampling and air quality or emissions monitoring. Total suspended particulates in the air are sampled by a vacuum motor which pulls ambient air onto the 8″ x 10″ glass fiber filter at a flow rate of 44 cubic feet per minute (CFM). TSP air particulate samplers do not use a particle separator which results in the collection of all ambient particulates. The glass fiber filters are weighed pre and post sample and the weight is used to determine the total suspended particulate matter. The flow rate is controlled by a critical orifice with a predetermined orifice hole diameter and a maintenance-free brushless style motor assembly that operates wide open. A 7-day mechanical timer, an elapsed time indicator, and a 24-hour Dickson pressure chart recorder are included with the instrument. An anodized aluminium housing is available as the default setup. Power supply for the TE-5170V-BL model is 110 V, 60 Hz.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2177'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2176/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2176/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2176/>;
    dc:modified '2025-06-24T09:45:11'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Shimadzu RF-10AXL'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Shimadzu RF-10 AXL fluorescence detector'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A high-sensitivity fluorescence spectrometer that can be used as a standalone instrument or in combination with HPLC systems. The fluorescence detector uses the principle of Raman spectroscopy to excite a liquid sample with excitation light from a high precision 150W Xenon lamp. The wavelength of this excitation light is selected by an excitation monochromator and fluorescence from the sample is wavelength selected by the emission monochromator. A photomultiplier detector converts the fluorescence signal into an electrical signal. A refined optical design offers an improved water-Raman signal-to-noise ratio of 300 or higher. A wavelength scanning function determines optimum detection wavelengths for target constituents and a wavelength programming function allows for simultaneous analysis of multiple constituents. More precise wavelength correction improves wavelength accuracy (+/- 2 nm) and reproducibility (+/- 0.2 nm). Wavelength range is 200 - 650 nm and bandwidth is 15 nm on both excitation and emission sides. Different flow cell options are available for a range of specialist applications and optional photomultiplier upgrades can increase the wavelength range of the instrument.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2176'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2174/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2174/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2174/>;
    dc:modified '2025-06-19T14:15:44'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thies Clima 1.1005.50'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thies Clima 1.1005.50 Hygro-ThermoTransmitter'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A combined temperature and humidity sensor consisting of a PT100 resistance thermometer and a hair humidity element, suitable for meteorological applications. Temperature data are output as electrical analogue signals, and humidity is displayed additionally. Temperature is measured using a PT100 resistance thermometer with class B accuracy DIN 1/3 (as defined by IEC 60751). A human hair measuring element is used to determine relative humidity. This sensor available with either a Lemosa connector or a 3 m cable electrical connection. Relative humidity measuring range: 10 - 100 percent; graduation: 1 percent; accuracy: +/- 3 percent (at 20 - 100 percent relative humidity and room temperature). Instrument ambient temperature: -35 to 70 degrees C.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2174'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2175/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2175/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2175/>;
    dc:modified '2025-06-19T14:15:44'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thies Clima 2.1235.00'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thies Clima 2.1235.00 Temperature Transmitter'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A temperature sensor suitable for meteorological applications. Temperature is measured using a PT100 resistance thermometer, with class B accuracy DIN 1/3 (as defined by IEC 60751), protected by a waterproof and stainless-steel tube. This instrument is available with 5 m, 10 m, and 20 m cable length. Temperature measuring range: -30 to 100 degrees C; accuracy: +/- 0.1 kelvin.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2175'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2173/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2173/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2173/>;
    dc:modified '2025-06-19T12:52:51'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Suunto Vyper Novo'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Suunto Vyper Novo dive computer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A dive computer for monitoring water depth and pressure, as well as a divers\' dissolved and free gas in blood and tissue. It can operate in five modes: air, nitrox, gauge, free and off. It has an apnea timer for free diving and a timer in air/nitrox modes. In nitrox mode it can measure up to three gases (oxygen, nitrogen, helium); oxygen outputs are partial pressure of oxygen (0.2 - 3.0) and oxygen saturation (21-50 %). It features the Suunto RGBM algorithm for calculating and monitoring dive decompression and gas switching during ascent. Detailed graphical logs and dive data can be viewed on a PC using Suunto DM5 software. It features an integrated tilt-compensated 3D digital compass (accuracy: +/- 15 degrees), a single-channel 5.3 kHz radio transciever, and a temperature compensated pressure sensor (resolution: 0.1 m). Supports dives down to 120 m.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2173'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2172/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2172/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2172/>;
    dc:modified '2025-06-19T12:18:17'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thermo Scientific GENESYS 30 Vi'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thermo Fisher Scientific GENESYS 30 Visible spectrophotometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A spectrophotometer designed for education, basic QC, and life science applications. The GENESYS 30 Vi features a Tungsten-Halogen lamp (> 1000 hours typical service life), a single beam optical design, and a silicon photodiode detector. The instrument operates at a wavelength range of 325 - 1100 nm (+/- 2 nm accuracy) with an automatic scan speed (up to 1200 nm/min) and a 1 nm resolution. The photometric range spans -3 A to 3 A with an accuracy of +/- 0.002 A (at a 0 - 0.3 A photometric range) or 0.5% of ABS reading (at a 0.301 A - 2.5 A photometric range) and a < 0.002 A/Hr drift. The 5 inch, waterproof screen has a 32 bit colour display and a 800 x 480 pixel resolution and the 23-key rubber keypad ensures a water-tight design. A number of accessories are available for the GENESYS 30 Vi, including: various test tube holders and caps, cell holders, and a thermal printer. A number of line cord options are also available for the instrument, including: US, UK, Europlug, and India.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2172'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2170/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2170/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2170/>;
    dc:modified '2025-06-16T15:14:28'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'CAMECA NanoSIMS 50L'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'CAMECA NanoSIMS 50L secondary ion mass spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The CAMECA NanoSIMS 50L is a secondary ion mass spectrometer (SIMS) for isotopic and trace element analysis at high spatial (sub-micron) resolution. It is based on a coaxial optical design of the ion beam and secondary ion extraction, and on a magnetic sector mass analyser with multicollection. The NanoSIMS 50L has applications in materials science (hydrogen and deuterium analysis), cell biology (aging and biology), geosciences, and environmental microbiology. The NanoSIMS is unique in enabling simultaneously small spot of reactive species, high mass resolving power with near full transmission, and DC beam for high throughput and lowest background and noise. Spatial resolution is down to 50 nanometres, sensitivity is ppm in element imaging. Isotope ratio reproducibility is a few tenths per mille.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2170'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2171/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2171/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2171/>;
    dc:modified '2025-06-16T15:14:28'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Leica DM1000 LED microscope'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Leica DM1000 LED optical microscope'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An optical microscope with clinical laboratory applications, in particular cytology, haematology, and pathology. The DM1000 LED is certified for in-vitro-diagnostics like in-vitro-fertilisation and is suitable for fluorescence analysis. The 4 W LED bulb has a long product life of approximately 100,000 hours assuming six hours of use per day, with a service life of 50 years. The LED bulb provides near daylight, bright illumination, with constant colour temperature and less heat emission. The microscope features a five-fold objective turret, and two-gear focusing knobs, for coarse, fine, and focus stop. It is compatible with the Leica MC170 and 190 HD cameras for snapshots of target samples, and the Leica Hi Plan or N Plan objectives, for 4, 5, 10, 40, and 100 x magnification.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2171'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2169/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2169/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2169/>;
    dc:modified '2025-06-10T09:30:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Agilent 7900 ICP-MS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Agilent 7900 inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A compact benchtop single quadrupole inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer (ICP-MS) for multielement analysis. The range of potential applications is increased by Ultra High Matrix Introduction (UHMI) technology which enables analysis of samples with up to 25% total dissolved solids. The instrument includes a standard low-flow, Peltier-cooled sample introduction system, a 27MHz plasma RF generator, an off-axis ion lens, and a hyperbolic quadropole for superior peak separation. The Orthogonal Detector System (ODS) delivers higher sensitivity and decreases background noise, resulting in a measurement range of up to 11 orders of magnitude, and a 4th-generation Octopole Reaction System (ORS) allows for fast cell gas switching. Ultrafast data acquisition with 10,000 separate measurements per second enables faster analysis of transient signals such as single nanoparticles. Optional extras include different autosamplers, an Advanced Valve System for high sample throughput, and an Advanced Dilution System for automating dilutions. The system can be combined with HPLC or GC systems and there is a range of options for the nebuliser system to suit unique sample types and volumes.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2169'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2168/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2168/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2168/>;
    dc:modified '2025-06-10T09:11:28'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'VG Elemental PQ2+'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'VG Elemental PlasmaQuad 2+ inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An early model of quadrupole inductively coupled mass spectrometer (ICP-MS) designed for the determination of trace elements in a range of sample types. It has a mass range of 0 to 300 amu and a resolution of 1M and 3M over this mass range. The ICP generator is frequency-stabilised with a frequency of 27.12 MHz. The detector is an ion counting system/ analog detection and there is a three stage differentially pumped vacuum system with diffusion pumps on expansion and analyser stages. The 2+ model has a dynamic range of 8 orders of magnitude and uses an 80386 processor. Accessories include laser ablation, an autosampler, HPLC software, and flow injection. This model was introduced in 1988 and is no longer in production.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2168'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2167/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2167/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2167/>;
    dc:modified '2025-06-09T10:57:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'UnSpec tablet GNSS receiver'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Unspecified tablet computer Global Navigation Satellite System (GNSS) receiver'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An in-built Global Navigation Satellite System (GNSS) receiver (e.g. a GPS chip or a GPS module embedded in gpu, cpu, wifi receiver etc.) in an unspecified make and model of mobile tablet device. The GNSS receiver digitally processes signals from a navigation satellite constellation (e.g. GPS, GLONASS, Galileo, etc.) to provide positional information. Precision and accuracy metrics are unspecified.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2167'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2166/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2166/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2166/>;
    dc:modified '2025-05-21T10:54:58'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Nu Attom ES HR-ICP-MS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Nu Instruments Attom Enhanced Sensitivity High Resolution Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass Spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A double focussing, high-resolution (HR), inductively coupled plasma (ICP) mass spectrometer (MS) designed for isotope ratio and quantitative analysis of trace elements in solid and liquid matrices. Its applications span geochronology, environmental science, biological studies, nanoparticle characterisation, and materials research. It features a double-focusing mass analyser that enhances resolution and sensitivity, a fast-scanning detector capable of measuring up to 73 elements in under 105 milliseconds, and a wide dynamic range detector system that ensures accurate quantification across varying concentrations. It uses vertical fixed slit assemblies to provide flexible resolutions from 300 to >10000. The enhanced sensitivity (ES) interface is fitted as standard, providing the highest possible laser ablation sensitivities with minimal matrix effects.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2166'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2165/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2165/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2165/>;
    dc:modified '2025-05-21T10:54:58'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Nu Perspective IRMS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Nu Instruments Perspective Isotope Ratio Mass Spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A high-performance stable isotope ratio mass spectrometer designed for precise measurements of carbon, nitrogen, oxygen, sulphur, and hydrogen isotopes. It features unique zoom optics with no moving parts, enabling accurate analysis from small sample sizes. The IS variant offers exceptional sensitivity and linearity for clumped isotope analysis. Delta 13C and delta 18O carbonate analysis from <5ug sample sizes.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2165'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2164/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2164/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2164/>;
    dc:modified '2025-05-13T08:09:37'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'RBR quadrante'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'RBR quadrante radiometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A four-channel, multi-spectral radiometer with four configurable channels capable of measuring multiple wavebands simultaneously. The channels available in the RBR quadrante are PAR, with a wavelength range of 400 - 700 nm (+/- 0.010 umol/m^2/s resolution), and narrow-band radiation, with a variety of requestable wavelengths available within the range of 400 - 1100 nm (standard wavelength options are: 413, 445, 475, 488, 508, 532, and 560 nm). Resolution is wavelength dependent for narrow-band radiometers. The instrument features a high dynamic range, optimised cosine response, and excellent low-light detection. The instrument is compact, housed in titanium, and depth rated to 2000 m. Operating temperature range is between -5 to 35 degC. Sampling rate is up to 32 Hz. Dynamic range for optical radiometry is > 5.5 decades with an initial accuracy of +/- 2 % and a linearity of +/- 1.5 %. Power requirements are 4 mJ/sample (at 4 Hz or slower) or 36 mW (at 8 Hz or faster). Output is RS-232.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2164'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2163/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2163/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2163/>;
    dc:modified '2025-05-09T14:57:47'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'AA optode 4797'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Aanderaa 4797 pCO2 optode prototype'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A prototype optical sensor for measuring partial pressure of dissolved carbon dioxide (pCO2) in natural waters. A titanium housing includes a sensing foil composed of two fluorescence indicators embedded in an ion-impermeable, hydrophobic, gas permeable polymer layer. One of these indicators responds to the pH change induced by the diffusion of CO2 gas from the surrounding water into the sensing layer. The second indicator acts as a reference with a fluorescence intensity independent of pH. The combined indicators are excited by an amplitude modulated blue light (LED) and the fluorescence light is detected by a photodiode fitted with a filter to exclude light from the excitation light. The lifetime and phase shift of the returning fluorescent signals are used to determine pCO2 concentration. A temperature sensor is included in the titanium housing close to the foil and this allows for temperature compensation by the internal microprocessor. Response time is limited by CO2 diffusion into the foil and is approximately 5 mins in cold water. Sensors are rated to 6000 m depth, have a wide dynamic range (0 - 50000 uatm), and are stable in water for time periods longer than 7 months. Not to be deployed in sulphidic environments as foil is sensitive to hydrogen sulphide. Full description can be found in Atamanchuk et al. (2014).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2163'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2161/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2161/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2161/>;
    dc:modified '2025-05-08T12:41:28'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Garmin GPSMAP 78 series'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Garmin GPSMAP 78 handheld marine Global Positioning System receiver series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A series of handheld battery-powered global positioning system (GPS) devices that includes the GPSMAP 78, 78s and 78sc models. They have an IPX7 waterproof rating, colour mapping, a high-sensitivity receiver, moulded rubber side grips, plus a microSD card slot. The 78s and 78sc also feature a 3-axis tilt-compensated compass and barometric altimeter. The 78sc also comes pre-loaded with BlueChart g2 coastal charts and a worldwide basemap. All three models float in water. 20 hour battery life, 1.43" x 2.15" (3.6 x 5.5 cm); 2.6" diag (6.6 cm) display size. 1.7 GB internal memory.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2161'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2162/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2162/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2162/>;
    dc:modified '2025-05-08T12:41:28'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Hemisphere GNSS V200 series'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Hemisphere GNSS Vector V200 GPS compass series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A series of 424 channel GNSS compasses that includes the V200s and V200n models, used for navigation in a range of applications. Capable of tracking and using GPS, GLONASS, Galileo, BeiDou and QZSS satellites. The V200s uses Hemisphere\'s GNSS Crescent Vector H220 GNSS module, the V200n does not include this. Both feature integrated gyro and tilt sensors to provide heave, roll and pitch information in addition to heading and positioning. Both the V200s and V200n offer 30 cm (RMS) worldwide accuracy via Hemisphere\'s Atlas GNSS global correction service. 10 Hz standard update rate, 20 Hz is optional. Operational temperature range from -40 to +70 degC.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2162'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2160/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2160/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2160/>;
    dc:modified '2025-05-08T10:52:16'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Isotopx IsoProbe-T MC TIMS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Isotopx IsoProbe-T multi-collector thermal ionisation max spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The IsotopX IsoProbe-T is a multi-collector thermal ionisation mass spectrometer (TIMS) with a multiple-Faraday/ion-counting collector assembly for the precise determination of isotopic ratios. Ions are generated in an evacuated source by passing a current through a sample loaded filament and are focused into a beam and are directed towards the entrance slit of the mass spectrometer. The IsoProbe-T incorporates high quality electronics, unique ion-optics and a wide flight tube for 20% relative mass separation in the static mode of collection. The M17 collector assembly is designed for total flexibility and incorporates field proven LIF Faraday collectors, together with the option of a multiple ion counting array, to measure isotope ratios at picogram sample sizes. The detector technology combines very low noise Faraday collectors for the highest < 0.0005% (5 ppm) precision isotope ratio measurements, with a comprehensive range of highly stable, multiple ion counting detectors, that can simultaneously measure for example the isotopes of Uranium and Plutonium in the smallest environmental samples.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2160'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2157/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2157/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2157/>;
    dc:modified '2025-05-06T14:04:35'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Agilent 5110 ICP-OES'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Agilent 5110 inductively coupled plasma-optical emission mass spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Agilent 5110 is an inductively coupled plasma-optical emission mass spectrometer. It is available in three configurations, synchronous vertical dual view (SVDV), vertical dual view, and radial view. It has a dichroic spectral combiner which allows it to use under 30 l of argon per sample. It measures all wavelengths in one and the SVDV version requires only one measurement per sample. The Agilent 5110 has a readback stability over 4 hours of near 100 % for over 10 elements in a 25 % NaCl solution, with a relative standard deviation under 1.3 %. Operating conditions altitude 0-3000 m, 15-30 deg C, 20-80 % relative humidity.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2157'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2156/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2156/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2156/>;
    dc:modified '2025-05-06T14:04:35'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thermo Scientific Dionex ICS-2100'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thermo Fisher Scientific Dionex ICS-2100 ion chromatography (IC) system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Thermo Scientific Dionex ICS-2100 system is a reagent-free ion chromatography system, capable of electrolytic sample preparation and eluent generation. It uses conductivity detection to perform electrolytically generated isocratic and gradient IC separations. It supports 2 and 4 mm columns. It has automated eluent generation, a dual piston pump, and a column heater. The conductivity detector has a resolution of 0.00238 nS/cm and linearity of 1 % up to 1 mS/cm. Operating temperature is 4-40 deg C and relative humidity 5-95 %.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2156'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2159/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2159/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2159/>;
    dc:modified '2025-05-06T14:04:35'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'UIC CM5012'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'UIC CM5012 CO2 coulometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The UIC CM5012 is a CO2 coulometer providing absolute determinations of carbon in any CO2-containing gas stream. The coulometer detects carbon in the range of 0.01 ug to 100 mg. Its cell contains monoethanolamine and a colorimetric pH indicator, as well as a platinum cathode and silver anode. The cell is placed between a light source and a photodetector. The CO2 is quantitative absorbed, reacting with the monoethanolamine to form a titratable acid. The titration current is continually measured and is the titrant making sample calibration unnecessary. The coulometer has an integrated timer and RS232 interface, and can provide results in the following units: ug C, mg C/L, ug CO2, ug CO3, ug equivalent. The measurement range is 0.0001 to 100 % of carbon, readability of 0.01 ug of carbon, detection limit below 2 ug of carbon, accuracy of 1.25 %, and precision of 0.2 %.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2159'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2158/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2158/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2158/>;
    dc:modified '2025-05-06T14:04:35'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Waters 2475'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Waters 2475 multiwavelength fluorescence detector'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Waters 2475 multiwavelength fluorescence detector is a multichannel, tunable, fluorescence detector designed for high-performance liquid chromatography (HPLC) applications. The detector operates at wavelengths between 200 and 900 nm which can be used in single or multichannel mode. The detector optics include xenon arc lamp, two ellipsoidal mirrors and one parabolic mirror, filters, slits, photomultiplier tube (PMT), axially illuminated flow cell, and blazed, plane, and concave holographic diffraction gratings. The 2475 detector provides outputs in emission and energy units. Emission units are normalised to a standard water reference and their magnitude is as independent of the PMT gain as possible. Energy units are similar to traditional HPLC fluorescence detectors, they are directly influenced by the instrumental variables and therefore are less reliable.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2158'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2155/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2155/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2155/>;
    dc:modified '2025-05-01T10:10:01'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'METAS PCI-160'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'METAS AS PCI-160 Crawler Interface Container'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A versatile and robust hardware unit designed for sensor integration and communication in demanding environments. It plays a crucial role in various Metas products by enabling efficient data exchange between sensors and external systems. It features two main sections - a power section and an interface section, positioned on opposite container lids, with ample space for additional payload. Several units can be installed together in a Master-Slave configuration. The Interface can communicate with external mission planner module if available in the system. The standard net length of the container is 380 mm, measured between flanges, but it can be adjusted based on the payload space needs, with container thickness varying accordingly. The container is available in four pressure ratings: 150, 300, 400, and 600 Bar. It includes necessary power modules to run all connected sensors, including propulsion drivers and optional METAS MSL-13 drivers. The power section can be customised to fit specific sensor requirements.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2155'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0805/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0805/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0805/>;
    dc:modified '2025-04-30T15:31:55'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'AA optode'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Aanderaa optode'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A generic label for a range of dissolved oxygen sensors produced by Aanderaa covering various mounting options. Each has a specific model number but in this case it is not known. All make measurements based on the ability of selected substances to act as dynamic fluorescence quenchers. The fluorescent indicator is a special platinum porphyrin complex embedded in a gas permeable foil that is exposed to the surrounding water. A black optical isolation coating protects the complex from sunlight and fluorescent particles in the water. This sensing foil is attached to a window providing optical access for the measuring system from inside a watertight titanium housing.The foil is excited by modulated blue light, and the phase of a returned red light is measured. By linearizing and temperature compensating, with an incorporated temperature sensor, the absolute O2 concentration can be determined.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL0805'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2154/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2154/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2154/>;
    dc:modified '2025-04-28T09:05:44'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Hydroptic UVP5 series'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Hydroptic Underwater Vision Profiler 5 {UVP5} imaging sensor series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A submersible imaging sensor designed to study particles and zooplankton simultaneously and to quantify them in a known volume of water. The UVP counts and sizes all objects > 100 um and records images of aggregates and plankton > 700 um. It is usually operated as a stand-alone system, attached to a CTD-Rosette frame. The UVP5 acquires only in-focus images in a volume of water delimited by a light beam issued from red light-emitting diodes (LEDs) in approximately 100 microsecond flashes. The collimated light beam illuminates a sampling volume of approximately 1 litre per image which are acquired and processed at up to 20 Hz. When interfaced with conventional CTD measuring devices, the total abundance of particles can be displayed in real time, integrated with the CTD data. The system has a typical depth range of 6000 m.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2154'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2153/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2153/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2153/>;
    dc:modified '2025-04-28T09:05:44'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SBE Deep SeapHOx v2'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sea-Bird SBE Deep SeapHOx V2 conductivity, temperature, pH, and dissolved oxygen system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Sea-Bird Deep SeapHOx V2 combines the SeaFET V2 pH sensor with the SBE 37-SMP-ODO MicroCAT CTD+DO sensor. This system is designed to be used on moorings to collect oceanographic data. Outputs include conductivity, temperature, pressure, dissolved oxygen, and pH. Deep SeaFET V2 adapts the MBARI/SIO Deep-Sea DuraFET technology to measure pH in a deep moored package. The SeapHOx V2 allows for the integrated data collection of pH with the critical oceanographic and biological measurement of temperature, salinity, and oxygen. The integrated package also allows the SeaFET V2 to take advantage of the SBE 37\'s pumped flow path and anti-fouling technology, extending deployment durations in some cases. The conductivity ranges from 0 to 7 S/m with an accuracy of 0.0003 S/m, and resolution of 0.00001 S/m. Temperature ranges from -5 to 45 degC with an accuracy of 0.002 degC (-5 to 35 degC) or 0.01 degC (35 to 45 degC), and resolution of 0.0001 degC. Pressure ranges 0 to 20 m, 100 m, 350 m, 600 m, 1000 m, 2000 m, with an accuracy 0.1 percent of full-scale range, and resolution 0.002 percent of full-scale range. Dissolved oxygen ranges to 120 percent of surface saturation in all natural waters (fresh and salt), accurate to 3 umol/kg or 2 percent, and resolution 0.2 umol/kg. pH ranges from 6.5 to 9, accuracy 0.05, and resolution 0.004. Depth rating is 2000 m.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2153'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2152/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2152/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2152/>;
    dc:modified '2025-04-25T15:29:41'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Hanna HI93501P'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Hanna Instruments HI93501P digital thermometer with thermistor probe'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A handheld digital thermometer designed to be compatible with Hanna Instruments HI762 or FC762 lines of thermistor probes, enabling measurements in different media (air, gases, water, semi solids). The thermometer is battery powered, and typically provided with the FC762PW probe. Depending on the probe, the thermometer is capable of spot measuring temperatures from -50 to 150 degC. Resolution is 0.1 degC, response time is 10 seconds. Probe accuracy (for the FC762PW probe) is +/- 0.3 degC (-10 to 80 degC), or +/- 0.7 degC (remaining measurement range).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2152'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2151/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2151/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2151/>;
    dc:modified '2025-04-25T12:02:19'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thies Clima 7.1416.10.0xx'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thies Clima 7.1416.10.0xx Silicon UVAB Sensor E 1.1'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A radiation sensor designed to acquire UV-A and UV-B irradiance separately, using a silicon photo diode sensor. Multiple versions of this instrument are available with differing power supply and data output analog output type. UV-A is measured up to 100 W/m^2 over a spectral range 310 - 400 nm; maximum sensitivity: 335 nm. UV-B is measured up to 0.5 W/m^2 over a spectral range 265 - 315 nm; maximum sensitivity: 297 nm. Measurements are cosine-corrected. This instrument has a non-linearity of +/- 3 percent and absolute error of +/- 10 percent. Cosinus-correction: Fehler f2 +/- 2 percent. This instrument operates in ambient temperatures -30 to 60 degrees C.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2151'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1306/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1306/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1306/>;
    dc:modified '2025-04-25T10:32:50'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Idronaut OS 316 plus'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'IDRONAUT Ocean Seven 316 plus CTD'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An underwater CTD probe designed for on-line profiling or used in self-recording applications such as on moorings or AUVs. It comprises a piezoresistive pressure transducer, a platinum resistance thermometer, a platinum seven-ring quartz conductivity cell, a pressure-compensated polarographic oxygen sensor, a pH glass sensor and solid gel pH reference probe. The conductivity cell employs a large diameter (8 mm) and a short length (46 mm) which facilitates self-flushing and prevents clogging. The conductivity cell design does not require platinum black deposition and can be cleaned in the field without re-calibrating. The probe can accommodate up to 16 auxiliary sensors. The probe can be interfaced with a telemetry deck unit for real-time data acquisitions. It is depth rated to 7000 dbar. Pressure accuracy: 0.01 - 0.05 % FS. Temperature accuracy: 0.002 deg C. Conductivity accuracy: 0.003 mS/cm.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1306'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0861/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0861/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0861/>;
    dc:modified '2025-04-25T10:32:49'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Idronaut OS 304 CTD'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'IDRONAUT Ocean Seven 304 CTD'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A low powered micro conductivity temperature depth (CTD) recorder containing 512 Mb logging memory, selectable conductivity range and fast sampling rate between 0.1 - 8 Hz. It can be optionally equipped with a highly accurate Precise pressure transducer, IDRONAUT OEM Turbidity Meter and IDRONAUT dissolved oxygen sensor.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL0861'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0213/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0213/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0213/>;
    dc:modified '2025-04-25T10:32:49'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Idronaut OS 320 CTD'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'IDRONAUT Ocean Seven 320 CTD'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A fast response, multi-parameter conductivity, temperature and depth probe. It can be fitted with an additional (redundant) pair of conductivity and temperature sensors allowing the precision and quality of the data to be checked.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL0213'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2150/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2150/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2150/>;
    dc:modified '2025-04-24T13:01:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'ClearWater Phosphate Sensor'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ClearWater Phosphate Lab-On-Chip (LOC) sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A miniaturised microfluidic phosphate sensor based on advanced lab-on-chip (LOC) technology. Designed to perform an automated in-situ wet-chemical analysis in any liquid water environment. Can be deployed in time-series mode for fixed-location deployments or in profiling mode for autonomous vehicles or profilers. The sensor draws in a water sample which passes through a 0.45 um pore-size filter membrane to prevent blockages. The sample is mixed with chemical reagents and the resulting colour change is measured using LEDs and photodiodes. The sensors carry onboard reference standards which are analysed frequently to correct for instrumental drift. All chemical waste is stored within waste bags inside the instrument. Data can be accessed in real time via the RS232 interface or post deployment via USB download. Sample volume is 0.6 mL and measurement interval is 27 mins with calibration or 9 mins in profiling mode (no calibration during profile measurement). Measurement range is 0 - 10uM phosphate (0 - 20 uM is available upon request). Limit of detection is 0.05 uM and typical precision is 2%. Temperature range 0 - 35 degrees C. Depth rating 6000 m. Sensor can be configured for use within an autonomous vehicle or any other application where reagent housing might not easily fit upon request.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2150'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2149/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2149/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2149/>;
    dc:modified '2025-04-11T12:02:07'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'RBR tridente'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'RBR tridente scattering fluorescence sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A three-channel optical fluorescence and backscatter sensor with three configurable channels, capable of making multiple fluorescence and backscatter measurements simultaneously. The sensor is capable of measuring any three of the following channels: chlorophyll a, fDOM, phycocyanin, phycoerythrin, rhodamine, fluorescein, backscatter, and turbidity. The sensor features a high dynamic range permitting exposure to full sunlight with very low detection limits. A dry bay original equipment manufacturer (OEM) variant of the RBR tridente is available for vehicle integration applications. The instrument is compact, and depth rated to 6000 m or 1250 m (dry bay), with a titanium housing. Operating temperature range is between -5 to 35 degC. Sampling rate is up to 32 Hz. Centroid angle for optical measurements is 120 degrees, with a sensing volume of ~1.3 mL, R-squared linearity of 0.99, and calibration accuracy of 5%. Power requirements are 20 mJ/sample (at 4 Hz or slower) or 384 mW (at 8 Hz or faster). Output is RS-232.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2149'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2148/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2148/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2148/>;
    dc:modified '2025-04-11T09:52:48'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Unknown Hach probe'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Unknown Hach multiparameter handheld probe'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An unknown model of Hach multiparameter handheld probe or series of probes for electrochemistry measurements, capable of measuring at least salinity, conductivity, temperature, oxygen, oxidation reaction potential, turbidity, total dissolved solids, and pH in water samples. Typical applications include water quality testing in the field or laboratories.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2148'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2146/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2146/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2146/>;
    dc:modified '2025-03-28T11:52:14'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Satlantic OCR-507 ICSA'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Satlantic {Sea-Bird} OCR-507 ICSA multispectral radiometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A cosine-response radiometer designed for multiwavelength measurements of irradiance for in-air use. The instrument uses silicon photodiodes as detectors and a custom low-fluorescence interference filter. The standard version comes with 7 customer defined channels that measure wavelengths in the bandwidth from 400 to 700 nm. The radiometer has a sampling rate of 7 to 24 Hz and a spectral bandwidth of 10 or 20 nm. An optional bioshutter is available to decrease biofouling on the optical faces of the sensor. Bandwith range can be customised. Typical Noise Equivalent Irradiance (NEI) is 2.5 x 10-3 uW cm-2 nm-1.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2146'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2147/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2147/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2147/>;
    dc:modified '2025-03-28T11:52:14'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Satlantic OCR-507 ICSW'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Satlantic {Sea-Bird} OCR-507 ICSW multispectral radiometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A cosine-response submersible radiometer designed for multiwavelength measurements of irradiance for in-water use. The instrument uses silicon photodiodes as detectors and a custom low-fluorescence interference filter. The standard version comes with 7 customer defined channels that measure wavelengths in the bandwidth from 400 to 700 nm. The radiometer has a sampling rate of 7 to 24 Hz and a spectral bandwidth of 10 or 20 nm. The instrument can be mounted on real-time profilers, moored and autonomous deepwater buoys and autonomous underwater vehicles, and has a depth rating of 350 m. An optional bioshutter is available to decrease biofouling on the optical faces of the sensor. Bandwith range can be customised. Typical Noise Equivalent Irradiance (NEI) is 2.5 x 10-3 uW cm-2 nm-1.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2147'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2145/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2145/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2145/>;
    dc:modified '2025-03-28T09:39:24'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Vaisala GMP343 CO2 probe'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Vaisala GMP 343 atmospheric carbon dioxide probe'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An instrument designed for the measurement of atmospheric carbon dioxide. The GMP343 is a small, lightweight but rugged CO2 probe with low power consumption and heat emission designed for ecological measurements in harsh environments, especially outdoors. The probe contains a CARBOCAP sensor comprising three major components - a light source, a Fabry-Perot interferometer and a non-dispersive infrared (NDIR) detector. The interferometer allows light of two wavelengths to pass through to the detector - the wavelength at which carbon dioxide absorbs light and a nearby non-absorbing wavelength for comparison purposes. The GMP343 can output both numerically filtered and raw measurement data, and it can also compensate the measurement with an internal temperature measurement and user-set relative humidity, pressure and oxygen values. Diffusion and flow-through models are available, and an M170 indicator can be used as a display, communication, and data logging device. Accuracy (excluding noise) at 25 deg C and 1013 hPa after factory calibration with 0.5 % accurate gases for the 0 -1000 ppm model is +/- 3 ppm + 1 % of reading.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2145'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2144/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2144/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2144/>;
    dc:modified '2025-03-26T11:59:16'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Leco AMA254'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Leco AMA 254 Advanced mercury analyser'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The AMA254 advanced mercury analyser is an atomic absorption spectrometer (AAS) designed to determine total mercury content in solids and liquids without pre-treatment or pre-concentration. Samples are decomposed using combustion (approximately 750 degC). The gases are pased through catalytic compounds and impurities are removed. Gold-plated ceramics collect the mercury vapour which is then heated to 900 degC and released to the detection system. The vapour passes through the cuvette and is detected by the AAS. The AAS uses a lamp that emits at a wavelength of 253.7nm, and a silicon UV diode detector. The instrument range at 100 mg is 0.5 ppb to 5 ppm, with a precision of 0.25 ppb or <5 % relative standard deviation. It works with nominal sample sizes of 100 mg of solids and 100 ul of liquids. It requires environmental conditions of 0 to 35 deg C and humidity between 20 and 80 %.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2144'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2142/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2142/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2142/>;
    dc:modified '2025-03-26T11:59:15'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thermo Scientific MAT 253 IRMS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thermo Fisher Scientific MAT 253 isotope ratio mass spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Thermo Scientific MAT 253 stable isotope ratio mass spectrometer is designed to determine isotopic ratios of D/H, 13C/12C, 15N/14N, 34S/32S, 28Si/29Si, Ar, Kr, and Xe. It can be used in dual inlet mode or continuous flow mode. The instrument includes amplifiers up to 50 V, hydrogen continuous flow capability, up to eight simultaneous acquisition channels, and the integration of Isodat software. Its analytical performance and ruggedness are due to the geometry with stigmatic focus and large dispersion. The magnetic sector field is generated by an electromagnet. Collectors are located at the focal plane of the full deflection radius, and they use individually shielded Faraday cups. The MAT 253 has a mass range of 1-150 Dalton at 10 kV, a sensitivity of 600 molecules CO2 per mass 44 ion in the dual inlet mode, and 900 molecules/ion in the continuous flow mode. For this instrument, the ambient temperature must be 18 - 28 deg C, with a relative humidity of 20 - 70 %. It requires power 230 V. and compressed air 350 - 500 Kpa (50 - 75 psi).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2142'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2143/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2143/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2143/>;
    dc:modified '2025-03-26T09:53:21'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Nu Plasma III MC-ICP-MS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Nu Instruments Plasma III Multi-Collector Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass Spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A double-focusing multi-collector inductively coupled plasma source mass spectrometer (MC-ICP-MS) featuring unique variable dispersion optics. The instrument uses zoom optics to provide simultaneous isotopic measurements of elements from lithium to actinide. The static collector array includes 16 Faraday collectors and up to six ion counting detectors (either scanning electron microscope, SEM, or Daly), which can be interspersed amongst the Faraday collectors. Faraday preamplifiers can be fitted to adjust signal amplification and increase the detector\'s range. Abundance sensitivity < 2 ppm pre-deceleration filter and < 0.5 ppm post-deceleration filter. An additional lens element, Enhanced Abundance Transfer Optics (EATO) provides abundance sensitivity < 1 ppm pre-filter and < 0.05 ppm post-filter. Collector slit widths can be modified to obtain full resolution from interferences.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2143'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2141/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2141/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2141/>;
    dc:modified '2025-03-24T12:45:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Hydroptic UVP6 series'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Hydroptic Underwater Vision Profiler 6 {UVP6} imaging sensor series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A series of submersible imaging sensors incorporating the UVP 6 High Frequency (HF) model and Low Power (LP) model. Designed to study particles and zooplankton simultaneously and to quantify them in a known volume of water. The UVP counts and sizes all objects > 60 um and records images of aggregates and plankton > 620 um. The UVP6 acquires only in-focus images in a volume of water delimited by a light beam issued from a red laser diode in approximately 100 microsecond flashes. The collimated light beam illuminates a sampling volume of approximately 0.6 litre per image and the pixel size is 73 um. The images can be acquired at up to 20 Hz. The system weighs 1.6Kg in water and consumes very low power. It has been utilised in long term mooring, cabled observatories, CTD-rosette frames, gliders, AUVs, profiling floats and drifting lines. When interfaced with conventional CTD measuring devices, the total abundance of particles can be displayed in real time, integrated with the CTD data. The system has a typical depth range of 6000 m. The High Frequency model is fitted with a powerful image processor allowing acquisition and processing of images at up to 20 Hz (max power = 6 W). The Low Power model is fitted with a low power image processor allowing to adjust the mean power (<0.8 W) according to the acquisition rate (<1.3 Hz).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2141'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1316/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1316/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1316/>;
    dc:modified '2025-02-28T09:00:06'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'WET Labs ECO BB2FL-SLC'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'WET Labs {Sea-Bird WETLabs} ECO Puck Triplet BB2FL-SLC {FLBBBB-SLC} scattering fluorescence sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A variant of the ECO Puck Triplet (http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0673/). It is a three-optical-sensor, user-defined instrument that carries a fluorometer and 2 scattering meters. ECO Pucks are real‐time only sensors as they are integrated onto the OEM platform that provides power and data handling. The SLC designation signifies this is a third generation model that is specific for integration into Slocum gliders with a dry science bay. The fluorometer and scattering meters are single wavelength sensors. The model is fitted with an added copper faceplate for bio-fouling mitigation and is depth-rated to 1000 m.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1316'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2139/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2139/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2139/>;
    dc:modified '2025-02-21T14:18:37'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thermo Scientific Dionex ICS-5000'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thermo Fisher Scientific Dionex ICS-5000 ion chromatography (IC) system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An ion chromatography system which offers a full range of reagent-free components. This instrument can be configured to use single or dual pumps. The single-channel Dionex ICS-5000 can be configured to run capillary, microbore or standard bore IC applications. A dual Dionex ICS-5000 system can be configured with any combination of these applications. This system uses an eluent generator (EG) to generate high purity acid or base eluents from deionized water, in the amount and concentration needed for sample analysis, configurable for single or dual channel operation. Eluent regeneration may also be used without an EG - eluent regeneration uses the suppressor to reconstitute the starting eluent, allowing use of a single 4-liter bottle of eluent for up to four weeks. An eluent organizer (EO) module is used to contain eluent spills and leaks. The ICS-5000 detector/chromatography module (DC) can accommodate components for two channels, plumbed either serially or in parallel, in a temperature-controlled environment. Available DC components include conductivity detectors, electrochemical detectors, injection valves, switching valves, guard and separator columns, suppressors, and Dionex IC cubes or ICS-5000 Automation Manager. Detectors outside of the DC include a Dionex ICS Series Photodiode Array Detector (PDA); Dionex ICS Series Variable Wavelength Detector (VWD); MSQ Plus Mass Spectrometer.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2139'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2138/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2138/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2138/>;
    dc:modified '2025-02-14T11:24:53'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thermo Scientific iCAP TQ ICP-MS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thermo Fisher Scientific iCAP TQ inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A benchtop triple quadrupole (TQ) inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometer (ICP-MS) with a four channel peristaltic pump, three plasma gas flow controllers, and four QCell mass flow controllers. The iCAP TQ utilises triple quadrupole technology which allows the analyte signal to be isolated from interferences, enabling the analysis of complex or high-matrix samples. The high frequency (4 MHz) quadrupole mass analyser has pre and post filters for isolation of wanted ions. The instrument features Peltier cooled high purity quartz or perfluoroalkoxy alkane (PFA), and low volume, baffled cyclonic or double pass spray chambers to efficiently filter out larger aerosol droplets for improved plasma stability. A reaction finder method development assistant aids easy method development. The plasma system is designed to rapidly adapt to changing matrices and provide robustness for challenging samples such as highly volatile organic solvents. The argon ICP ion source has a digital, solid state radiofrequency generator, and dynamic frequency impedance matching the plasma at 27 MHz. The iCAP TQ has applications in trace element analysis of solid or liquid (particularly sediment or sea water) samples. It has a nebuliser default flow rate of 400 uL/min.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2138'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1523/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1523/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1523/>;
    dc:modified '2025-02-11T08:34:19'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SMRU GSMDL tag'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'SMRU Fastloc GSM {GSMDL} GPS phone tag'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A GPS system mounted on marine mammals that is used for animal tracking and monitoring dives. A GPS sensor is used to locate the animal upon surfacing. Mobile cellular networks are used to transfer data when the animal is close to land. Data are stored to internal memory where data transfer is not possible. Environmental sensors are used to determine the behaviour of animal dives. To enable GPS location, the system splits the GPS determination into to separate phases. A snapshot of satellite data is captured and the pseudo-ranges are calculated on board and stored. After these pseudo-ranges are relayed ashore, they are combined with publicly available archived ephemeris information to compute locations. The integrated system consists of a Fastloc GPS sensor (Wildtrack Telemetry Systems, UK), a quad-band GSM mobile phone module, and precision wet/dry pressure and temperature sensors. Battery or solar powered versions are available.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1523'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2135/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2135/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2135/>;
    dc:modified '2025-02-10T13:29:48'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Leica Viva GS10 GNSS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Leica Viva GS10 GNSS receiver'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A 120-channel, multiple-frequency Global Navigation Satellite System (GNSS) receiver designed for precise positioning in various survey applications. It tracks various signals including GPS, GLONASS, Galileo, and BeiDou. The receiver features an integrated antenna, long battery life and rugged design for field durability. It can be used in conjunction with Leica\'s Captivate processing software. 8 mm accuracy in real-time kinematic mode.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2135'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2136/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2136/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2136/>;
    dc:modified '2025-02-10T13:29:48'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'R2Sonic SONIC 2020'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'R2Sonic SONIC 2020 wideband multibeam echosounder'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A wideband multibeam echosounder designed for shallow water hydrographic and bathymetric surveys. Operates at user-selectable frequencies between 200 and 400 kHz, providing swath coverage selections from 10 to 130 degrees. Has along and across-track beam widths of 1 degrees. An optional ultra-high resolution 700 kHz frequency version is available. Standard immersion depth of 100 metres, or an optional 4000 metre version. Up to 1024 soundings per ping.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2136'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2137/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2137/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2137/>;
    dc:modified '2025-02-10T13:29:48'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Septentrio Altus NR3 RTK-GNSS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Septentrio Altus NR3 RTK-GNSS receiver'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A 144-channel, multiple-frequency real-time kinematic (RTK) Global Navigation Satellite System (GNSS) receiver designed for precise positioning in various survey applications. It tracks various signals including GPS, GLONASS, Galileo, and BeiDou. It includes APME+ multipath technology and IONO+ scintilliation mitigation to ensure position accuracy, together with LOCK+ to maintain tracking during mechanical shocks or vibrations. It also features AIM+ anti-jamming technology to reduce signal interference. 16 GB internal memory, with options to collect and store data in the cloud via PinPoint-GIS. Horizontal accuracy of 1.2 m, vertical accuracy of 1.9 m. Horizontal RTK accuracy of 0.6 cm + 0.5 ppm, vertical RTK accuracy of 1 cm + 1 ppm.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2137'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2134/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2134/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2134/>;
    dc:modified '2025-02-10T10:34:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'BD Accuri C6'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'BD Biosciences Accuri C6 flow cytometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A laser-based benchtop flow cytometer designed to detect fluorochromes (including FITC, PE, PerCP, and APC). The instrument is equipped with a blue and red laser, two light scatter detectors, and four fluorescence detectors with optical filters optimised for the detection of fluorochromes. Pre-optimised detector settings make the system easier to use. Optional filters and the selectable lasers module expand the available fluorochrome combinations. Laser and optical alignments are sand locked down during manufacture, ensuring standardised fluorescence performance and removing the need for users to adjust detector voltages. A low-pressure pumping system drives the fluidics, and a sheath-focused core enables event rates of up to 10,000 events per second and a sample concentration of over 5 x 10^6 cells per mL. In addition, the system derives sample volume and can calculate absolute counts or sample concentration per microliter. The system supports 48- and 96-well plates and deep-well plates, and is also supplied with a 24-tube rack for standard 12 x 75-mm tubes. Laser excitations are 488 and 640 nm. Minimum detectable particle size is 0.5 um, and minimum sample volume is 300 uL. Custom sample flow rates are between 10 - 100 uL/min, with a custom core diameter of 5 - 40 um. A maximum of 1 million events can be performed per sample well.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2134'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2133/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2133/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2133/>;
    dc:modified '2025-01-21T15:37:28'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'UIC CM150'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'UIC CM150 total carbon analyser'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An analytical system used to measure total carbon, total organic carbon, and total inorganic carbon in solid and/ or liquid samples. This instrument combines a high temperature combustion furnace, self-contained acidification module, and highly sensitive CO2 sensor to analyse a range of sample types. The coulometer automatically measures the absolute mass amount of carbon dioxide resulting from sample combustion or acidification and is sensitive to all CO2. Total carbon, total organic carbon, and total inorganic carbon are distinguished by the manner in which the CO2 is formed - either by combustion or acidification. The CM150 includes a CM5017 CO2 Coulometer, CM5300 Horizontal Furnace, and a CM5330 Acidification Module. This instrument requires no user-calibration and linear detection is available from less than 1 ug carbon to over 10000 ug carbon, relative standard deviations of 0.2 percent or better are common for standard materials. For smaller concentration, an absolute deviation of approximately 1 ug C is typical.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2133'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2132/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2132/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2132/>;
    dc:modified '2025-01-10T16:23:48'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'FSI 3D ACM'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Falmouth Scientific 3D Acoustic Current Meter'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A 3-dimensional acoustic current meter used to measure the speed and direction of water currents. Compact size and light weight make the 3D ACM suitable for deployment on multiple meter arrays. The current meter outputs velocity measurements in 3 axes. Averaged and/ or burst data output available. This instrument incorporates a 3-axis internal flux-gate compass and 2-axis tilt sensor to provide true current vector direction. High-accuracy conductivity, temperature, and depth sensor package is available. Velocity - Accuracy: +/- 2 percent of reading, or 1 cm/sec; Resolution: 0.01 cm/sec; Range: 0-300 cm/sec. Direction - Accuracy: +/- 2 degrees; Resolution: 0.01 degrees; Range: 0 - 360 degrees. Sampling rate: 2 Hz maximum. Depth rating: 1000 m with phenolic housing, 7000 m with titanium housing.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2132'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2131/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2131/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2131/>;
    dc:modified '2025-01-10T16:23:48'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'NOBSKA MAVS-3'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'NOBSKA MAVS-3 Acoustic Current Meter'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The MAVS-3 (Modular Acoustic Velocity Sensor) is a true 3-axis acoustic current meter used to measure the speed and direction of water currents. The current meter employs a differential travel time measurement technique. Measurements across 4 acoustic axes are used to provide a true vector averaged velocity measurement. This instrument features no moving parts to foul. Small transducer size significantly reduces the disturbance to water flow. This instrument is suitable for long-term deployment. Additional sensors are available to measure tilt, temperature, conductivity, and pressure. Internal logging memory is available from 4 - 96 MB. Programmable burst mode and triggered sampling mode are available. Speed - Accuracy: 0.3 cm/sec; Resolution: 0.03 cm/sec; Range: 200 cm/sec (other options available). Direction - Accuracy: +/- 2 degrees; Resolution: 1 degree; Range: 360 degrees. Drift: 0.15 cm/sec per month. Depth rating up to 6000 m.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2131'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1897/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1897/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1897/>;
    dc:modified '2024-12-18T10:07:47'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'NOC AESA camera system'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'National Oceanography Centre AESA camera system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The benthic camera system typically mounted on the UK National Oceanography Centre\'s Autosub6000 autonomous underwater vehicle is known as the AESA camera, named after the original project associated with its design (Autonomous Ecological Surveying of the Abyss). It uses the FLIR (formerly Point Gray Research Inc.) Grasshopper 2 GS2-GE-50S5C-C camera (5 MP). This is based on the Sony ICX625 CCD imaging sensor. More than one camera can be fitted in various orientations (e.g. oblique, downward-looking etc). The camera is fitted with a Navitar NMV-8M23 Machine Vision Lens, and a bespoke inhouse-developed Xenon high speed flash, with a 10J driver circuit. The camera sensor and lens are housed in bespoke inhouse-developed housing with a flat viewport. The 10J flash is housed in similar housing with the same flat viewport. The camera system can be removed and mounted on other NOC-owned vehicles such as the Remotely Operated Vehicle (ROV) ISIS, with the same setup and configuration. Image Data Output: 8, 12, 16 and 24-bit digital data. 1000 Mbit/s data transfer rate. Operating temperature: 0 to 40 degC.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1897'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2130/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2130/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2130/>;
    dc:modified '2024-12-13T16:43:31'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'BRIZO-X'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Xeos Technologies Brizo-X Directional GNSS Wave Height Sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A 400-plus channel dual-frequency wave height measurement device appropriate for use in marine environments. This instrument measures wave statistics such as wave height and direction, and features an internal logger. The wave motion sensor with integral GNSS antenna supports GPS and GLONASS. The sensor is housed in a fully weather and waterproof enclosure for use in rugged marine environments. Optional embedded Iridium communications are available on the Brizo-X, including modem and internal antenna. Measurement accuracy: better than 1 percent. Sampling frequency: 2 Hz.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2130'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2129/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2129/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2129/>;
    dc:modified '2024-12-13T16:43:31'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'GeoMax Zenith60'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'GeoMax Zenith 60 series GNSS Receiver'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Zenith60 series are 555-channel multi-frequency Global Navigation Satellite System (GNSS) smart antennas used for a range of survey and construction applications. The multi-constellation and Precise Point Positioning (PPP) receiver is capable of tracking GPS, GLONASS, BeiDou, Galileo, and QZSS constellations. The receiver also tracks SBAS EGNOS, WAAS, MSAS, GAGAN. The Zenith 60 is available in the following variants: LTE; LTE-UHF; LTE-IMU; LTE-UFH-IMU. With the IMU variant, an optional internal navigation system is used to determine tilt and tilt orientation, removing the need for calibration. Tilt compensation is resistant to magnetic interference. An optional UHF radio module is available. Operating temperature: -40 to 65 degrees C. 99.99% receiver reliability.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2129'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2128/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2128/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2128/>;
    dc:modified '2024-12-10T09:20:56'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Airmar PB100'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Airmar PB100 Ultrasonic WeatherStation'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An all-in-one ultrasonic weather sensor designed for precise weather data collection, integrating multiple sensors into a single, compact unit with no moving parts, making it highly durable and maintenance-free. Ideal for marine applications such as boating and sailing, as well as land-based weather monitoring. It provides digital outputs in NMEA 0183 format, including apparent wind speed, apparent wind direction, magnetic compass heading, air temperature, relative humidity, dew point temperature, wind chill temperature, angle of vessel pitch, angle of vessel roll, barometric pressure, Global Positioning System (GPS), vessel speed over ground (SOG), vessel course over ground (COG), true wind speed, true wind direction, heading relative to true north, true wind chill temperature, and true wind speed relative to water (requires speed-through-water input). Additional sensors may be fitted. The PB100 delivers real-time weather data essential for navigation and safety.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2128'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2127/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2127/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2127/>;
    dc:modified '2024-12-05T12:13:58'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Metrohm 797 VA Computrace'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Metrohm 797 VA Computrace voltammetry system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A computer-controlled voltammetric measuring stand with built-in potentiostat and galvanostat. Applications include voltammetric trace analysis of metal ions and other substances, and Cyclic Voltammetric Stripping (CVS) for the determination of additives in electroplating baths. Operation of the 797 VA Computrace Stand follows the potentiostatic 3-electrode principle in which the voltage of the working mercury electrode is controlled by means of a virtually currentless Ag/AgCl reference electrode to the preset desired value and the current flows across a separate platinum auxiliary electrode. The pneumatically operated Multi-Mode Electrode (MME) can operate in Hanging Mercury Drop Electrode (HMDE), Dropping Mercury Electrode (DME), or Static Mercury Drop Electrode (SMDE) modes. A Rotating Disk Electrode with exchangeable electrode tips can be used in place of the MME. Additional accessories such as autosamplers and sample processors allow for full automation of analysis, and a range of accessory kits are available to extend the range of applications. The instrument supports over 220 analytical methods.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2127'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2125/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2125/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2125/>;
    dc:modified '2024-12-03T15:30:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SMRU Ltd SRDL'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'SMRU Ltd Satellite Relay Data Logger'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A generic label for a range of Satellite Relay Data Loggers (SRDL) produced by SMRU Instrumentation. These instruments are designed for mounting onto marine animals. Each SRDL has a specific model name but in this case, it is not specified. Standard SRDL sensors can include pressure and temperature sensors, wet/ dry sensor (operation in salt and fresh water), and speed sensor. Data is recorded by these instruments while the animal is subsurface, and dive records are relayed via satellite when above surface. The SRDL TDR capability allows each model to retain a continuous record of depth and temperature, which can be retrieved upon recovery.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2125'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2126/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2126/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2126/>;
    dc:modified '2024-12-03T15:30:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Wildlife Computers TDR'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Wildlife Computers time depth recorder'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A generic label for a range of time-depth recorders produced by Wildlife Computers designed for mounting onto marine animals. Each time depth recorder has a specific model number but in this case, it is not specified. The Wildlife Computers TDR\'s record a range of data in, addition to time-depth, depending on model, including light level, stomach temperature, and GPS. A variety of sensor options and shape configurations are available depending upon desired output and research animal.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2126'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2123/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2123/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2123/>;
    dc:modified '2024-12-02T16:18:09'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Wise group AIM3'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'WISE Group Automasjon og Data Adaptive Inertial Matrix AIM3 Wave sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A wave measurement device utilising Adaptive Inertial Matrix (AIM) technology, integrating multiple Inertial Measurement Units (IMUs) such as accelerometers, gyroscopes, and magnetometers to provide precise wave data. It is used in offshore wind farms for wave analysis, autonomous vessels for navigation, and environmental research for long-term monitoring. The AIM3 Wave Sensor is characterized by high accuracy, durability in harsh oceanic environments, and flexibility to support additional devices like GPS and meteorological sensors. Adaptive Inertial Matrix (AIM) is a unique hardware and software development based around MEMS technology (Micro Electrical Mechanical Systems) digital Inertial Measurement Units (IMU). Operating by detecting and measuring wave motion through its IMUs, the built-in processor performs on-board data processing for real-time and non-real-time outputs. Optional configurations include different encapsulation materials, local data storage, and analogue output. Its capabilities encompass comprehensive data analysis, customizable outputs, and remote mounting options, making it a versatile and reliable tool for various maritime and environmental applications. The sensor outputs wave height with a resolution of 0.001 meters and accuracy better than 1.5%, wave period with a resolution of 0.1 seconds and accuracy better than 1%, and wave direction with full 360-degree measurement and accuracy better than 1 degree.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2123'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2124/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2124/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2124/>;
    dc:modified '2024-12-02T16:18:09'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'ZX300M'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ZX Lidars ZX300M continuous wave LiDAR'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A Continuous Wave LiDAR for high-precision wind measurement designed for offshore applications. It is used for offshore wind resource assessment, construction monitoring, and operations and maintenance. It is made with a multi-layered, highly insulated plastic housing that resists UV and marine growth. Optional configurations include integration with floating LiDAR platforms and additional meteorological sensors The sensor outputs wind speed with an accuracy of 0.1 m/s and direction variation of less than 0.5 degrees. Operating by measuring the line-of-sight wind speed every 20 milliseconds (sampling rate of 50Hz), it effectively mitigates motion-induced errors. The measurement range spans from 10 to 300 meters.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2124'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2122/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2122/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2122/>;
    dc:modified '2024-11-21T12:24:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SBE 11+ V2 deck unit'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sea-Bird SBE 11plus V2 deck unit'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A rack-mountable deck unit for use with the Sea-Bird SBE 9plus CTD unit for real-time data acquisition and recording. It supercedes the V1 model which was discontinued in 1997. It supplies DC power to the CTD, decodes the serial data stream, and passes the data to a computer (in IEEE-488 or RS-232 format). The deck unit\'s back-panel switch permits continuous operation from 120 or 240 VAC 50/60 Hz input power. The front panel provides numeric display of frequency and voltage via a thumbwheel switch and 8digit LED readout. Other features include a 300 baud modem interface which provides power and real-time control for a water sampler (SBE 32 Carousel, or G.O. 1015 or 1016 Rosette) or remote serial output device. The modem permits water sampler control through the 11plus deck unit or via Seasave software. Also features an NMEA Interface that merges position data with the CTD data, and an A/D converter for a surface PAR light sensor. Operating temperature from +5 to +40 degC, altitude up to 2000 m.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2122'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2121/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2121/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2121/>;
    dc:modified '2024-11-14T12:54:03'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'AML-3 RT'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'AML Oceanographic AML-3 RT sonde'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A highly configurable multiparameter sonde designed for a wide range of data collection applications. The AML-3 RT has the ability to both stream data while in-situ and internally record data. Configurations include Sound Velocity Profiling (SVP); Sound Velocity and Turbidity Profiling (SVP Tu); Conductivity Temperature and Depth (CTD); Sound Velocity/ Conductivity Temperature and Depth (SVCTD). Streep lamp UV biofouling protection may be added to this instrument. This instrument allows for three sensors to be simultaneously installed on the endcap, and another two sensors may be connected externally. This instrument has a depth capability of up to 500 m with acetal pressure housing, or up to 6000 m with titanium pressure housing.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2121'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2120/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2120/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2120/>;
    dc:modified '2024-11-12T09:04:09'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SBE 5T/5P pump'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sea-Bird SBE 5 submersible pump series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The SBE 5 pump series includes the 5T (titanium) and 5P (plastic) models. It is a modular component on several Sea-Bird CTD packages, and is standard equipment on the SBE 9plus CTD and 25/25plus Sealogger CTD. The pump flushes water through the conductivity cell at a constant rate independent of the CTD\'s motion, improving dynamic performance. Models in the series differ in housing material and depth rating: the 5T model has a titanium housing, allowing it to reach depths of up to 10,500 metres, while the 5P model uses a plastic housing with a depth limit of 600 metres. The pump may also be suitable for custom applications, where pressure heads are in less than 300 cm of water and flow rates are less than 100 mL/sec. The 5 series features a centrifugal pump head, ball-bearing motor, and several motor speed options (1300, 2000, 3000, and 4500 rpm speeds) to meet various flow requirements.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2120'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2119/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2119/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2119/>;
    dc:modified '2024-11-11T15:49:56'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'MTi-320'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Movella Xsens MTi-320 active heading tracker'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The MTi-320 is a compact, high-performance Active Heading Tracker (AHT) designed for embedded applications that require precise motion tracking. It fuses data from a gyroscope, accelerometer, and magnetometer to deliver accurate orientation and heading measurements. The instrument utilises Xsens\' optimised strapdown algorithm (AttitudeEngine), the sensor is capable of high-speed, real-time dead-reckoning calculations at 1 kHz, accurately capturing high-frequency motions. The device is IP51-rated and supports a wide operating temperature range from -40°C to 85°C. It is supported by a graphical user interface (GUI) and is compatible with the MT Software Suite, providing tools for integration and development across various platforms, including ROS. The MTi-320 offers 0.5 degrees RMS roll/pitch accuracy, a 1 kHz update rate, a 2000 deg/S gyroscope range, 16 g accelerometer range, and a +/- 8 G magnetometer range, with 0.2% linearity, 0.25 mG resolution, and 0.5 mG total RMS noise.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2119'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0751/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0751/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0751/>;
    dc:modified '2024-11-05T13:59:02'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Applanix POSMV 320'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Trimble Applanix POSMV 320 global positioning system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Applanix POS/MV 320 (POS) is a vessel positioning and orientation system. The GPS aided Inertial Motion Unit (IMU) provides measurements of roll, pitch, and heading that are all accurate to +/- 0.02 degrees. There have been 5 generations of this unit (V1-5).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL0751'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1348/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1348/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1348/>;
    dc:modified '2024-11-04T11:57:46'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Septentrio PolaRx5 GNSS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Septentrio PolaRx5 Global Navigation Satellite System (GNSS) receiver'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A multi-frequency Global Navigation Satellite System (GNSS) receiver used to track visible signals (GPS, GLONASS, Galileo, BeiDou, IRNSS) for satellite positioning. It is specifically designed to support applications in earth science. The device operates by converting signals from visible satellites into a position on earth. The PolaRx5 offers 544 channels for GNSS tracking, and uses Advanced Interference Mitigation (AIM+) technology to filter out sources of interference. The devices also uses Septentrio’s patented APME+ multipath mitigation technology to eliminate short delay multipath without the introduction of bias. APME+ can be activated or de-activated by the user as necessary. It is compatible with Septentrio PolaNt Choke Ring B3/E6 Antenna. The IP68 compliant variant, the PolaRx5e comes complete with battery. The PolaRx5 offers an in-built web-UI, internal data logging up to 16 GB, and up to 100 Hz raw data output. Operating temperature ranges between -40 and +65 degC, and measurement precision (unsmoothed pseudorange) ranges from 1.5 to 25 cm.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1348'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1491/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1491/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1491/>;
    dc:modified '2024-11-04T11:56:57'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'R2Sonic SONIC 2022'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'R2Sonic SONIC 2022 wideband multibeam echosounder'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A multibeam echosounder with applications in construction, dredging, autonomous surface vehicles, and offshore oil and gas. Operates at frequencies between 170 and 450 kHz, providing coverage up to 400 metres. Has along and across-track beamwidths ranging from 0.6 to 2 degrees depending on the frequency used. An optional ultra-high resolution 700 kHz frequency version is available. Standard immersion depth of 100 metres, or an optional 4000 metre version. Selectable swath coverage between 10 and 160 degrees. Up to 1024 soundings per ping.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1491'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1281/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1281/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1281/>;
    dc:modified '2024-11-04T11:56:34'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'R2Sonic SONIC 2024'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'R2Sonic SONIC 2024 wideband multibeam echosounder'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A broadband - wideband high resolution shallow water multibeam echosounder. It is particularly suited to small survey vessel, ROV and AUV operations in the hydrographic,  dredging, defence and research sectors. It primarily measures bathymetry elevation and consists of a projector, receiver and dry-side Sonar Interface Module (SIM). Sonar operation is controlled via  graphical user interface on a PC or laptop. Commands are transmitted via Ethernet interface to the SIM, which supplies power to the sonar heads, synchronizes multiple heads, time tags sensor data,  relays data to the workstation and relays commands to the sonar head. The receiver head decodes the sonar commands, triggers the transmit pulse, then receives, amplifies, beamforms, bottom detects,  packages and transmits the data through the SIM via Ethernet to the control PC. Key characteristics of the SONIC 2024 include user selectable operating frequencies, with flexibility to trade off  resolution, range and controlling interference from other active acoustic systems. It has variable swath coverage selections from 10 to 160 degrees, the ability to rotate the swath sector, as well  as roll stabilisation. The frequency and swath coverage may also be selected in real-time. Frequency ranges from 170 kHz - 450 kHz at 1 Hz resolution (optional 700 kHz). Number of soundings up to  1024 per swath, per head. The pulse length is 15 to 1115 micro-seconds, ping rate is up to 60 Hz and depth rating is 100m.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1281'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2118/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2118/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2118/>;
    dc:modified '2024-11-01T12:27:09'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Europa Scientific TracerMass'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Europa Scientific TracerMass Stable Isotope analyser'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A compact desktop isotope ratio mass spectrometer (IRMS) developed to analyse samples of 15N and 13C. This instrument measures the isotopic ratio of Carbon-13 and Nitrogen-15 in a sample using an electron ionisation source.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2118'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2117/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2117/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2117/>;
    dc:modified '2024-11-01T11:54:26'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Nu Plasma II MC-ICP-MS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Nu Instruments Plasma II Multi-Collector Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass Spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A double-focusing multi-collector inductively coupled plasma source mass spectrometer (MC-ICP-MS) featuring unique variable dispersion optics. The instrument provides high precision isotope ratio data for elements across the mass range from 3 to 300 amu. The collector assembly includes 16 Faraday collectors and there are up to five ion counting discrete dynode multipliers, interspersed amongst the Faraday collectors at the low-mass end of the array. This overall configuration allows comprehensive coverage of isotopic applications over the full mass range. The Nu Plasma II has true high-resolution capabilities made possible by the application of three sets of independently adjustable slits positioned at various points on the instrument. Deceleration filters may be installed on up to five ion counting collectors to improve abundance sensitivity.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2117'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2116/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2116/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2116/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-31T11:18:22'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Biospherical QCP-2300-HP'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Biospherical Instruments QCP-2300-HP underwater PAR sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A cosine-corrected Photosynthetically Active Radiation (PAR) quantum irradiance profiling sensor for use in underwater applications. A variant of the QCP-2300 model, it uses a pressure-tolerant XSG-4-BCL-HP connector and is designed for operation in natural waters up to 6800 m in depth. The sensor has a flat quantum response over the PAR spectral region (400-700 nm) with the spectral response being shaped by a combination of absorbing glass and custom dichroic filters to accurately cover the PAR spectral region and block out-of-band radiation. Ideal to measure light available for photosynthesis on a flat surface. Custom-housed versions are available for gliders and other undersea monitoring applications. Low power consumption of <5 mA at 6-15 volts DC and can operate in a temperature range of -2 to 50 degrees Celsius. Uses a 24‐bit analog to digital converter to sample the signal before the logarithm is computed and the result is converted into an analog voltage (0‐5 V).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2116'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2115/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2115/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2115/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-22T09:19:35'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'OIS Sediment Profiling Camera'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Ocean Imaging Systems Model 3731 Sediment Profiling Camera'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A sediment profile imaging (SPI) camera that provides in situ imaging of organism-sediment relationships on the seafloor. It obtains a vertical cross section of the sediment-water interface by imaging the sediment in profile via a water-filled prism. High resolution images of an area as large as 320 square centimetres of sediment profile are taken with each exposure. Optical clarity is not affected by local water conditions since the optical path is through air and distilled water. The current version incorporates a 24.1 megapixel Nikon DSLR camera. A variety of designs are available including ones for diver operation, for handheld operation in shallow environments, and with a lightweight aluminium frame for small boat operations. It is available in three housing materials and rated for either 1000 or 4000 m operation. Can be utilised to measure a wide variety of features including grain size, small-scale surface boundary roughness, dredged material thickness, apparent redox potential discontinuity depth, and surface microbial aggregations. The system is easily upgradeable with some systems built in the early 1990s still in use.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2115'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2114/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2114/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2114/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-18T11:47:28'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Chelsea Technologies LabSTAF'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Chelsea Technologies Group LabSTAF single turnover active fluorometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An active fluorometer that employs the Single Turnover Active Fluorometry (STAF) method for the quantitative assessment of phytoplankton photosynthesis. It enables evaluation of primary productivity by phytoplankton (PhytoPP) towards greater understanding of the global carbon cycle. LabSTAF represents a significant update to Chelsea\'s well-established FastOcean Fast Repetition Rate fluorometer (FRRf) and Act2 laboratory systems. It provides 39 fluorescence parameters, in addition to the standard Fluorescent Light Curve (FLC) parameters, plus options for the correction of baseline fluorescence. Includes Windows-based RunSTAF software, enabling a wide variety of experimental setups, manual control or automated operation, plus real-time data analysis. 20 mL maximum sample volume. Excitation waveband central wavelengths: 416, 452 x2, 473, 495, 534, 594, 622 nm. Actinic light source collimated output from 10 to > 1600 umol photons m-2 s-1. Can resolve Fv with an amplitude equivalent to the fluorescence signal generated under 452 nm excitation by 0.001 mg m-3 of chlorophyll.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2114'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2113/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2113/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2113/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-17T16:26:39'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Druck PTX 7500 series'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Druck PTX 7500 series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A series of industrial pressure transmitters suitable for a wide range of pressure media and operating conditions. The 7500 series operates using the principle of piezoresistance, using a silicon sensor. The PTX 7500 series consists of models using a range of electrical connections - PTX 7511 Integral Cable (IP65); PTX 7516 6 Pin Bayonet (IP65); PTX 7517 DIN 43650A Plug/Socket (IP 65); PTX 7533 Integral Cable (IP 67); PTX 7535 M20 Female Conduit (IP 65). Operating temperature range: -40 to 100 degrees C (80 degrees C maximum for PTX 7511/ 7533). Accuracy: Best straight Line +/- 0.1 percent F.S. typical (+/- 0.2 percent maximum). Operating pressure ranges up to 700 bar.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2113'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2111/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2111/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2111/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-09T09:57:04'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'NOC UoS pCO2 sensor'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'National Oceanography Centre pCO2 optode sensor - Clarke et al. (2017)'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A custom-designed pCO2 sensor, developed by the National Oceanography Centre Southampton in collaboration with the University of Southampton. The sensor is based on an immobilised indicator entrapped in a polymer membrane alongside a fluorescent reference compound. The indicator fluorescence is altered according to the partial pressure of CO2 of the seawater. This instrument uses a sensing spot from PreSens GmbH which is attached to the fibre optic cable head. Custom-made electronics (Sensoptics Ltd. SGS 42000) and dedicated software (Sensoptics Photon Counter V1.2) are used to record the fluorescence decay curve. The optode measures at a rate of 0.0028 Hz. pCO2 is measured with an uncertainty of +/- 0.0917 micro atm. More information may be found in https://eprints.soton.ac.uk/384569/.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2111'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1650/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1650/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1650/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-03T14:39:03'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Hydroptic UVP5-Shallow'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Hydroptic Underwater Vision Profiler 5 Shallow {UVP5} imaging sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A submersible imaging sensor designed to study large (>100 &micro;m) particles and zooplankton simultaneously and to quantify them in a known volume of water. The UVP sizes marine snow, aggregates > 100 &micro;m and images plankton > 500 &micro;m and can be operated as a stand-alone system or deployed on a Rosette frame, ROV, AUV or mooring. The UVP5 acquires only in-focus images in a volume of water delimited by a light beam issued from red light-emitting diodes (LEDs) in 100 &micro;s flashes. The typical light beam illuminates an area of 4x20 centimetres which gives a sampling volume of 1 litre per image. When interfaced with conventional CTD measuring devices, the distribution of particles and fauna can be displayed in real time integrated with the CTD metadata. The high-resolution digital image can then be processed by the computer. Optional telemetry. The imaging rate is 20 images per second. The system is depth-rated to 600 m. The shallow model is only available with a standard definition camera.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1650'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1577/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1577/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1577/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-03T14:32:57'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Hydroptic UVP5-DEEP'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Hydroptic Underwater Vision Profiler 5 DEEP {UVP5} imaging sensor series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A submersible imaging sensor designed to study particles and zooplankton simultaneously and to quantify them in a known volume of water. The UVP counts and sizes all objects > 100 um and records images of aggregates and plankton > 700 um. It is usually operated as a stand-alone system, attached to a CTD-Rosette frame. The UVP5 acquires only in-focus images in a volume of water delimited by a light beam issued from red light-emitting diodes (LEDs) in approximately 100 microsecond flashes. The collimated light beam illuminates a sampling volume of approximately 1 litre per image which are acquired and processed at up to 20 Hz. When interfaced with conventional CTD measuring devices, the total abundance of particles can be displayed in real time, integrated with the CTD data. The system has a typical depth range of 6000 m. The system can be equipped with either a standard or high definition camera.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1577'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2110/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2110/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2110/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-03T14:20:33'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Hydroptic UVP5 HD'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Hydroptic Underwater Vision Profiler 5 High Definition {UVP5} imaging sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A submersible imaging sensor designed to study particles and zooplankton simultaneously and to quantify them in a known volume of water. The UVP counts and sizes all objects > 100 um and records images of aggregates and plankton > 700 um. It is usually operated as a stand-alone system, attached to a CTD-Rosette frame. The UVP5 acquires only in-focus images in a volume of water delimited by a light beam issued from red light-emitting diodes (LEDs) in approximately 100 microsecond flashes. The collimated light beam illuminates a sampling volume of approximately 1 litre per image which are acquired and processed at up to 20 Hz. When interfaced with conventional CTD measuring devices, the total abundance of particles can be displayed in real time, integrated with the CTD data. The system has a typical depth range of 6000 m. The HD model is equipped with a 4 megapixel camera (pixel size: approximately 90 um).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2110'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2109/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2109/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2109/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-03T14:20:33'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Hydroptic UVP5 SD'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Hydroptic Underwater Vision Profiler 5 StandarD {UVP5} imaging sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A submersible imaging sensor designed to study particles and zooplankton simultaneously and to quantify them in a known volume of water. The UVP counts and sizes all objects > 100 um and records images of aggregates and plankton > 700 um. It is usually operated as a stand-alone system, attached to a CTD-Rosette frame. The UVP5 acquires only in-focus images in a volume of water delimited by a light beam issued from red light-emitting diodes (LEDs) in approximately 100 microsecond flashes. The collimated light beam illuminates a sampling volume of approximately 1 litre per image which are acquired and processed at up to 20 Hz. When interfaced with conventional CTD measuring devices, the total abundance of particles can be displayed in real time, integrated with the CTD data. The system has a typical depth range of 6000 m. The standard model is equipped with a 1.3 megapixel camera (pixel size: 140-184 um).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2109'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2108/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2108/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2108/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-03T10:48:44'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel '4H JENA CONTROS HydroFIA TA'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel '4H JENA engineering CONTROS HydroFIA TA total alkalinity analyser'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An automated flow through analyser for total alkalinity in seawater. Used for ocean acidification and carbonate chemistry research, monitoring of biological processes, and aquaculture monitoring. It can be used for continuous monitoring during surface water applications as well as for discrete water sample measurements. It can be integrated into existing systems on Voluntary Observing Ships (VOS) such as FerryBoxes. Seawater is acidified by injection of hydrochloric acid (HCl). After acidification the generated CO2 is removed by a TOUGH membrane based degassing unit, resulting in an open cell titration. The subsequent pH determination is carried out by indicator dye (Bromocresol Green) and VIS absorption spectrometry. Together with salinity and temperature, the resulting pH is used for the calculation of total alkalinity. Measurement cycles of less than 10 mins. Low sample (<50 ml) and reagent (100 uL) consumption. Operating temperature range from +5 - +30 degC. Salinity range from 20 - 37 PSU. Measuring range from 400 umol/kg (dynamic) to 2000 umol/kg (standard). Resolution of 0.1 umol/kg. Accuracy +/- 5 umol/kg, precision +/- 2 umol/kg.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2108'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2106/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2106/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2106/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-03T10:41:26'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Hydroptic UVP5 Z'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Hydroptic Underwater Vision Profiler 5 standard Zoomed {UVP5} imaging sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A submersible imaging sensor designed to study particles and zooplankton simultaneously and to quantify them in a known volume of water. The UVP counts and sizes all objects > 100 um and records images of aggregates and plankton > 700 um. It is usually operated as a stand-alone system, attached to a CTD-Rosette frame. The UVP5 acquires only in-focus images in a volume of water delimited by a light beam issued from red light-emitting diodes (LEDs) in approximately 100 microsecond flashes. The collimated light beam illuminates a sampling volume of approximately 1 litre per image which are acquired and processed at up to 20 Hz. When interfaced with conventional CTD measuring devices, the total abundance of particles can be displayed in real time, integrated with the CTD data. The system has a typical depth range of 6000 m. The zoomed model is equipped with a 1.3 megapixel camera (pixel size: approximately 1204 um).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2106'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2107/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2107/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2107/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-03T10:41:26'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Hydroptic UVP6 HF'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Hydroptic Underwater Vision Profiler 6 High Frequency {UVP6} imaging sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A submersible imaging sensor designed to study particles and zooplankton simultaneously and to quantify them in a known volume of water. The UVP counts and sizes all objects > 60 um and records images of aggregates and plankton > 620 um. The UVP6 acquires only in-focus images in a volume of water delimited by a light beam issued from a red laser diode in approximately 100 microsecond flashes. The collimated light beam illuminates a sampling volume of approximately 0.6 litre per image and the pixel size is 73 um. The images can be acquired at up to 20 Hz. The system weighs 1.6Kg in water and consumes very low power. It has been utilised in long term mooring, cabled observatories, CTD-rosette frames, gliders, AUVs, profiling floats and drifting lines. When interfaced with conventional CTD measuring devices, the total abundance of particles can be displayed in real time, integrated with the CTD data. The system has a typical depth range of 6000 m. The High frequency model is fitted with a powerful image processor allowing acquisition and processing of images at up to 20 Hz (max power = 6 W).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2107'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1578/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1578/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1578/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-03T09:54:55'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Hydroptic UVP6 LP'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Hydroptic Underwater Vision Profiler 6 LP {UVP6} imaging sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A submersible imaging sensor designed to study particles and zooplankton simultaneously and to quantify them in a known volume of water. The UVP counts and sizes all objects > 60 um and records images of aggregates and plankton > 620 um. The UVP6 acquires only in-focus images in a volume of water delimited by a light beam issued from a red laser diode in approximately 100 microsecond flashes. The collimated light beam illuminates a sampling volume of approximately 0.6 litre per image and the pixel size is 73 um. The images can be acquired at up to 20 Hz. The system weighs 1.6 kg in water and consumes very low power. It has been utilised in long term mooring, cabled observatories, CTD-rosette frames, gliders, AUVs, profiling floats and drifting lines. When interfaced with conventional CTD measuring devices, the total abundance of particles can be displayed in real time, integrated with the CTD data. The system has a typical depth range of 6000 m. The low power model is fitted with a low power image processor allowing to adjust the mean power (<0.8 W) according to the acquisition rate (<1.3 Hz).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1578'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2105/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2105/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2105/>;
    dc:modified '2024-10-02T14:56:48'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'VG Optima IRMS'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'VG Optima Isotope-Ratio Mass Spectrometer (IRMS)'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An Isotope-Ratio Mass Spectrometer (IRMS) used to determine the d13C/12C of carbon in different materials (organic matter, carbonates, dissolved carbon in water). This instrument analyses the isotopic content of materials which have first been processed to CO2. The prepared and purified CO2 is then ionized and analysed by the IRMS, which operates in dual-inlet mode for the measurement of the stable isotope ratio of CO2.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2105'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2101/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2101/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2101/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-23T16:16:13'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel '4h Jena Contros HydroCR Co2'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel '4H JENA engineering CONTROS HydroC CO2 pCO2 sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A versatile underwater carbon dioxide sensor suitable for in-situ and online measurements of dissolved CO2. Applications include use on unmanned platforms such as ROV and AUV, long-term deployment on seabed observatories, buoys, and moorings, and profiling applications using water sampling rosettes. The partial pressure of carbon dioxide is determined by infrared absorption spectrometry of dissolved CO2 molecules which have passed through the instrument membrane into the detector chamber. Concentration dependent infrared light intensities are converted into an output signal from calibration coefficients stored in the sensor\'s firmware and data from additional sensors within the gas circuit. This instrument has deep sea capability, depth rating up to 6000 m. Temperature range: -2 to 35 degrees C. Measuring range: 200 - 1000 micro atmospheres. Resolution: < 1 micro atmosphere. Accuracy: 0.5 percent of reading.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2101'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2102/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2102/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2102/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-23T16:16:13'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Aqua Troll 500 sonde'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'In-Situ Aqua TROLL 500 multiparameter sonde'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Aqua TROLL 500 is a fully customizable five-port multiparameter sonde with capacity for four interchangeable sensors and an antifouling wiper, designed for spot-checking and profiling applications or long-term monitoring, depending on method of communication between instrument and operator. This instruments smartphone interface enables simplified calibration, panoramic data view, and report creation. vented and non-vented options are available, as well as the addition of a range of sensors including CTD and nutrient sensors. Pressure rating up to 150 PSI. Operating temperature: -5 to 50 degrees C.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2102'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2100/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2100/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2100/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-23T16:16:13'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Aqua Troll 600 sonde'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'In-Situ Aqua TROLL 600 multiparameter sonde'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Aqua TROLL 600 is a fully customizable five-port multiparameter sonde with capacity for four interchangeable sensors and an antifouling wiper, designed for short-term and long-term deployment. This instruments smartphone interface enables simplified calibration, panoramic data view, and report creation. vented and non-vented options are available, as well as the addition of a range of sensors including CTD and nutrient sensors. Pressure rating up to 350 PSI. Operating temperature: -5 to 50 degrees C.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2100'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2103/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2103/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2103/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-23T16:16:13'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Aqua Troll 700 sonde'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'In-Situ Aqua TROLL 700 multiparameter sonde'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Aqua TROLL 700 is a fully customizable, seven-port multiparameter sonde with capacity for six interchangeable sensors and an antifouling wiper, designed for spot-checking and profiling applications or long-term monitoring, depending on method of communication between instrument and operator. This instruments smartphone interface enables simplified calibration, live time-series data view, and report creation. vented and non-vented options are available, as well as the addition of a range of sensors including CTD and nutrient sensors. Pressure rating up to 350 PSI. Operating temperature: -5 to 50 degrees C.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2103'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2104/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2104/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2104/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-23T16:16:13'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Aqua Troll 800 sonde'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'In-Situ Aqua TROLL 800 multiparameter sonde'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Aqua TROLL 800 is a fully customizable, seven-port multiparameter sonde, with capacity for six interchangeable sensors and an antifouling wiper, designed for short-term or long-term deployments in fresh water or saltwater, surface water or groundwater. The Aqua TROLL 800 features long-lasting battery power and a smartphone interface that enables simplified calibration, live time-series data view, and report creation. vented and non-vented options are available, as well as the addition of a range of sensors including CTD and nutrient sensors. Pressure rating up to 350 PSI. Operating temperature: -5 to 50 degrees C.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2104'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2098/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2098/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2098/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-23T16:16:13'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Gill GMX560'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Gill Instruments MaxiMet Marine GMX560 weather station'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A multiparameter compact weather station designed for use in marine environments. The GMX560 outputs five measured meteorological parameters: Wind speed and direction, temperature, humidity, and pressure, in addition to multiple derived parameters. This instrument comes with optional heating function and optional integrated GPS capability, GPS timestamp and calculation of true wind if the platform is moving. Wind speed - range: 0 - 60 m/s; accuracy up to 0.3 m/s RMSE; resolution: 0.01 m/s. Wind direction - range: 0 - 360 degrees; accuracy up to +/- 3 degrees; resolution: 1 degree. Air temperature - range: -40 - 70 degrees C with heating; accuracy: +/- 3 degrees; resolution: 0.1 degree. Relative humidity - range: 0 - 100 percent RH; accuracy: +/- 2 percent RH; resolution: 0.1 percent RH. Barometric pressure - range: 300 - 1250 hPa; accuracy: +/- 0.4 hPa (absolute), +/- 0.08 hPa (relative); resolution: 0.1 hPa.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2098'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2099/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2099/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2099/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-23T16:16:13'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Valeport MIDAS ECM'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Valeport MIDAS ECM multiparameter current meter'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A versatile point current meter designed for real time underwater current measurement and autonomous deployment. The ECM outputs measurements of current speed and direction. This instrument comes with titanium housing, polyurethane sensor components, and a stainless-steel cage. Optional CTD and turbidity sensor are available to be added to this instrument. The titanium housing gives this instrument a depth rating up to 5000 m. This instrument can measure current speed at a range of 0 - 5 m/s, accuracy +/- 1 percent, and resolution of 0.001 m/s. Current direction can be measured over a range of 0-360 degrees, accuracy +/- 1 degree, and resolution of 0.001 degrees.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2099'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2097/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2097/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2097/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-17T10:53:14'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Thermo Scientific iCAP 7400 ICP-OES radial'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Thermo Fisher Scientific iCAP 7400 ICP-OES Radial inductively coupled plasma-optical emission mass spectrometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A compact benchtop inductively coupled plasma-optical emission mass spectrometer designed for the analysis and quantitation of trace elements in both liquid and solid samples. This instrument is configured with dedicated radial plasma viewing. A Charge Injection Device (CID) detector enables a selection of wavelengths between 166-847 nm. It features a 4-channel, 12 roller, peristaltic pump and a solid state, free-running 27.12 MHz RF plasma generator. Thermo Scientific Qtegra ISDS software is featured to minimize task times. It has an optimized purge gas distribution system which reduces the requirement for optical purge gas and employs only a 2 litre per minute purge during operation. Autosampler accessories are available, allowing the analysis of 180 to 720 liquid samples unattended. Optional sample handling kits are available for organic/ volatile solvent-based, hydrofluoric acid, and high solid solutions.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2097'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2096/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2096/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2096/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-10T09:52:24'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Valeport MIDAS SVX2'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Valeport MIDAS SVX2 combined SVP/CTD profiler'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A combined CTD and sound velocity profiler designed for use in both autonomous or real-time deployments. It measures sound velocity (m/s), conductivity (mS/cm), temperature (deg C) and pressure (bar) using a digital time of flight sound velocity sensor, a high stability conductivity sensor, a high accuracy temperature compensated piezo-resistive pressure transducer, and a fast response PRT temperature sensor. The instrument uses the concept of distributed processing to sample all data at the same instant and has 5 sampling modes - continuous, burst, trip/profile, conditional, and delay. The MIDAS SVX2 has a titanium housing and a stainless steel deployment cage. The instrument has a maximum depth rating of 6000 m (when equipped with 600 bar pressure sensor).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2096'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2095/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2095/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2095/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-06T08:13:05'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Kongsberg EM2040C MKII'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Kongsberg EM 2040C MKII multibeam echosounder'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A shallow water multibeam echosounder ideal for high resolution mapping and inspection applications. Sonar head pressure rated to 50 m depth. The MKII series has upgraded hardware and software to increase the swath and improve the data quality. Utilises both CW and FM chirp pulses for long range capability. Operating frequency range from 200 to 400 kHz with frequency selection in steps of 10 kHz. Output sample rate up to 60 kHz. Angular coverage for 200 to 320 kHz modes are 140 degrees with one sonar head allowing coverage of 5.5. times water depth. Full roll and pitch stabilisation techniques in real time as well as nearfield focussing both on transmit and receive. Available as single or dual head models. Can be delivered with dual swath capability or with 700 kHz mode. Easy to install and convenient for small boats.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2095'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2094/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2094/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2094/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-05T12:02:35'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'GO 8060 pCO2'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'General Oceanics model 8060 pCO2 measuring system'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An autonomous analytical system for measuring carbon dioxide in oceanic surface water. The system is an enhanced redesign of the previous 8050 model, necessitated by the discontinuation of the LI-7000 gas analyser. The model 8060 uses the LI-7815 gas analyser and consists of a headspace equilibrator, an infrared CO2 analyser, a network of valves and pumps, a barometer enclosure plus integrated computer and software. The following optional interface kits can be integrated: Seapoint Turbidity Meter, Seapoint Chlorophyll Fluorometer, Anderaa 4835 Oxygen Optode, Seabird SBE45 Thermosalinograph, Picarro G2301 analser and the Adam PPC-3120H touchscreen computer. It measures: pressure (flow) from 0 to 1 bar at 0.05 percent accuracy and of 0.0015 percent resolution; temperature from -3 to +50 degC; conductivity from 0 to 90 mS/cm at 0.0015 mS/cm accuracy; oxygen from 0 to 45 mg/l at 0.1 mg/l accuracy (250 percent saturation); pH from 0 to 14 pH at 0.01 pH accuracy; redox from -1000 to +1000 mV at 1 mV accuracy and 0.1 mV resolution.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2094'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2093/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2093/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2093/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-05T10:16:25'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Tekron NTS 03-G+'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Tekron NTS 03-G+ network time server'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A fully customisable satellite (GPS/GLONASS) reference clock with multiple Ethernet ports that support advanced Network Time Protocol (NTP) and Precision Time Protocol (PTP) synchronization based on the IEEE 1588v2-2008 standard. It provides a precision time reference with configurable time zone settings and supports mulitple user accounts with configurable access control. The high-drive IRIG-B option delivers legacy device interoperability. The electrically protected platform brings ultimate reliability through the usage of optional rubidium and OCXO oscillator options and time sync redundancy through Parallel Redundancy Protocol (PRP) support. Available with 3, 4, or 6 independent Ethernet ports and an optional second power supply for redundancy. Independently addressable and logically isolated Ethernet ports allow multiple networks to be connected to the same clock without compromising network security.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2093'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2091/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2091/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2091/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-04T16:23:46'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Sonardyne DPT 6 series'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sonardyne Dynamic Positioning Transponder 6 series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A series of seabed reference transponders designed to be used by ultra-short baseline (USBL) and long and ultra-short baseline (LUSBL) acoustic positioning systems installed on dynamically positioned (DP) vessels. The DPT 6 supports Sonardyne Wideband 2 acoustic ranging and telemetry, providing high accuracy positioning and robust performance in noisy and multipath conditions. The transponders feature hundreds of channels to reduce interference to and from other acoustic systems, enabling easier simultaneous operations (SIMOPS) on vessels. The device is constructed from an anodised aluminium alloy, with a protective polyurethane sleeve. It is fitted with a reliable release mechanism to enable the unit to be deployed in a floatation collar and recovered to the surface without remotely operated vehicle (ROV) intervention. Real time diagnostics on ranges are available to enable quality control. All types in the series operate in the medium frequency band (20 - 34 kHz), and feature a temperature sensor, tilt switch, strain gauge pressure sensor, and inclinometer tilt sensor as standard. Three depth ratings are available (3000, 5000, and 7000 m). Ranging precision is better than 15 mm. Battery life (listening) is 833 or 1390 days (alkaline and lithium respectively). All types have 500 unique Wideband 1 and 2 addresses.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2091'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2092/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2092/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2092/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-04T16:23:46'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Sonardyne Nano series'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sonardyne Nano transponder series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A series of transponders designed for acoustic positioning of divers or small underwater vehicles. The transponders are small and lightweight to allow easy attachment to a diver or vehicle. They are available in three variants: near field communication (NFC), with connector (cabled), and original equipment manufacturer (OEM). All variants are depth rated to 500 m and have an acoustic source level and beam shape that is designed to operate over a 995 m slant range under normal conditions. Variants also feature a three-month battery life, and over 300 independent acoustic addresses. The transponders operate in the medium frequency (MF) band from 20 - 34 kHz, and are compatible with Sonardyne\'s mini-ranger 2 6G Wideband ultra-short baseline (USBL) system. Transducer beam shape is omni-directional (+/- 130 degrees). Operating temperature is -10 to 45 degC.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2092'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1920/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1920/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1920/>;
    dc:modified '2024-09-02T08:48:37'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'Pro-Oceanus GTD-Pro'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Pro-Oceanus GTD-Pro dissolved gas sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Code deprecated on 02Sep2024: duplicates eisting code. Original description was: The GTD-Pro is a total dissolved gas sensor, used to determine air-sea gas transfer rates, estimate net biological production, study near-surface fluxes, and correct measurements of other dissolved gases. It measures the sum of the partial pressures of all dissolved gases, i.e. gas tension, and comes with a 2GB internal data logger. The instrument can come in titanium housing, rated to 4000 m. Accuracy is 0.01 %, resolution 0.0001 % with a drift under 0.02 mbar a year. Range is 800-2000 mbar, and depth rating is 0-600 m. Equilibration time (t63) is 3 min.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1920'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0856/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0856/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0856/>;
    dc:modified '2024-08-23T16:01:31'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'RBR Concerto'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'RBR Concerto CTD'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Conductivity, temperature depth recorder with fluorometer and turbidity loggers. Self-contained, autonomous CTD logger that can be deployed for a period of up to 5 years with 1 minute sampling intervals. High accuracy measurements, holds measurements internally even without battery and fast sampling options for profiling. Temperature sensor calibrated to accuracy of +/- 0.002 degC over range -5 to 35 degC. Conductivity measured with inductive sensor with no exposed contacts. Pressure measured with piezo-resistive transducer with accuracy of 0.05 % of full scale rating and achievable resolution of 0.001 %.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL0856'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1395/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1395/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1395/>;
    dc:modified '2024-08-23T16:01:31'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'RBR DUO 3-CT'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'RBR DUO 3-CT (submersible) CT logger'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A self-contained, dual channel conductivity and temperature sensor designed for deployment on moorings. Conductivity measurements are performed using a rugged inductive cell that can be frozen into ice. Conductivity accuracy: +/- 0.003 mS/cm. Temperature accuracy: +/- 0.002 degC. Depth rating is 750 m (plastic) - 10,000 m (titanium) depending on housing used.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1395'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1396/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1396/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1396/>;
    dc:modified '2024-08-23T16:01:31'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'RBR DUO-CT'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'RBR DUO CT (submersible) CT logger series'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Self-contained, dual channel conductivity and temperature sensors designed for deployment on moorings. This term describes sensors where the generation is not known.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL1396'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1398/2/> .
